{"id": "TDUAL-M0", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_pin_N1_i", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/StringTheory/TDualityBridge.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-01"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "SIGN-DISCIPLINE GATE (LL-1) for the T-duality bridge: four decide-pins for the Mathlib GL(2,R)-action of frickeW on the upper half-plane, whose values were computed FIRST from the physics formula -1/(N*tau) in exact Gaussian-rational arithmetic (python fractions, 2026-09-08) and only then written as Lean statements. W_1 . i = i (the self-dual point of GPR's generator S); W_2 . i = i/2 (catches a dropped factor of N, and catches a transposed frickeMatrix, which gives 2i); W_4 . (i/2) = i/2 (a genuine W_4 fixed point, also cross-checks TDUAL-M4, and catches the transpose, which gives 8i); W_1 . (1+i) = (-1+i)/2 (the only pin with nonzero real part, so it catches a sign error in the b-entry -- !![0,1;N,0] gives (1-i)/2 here -- and any error invisible on the imaginary axis). CORRECTED 2026-09-08 vs the statement layer's first draft: pin 4 does NOT catch a transposed frickeMatrix (the transpose !![0,N;-1,0] acts by tau -> -N/tau, which at N=1 is the SAME map and gives (-1+i)/2 at 1+i); the transpose is caught by pins 2 and 3 instead. And NO pin can ever catch an inverted action convention, because frickeW_sq_coe gives W_N^2 = -N*I, a scalar, so W_N and W_N^{-1} induce the same Moebius map on H -- recomputed against W_N^{-1} = (1/N)*!![0,1;-N,0], all four pins return the true values i, i/2, i/2, (-1+i)/2. PROOF ROUTE, as actually compiled (not as first hinted): UpperHalfPlane.coe_smul_of_det_pos needs 0 < g.det.val, which is Matrix.mem_glpos unfolded, so FRK-01's frickeW_mem_GLPos IS that proof and is passed directly; frickeMatrix_det_pos is about the RAW matrix, not the GL unit, and does not elaborate there. Then simp only [num, denom, frickeW_coe, frickeMatrix], push_cast, and the Gaussian arithmetic (field_simp/ring_nf/simp [Complex.I_sq]; div_eq_div_iff for pin 4). DISCRIMINATION IS ENFORCED, NOT ASSERTED: verification/TDual0PinNegControl.lean states the same four pins with the VARIANT right-hand sides (2i, 8i, (1-i)/2, i) and the SAME tactic blocks, and fails to compile with exactly four 'unsolved goals' errors. STATUS: all four proved sorry-free, axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], guarded in FinalCheck.lean under namespace Tdual0Pins; `lake build SocrateAI` completes successfully, 3768 jobs. Resolving names: SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_pin_N1_i, frickeW_pin_N2_i, frickeW_pin_N4_halfI, frickeW_pin_N1_onePlusI.", "built_from": ["SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW (FrickeInvolution.lean)", "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_mem_GLPos (FrickeInvolution.lean) -- FRK-01; supplies 0 < g.det.val directly, Matrix.mem_glpos being Iff.rfl", "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_coe (FrickeInvolution.lean)", "UpperHalfPlane.coe_smul_of_det_pos (Mathlib Analysis/Complex/UpperHalfPlane/MoebiusAction.lean:192)", "UpperHalfPlane.num, UpperHalfPlane.denom (MoebiusAction.lean:30,33)"]}
{"id": "TDUAL-M1", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_smul_coe", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/StringTheory/TDualityBridge.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["TDUAL-M0", "FRK-DEF", "FRK-01"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "The Mathlib GL(2,R)-action of frickeW on H is, pointwise in C, the textbook level-N Fricke map tau -> -1/(N*tau): for all N>0 and tau in H, ((frickeW hN . tau : H) : C) = -1 / ((N : C) * (tau : C)). At N=1 this is character-for-character the generator S : tau -> -1/tau of Giveon-Porrati-Rabinovici eq. 2.4.57 (hep-th/9401139); note that GPR's own framing puts S on the complex-structure modulus and the stringy Buscher R -> 1/R generator on the Kaehler modulus rho, so no physics attribution is made by THIS node -- it asserts only a Lean Moebius identity. For N>1 the map has determinant N and is not in SL(2,Z) at all, so GPR (2.4.57) supports the literature identification only at N=1; that restriction is TDUAL-01's problem, not this node's. PROVED: rw [coe_smul_of_det_pos (frickeW_mem_GLPos hN)]; simp [num, denom, frickeW_coe, frickeMatrix]. frickeW_mem_GLPos (FRK-01) IS the 0 < g.det.val that coe_smul_of_det_pos demands (Matrix.mem_glpos is that inequality definitionally), so the det-positive branch of sigma is taken and there is no hidden conjugation; num = 0*tau + (-1) = -1 and denom = N*tau + 0 = N*tau. No nonvanishing side condition is needed: division in C is total. (frickeMatrix_det_pos does NOT discharge it -- it is about the raw matrix, not the GL unit's determinant.) TDUAL-M0 was honoured as a PROCESS gate, not a logical dependency: pin values recomputed independently in exact Gaussian-rational arithmetic, pins compiled clean, and verification/TDual0PinNegControl.lean confirmed to fail with exactly 4 unsolved goals, all BEFORE this proof was attempted. Afterwards all four pins were re-derived FROM this lemma, and frickeW hN . frickeW hN . tau = tau was discharged from it via mul_smul plus the already-proved frickeW_sq_smul (FrickeComposite.lean). Not vacuous: verification/TDualM1NegControl.lean restates this theorem with four wrong right-hand sides (+1/(N*tau) b-flip, -1/tau dropped N, -N/tau transpose, -1/(N+tau) denom misread) under the IDENTICAL tactic block and fails with exactly 4 unsolved goals; each failing goal displays the simp-normalised LHS as -1 / (N * tau), i.e. the simp set computes the Fricke map independently of what it is compared against. Also closes a real seam in the library: -1 / ((N : C) * z) is verbatim the normal form EtaQuotientModularity.lean's eta_fricke_factor already runs on, while the Fricke* files spoke only of the GL(2,R)-action; no declaration connected them before this one. FinalCheck guard: SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_smul_coe, footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].", "built_from": ["UpperHalfPlane.coe_smul_of_det_pos (Mathlib Analysis/Complex/UpperHalfPlane/MoebiusAction.lean:192)", "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_mem_GLPos (FRK-01, FrickeInvolution.lean:55)", "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_coe, SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeMatrix (FRK-DEF)", "proof pattern of SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sq_smul (FrickeComposite.lean:41, proved)"], "difficulty": "easy", "negative_control": "verification/TDualM1NegControl.lean (must fail: exactly 4 unsolved goals)"}
{"id": "TDUAL-M2", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.StringTheory.mapGL_smul_eq_sl_smul", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/StringTheory/TDualityBridge.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "The action of the mapGL-image of SL(2,Z) inside GL(2,R) on the upper half-plane, and Mathlib's own SL(2,Z) modular action on the upper half-plane, are the SAME action: for gamma in SL(2,Z) and tau in H, Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.mapGL R gamma . tau = gamma . tau. PROVED, sorry-free, by rfl; axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (not [], because SLAction is noncomputable), guarded in SocrateAI.FinalCheck. Mathlib DEFINES UpperHalfPlane.SLAction as MulAction.compHom H (SpecialLinearGroup.mapGL R) (Analysis/Complex/UpperHalfPlane/MoebiusAction.lean:283-284, line numbers re-verified this session), so (MulAction.compHom_smul_def _ _ _).symm also proves it and rfl suffices. SCOPE HONESTY, recorded so it is not overstated downstream: this node has ZERO mathematical content. It is definitional unfolding. It mentions neither frickeW nor Gamma0, and it does NOT reduce to anything of ours -- it reduces to Mathlib's SLAction definition. Its whole job is the anti-pun check and it must never be presented in a paper as evidence that the bridge has substance; the substantive content sits in TDUAL-M1 (proved) and TDUAL-M3 (open). WHAT IT DOES SUPPLY, made explicit as a second proved declaration SocrateAI.StringTheory.exists_sl_smul_eq_of_mem_map_Gamma0: FRK-07 (frickeW_normalizes_Gamma0) is stated on (Gamma0 N).map (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.mapGL R) INSIDE GL(2,R) (FrickeInvolution.lean:117-119), and this lemma is what makes that group's action on H be Mathlib's SL(2,Z) action; without it 'the group W_N normalizes' and 'the group that acts by GPR's fractional-linear formula' are two different Lean objects and the bridge is a pun. depends_on is [] and that is correct: M2 is strictly upstream of frickeW, and the phrase 'the subject of FRK-07' in its docstring is descriptive context, not a dependency. DISCIPLINE, AND WHY IT IS NOT THE TDUAL-M0 KIND: because the proof is rfl there is NO wrong-right-hand-side variant of the general statement whose failure could certify that a tactic block did work -- the tactic does nothing, so a negative control on the general statement would be theatre. The discipline was therefore relocated to five PINS, discharged BEFORE the general lemma, each evaluating the GL(2,R) instance path and the SL(2,Z) instance path SEPARATELY (never one against the other, never either against the general lemma) against a value computed FIRST in exact Gaussian-rational arithmetic from (a*tau+b)/(c*tau+d): mapGL_sl_pin_id_i (gamma = 1, tau = i, value i); mapGL_sl_pin_T_i ([[1,1],[0,1]], tau = i, value 1+i); mapGL_sl_pin_S_onePlusI ([[0,-1],[1,0]], tau = 1+i, value (-1+i)/2); mapGL_sl_pin_G0two_lower_i ([[1,0],[2,1]], tau = i, value (2+i)/5); mapGL_sl_pin_G0two_i ([[3,1],[2,1]], tau = i, value (7+i)/5). The last two pins ASSERT Gamma0(2) membership as part of the statement, so the gate is exercised inside the bridge's own subgroup and not only on generators of the full SL(2,Z). Pin 3 is the only one with nonzero real part on both sides; pin 5 is the only one with all four entries nonzero, hence the only pin constraining every entry at once. Which variant each pin discriminates was recomputed variant-by-variant in the same exact arithmetic, and the NEGATIVE results are recorded rather than glossed: a transposed matrix is caught at pins 2 ((1+i)/2), 4 (2+i) and 5 ((5+i)/2) but NOT at pin 3, where [[0,1],[-1,0]] sends 1+i to (-1+i)/2, the true value; a b-entry sign flip is caught at pins 2 (-1+i), 3 ((1-i)/2) and 5 (1+i) but NOT at pin 4, whose b-entry is already 0 so flipping it is the identity. An SL/GL instance mismatch -- the failure this node exists to exclude -- is caught by EVERY pin, because each pin states the two sides independently, so if the two smuls were different maps at most one conjunct could hold. INSTANCE READOUT (the evidence a rfl can supply that a tactic cannot): under set_option pp.all true the LHS carries UpperHalfPlane.glAction and the RHS carries @UpperHalfPlane.SLAction Int Int.instCommRing (@Ring.toIntAlgebra Real Real.instRing), joined by @Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.mapGL (Fin 2) ... Int ... Real -- genuinely distinct instance paths, which is what makes the lemma non-vacuous as a check. A whole-library grep for competing MulAction instances on SL(2,-) and H (no head truncation) finds only UpperHalfPlane.SLAction, FixedDetMatrices.lean:54 on a different carrier, and SpecialLinearGroup.lean:231 (a DistribMulAction on V), so there is no instance diamond hiding a mismatch. INSTANCE-PINNING CAUTION: the Algebra Z R instance elaboration selects is Ring.toIntAlgebra R. Keep the statement instance-implicit exactly as written; restating it with an explicit Algebra Z R argument would in general produce a different instance term that rfl does not close.", "built_from": ["MulAction.compHom_smul_def (Mathlib Algebra/Group/Action/Hom.lean:60, line re-verified this session)", "UpperHalfPlane.SLAction (Mathlib Analysis/Complex/UpperHalfPlane/MoebiusAction.lean:283-284, line re-verified this session)", "UpperHalfPlane.coe_smul_of_det_pos and UpperHalfPlane.coe_specialLinearGroup_apply (MoebiusAction.lean:192, :286) for the five pins", "CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0_mem (Mathlib NumberTheory/ModularForms/CongruenceSubgroups.lean:89) for the two Gamma0(2) pin memberships"], "difficulty": "mechanical (rfl); the work is the five instance-agreement pins and their negative control, not the general lemma", "negative_control": "verification/TDualM2PinNegControl.lean -- restates all five pins with variant right-hand sides (conjugation at pin 1, transpose at pins 2/4/5, b-flip at pin 3) under the IDENTICAL tactic blocks; MUST fail. Verified this session: exit 1 with exactly 10 'error: unsolved goals' (two per pin), and each residual goal displays the tactic-computed true value against the wrong RHS (e.g. 'Complex.I = -Complex.I', '1 + Complex.I = 1/2 + Complex.I * (1/2)', 'Complex.I * 5 = Complex.I * 25'), i.e. the tactic blocks compute the Moebius value from the matrix rather than from what it is compared against. Confirmed to fail BEFORE mapGL_smul_eq_sl_smul was proved."}
{"id": "TDUAL-M3", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.StringTheory.sl_smul_coe_eq_flt", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/StringTheory/TDualityBridge.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "PROVED 2026-09-08, sorry-free.  Mathlib's SL(2,Z)-action on the upper half-plane is given by exactly the fractional-linear formula (a*tau+b)/(c*tau+d) with integer-cast entries: ((gamma . tau : H) : C) = (a*tau + b)/(c*tau + d) where a,b,c,d are the Int-cast entries gamma.1 0 0, gamma.1 0 1, gamma.1 1 0, gamma.1 1 1.  This is the SL(2,Z)_tau action on the T^2 complex-structure modulus whose GENERATORS Giveon-Porrati-Rabinovici eq. (2.4.57) displays (S : tau -> -1/tau, T : tau -> tau+1).  CITATION CORRECTED THIS RUN (LL-25): the earlier wording of this node and of the file docstring said 'the exact fractional-linear formula (a*tau+b)/(c*tau+d) of GPR eq. 2.4.57'.  GPR (2.4.57) does NOT display that scalar formula -- it displays the four generators S, T, S', T'.  A grep of the full pdftotext extraction (whole file, no head) for 'ctau + d', 'atau + b' and 'fractional linear' returns 12 hits, none of them a scalar (a tau + b)/(c tau + d); GPR's displayed fractional-linear transformations at (2.4.13), (2.4.24) and (4.2.30) are the MATRIX action on the background E, not the scalar action on tau.  The general tau-action is what the surrounding prose of section 2.4 presupposes and is entirely standard, but attributing a displayed equation that (2.4.57) does not contain is an overclaim, so the node now attributes to (2.4.57) only the generators it displays.  PROOF: rw [coe_specialLinearGroup_apply] (MoebiusAction.lean:286) at R = Z, then simp only [algebraMap_int_eq, eq_intCast] collapses the Z -> R -> C cast route to Z -> C (Algebra Z is a subsingleton, so algebraMap Z R = Int.castRingHom R), then push_cast; ring.  Axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (Classical.choice because SLAction is noncomputable), guarded in SocrateAI.FinalCheck.  SIGN GATE, DISCHARGED FIRST (LL-1): five fractional-linear pins whose values were computed FIRST in exact Gaussian-rational arithmetic (python fractions, 2026-09-08) and only then written as Lean statements.  What can silently go wrong in a statement of this shape is the ENTRY-POSITION ASSIGNMENT, not the arithmetic -- a transpose, an a/d swap, or a sign on b or c is still well-typed, still an equality in C, and still TRUE on symmetric matrices -- so each pin states the Mathlib action value and the TDUAL-M3 right-hand side (entries read through the same gamma.1 i j projections the theorem uses) as TWO SEPARATE CONJUNCTS against one value.  The pins: sl_flt_pin_2111_i (gamma = [[2,1],[1,1]], tau = i, value (3+i)/2); sl_flt_pin_Tsq_i (T^2 = [[1,2],[0,1]], tau = i, value 2+i); sl_flt_pin_L3_i ([[1,0],[3,1]] in Gamma0(3), asserted in-statement, tau = i, value (3+i)/10); sl_flt_pin_G5_i ([[7,2],[10,3]] in Gamma0(5), asserted in-statement, tau = i, value (76+i)/109); sl_flt_pin_negB_twoI ([[1,-1],[1,0]], tau = 2i, value (2+i)/2 -- the only pin with a negative entry and the only one away from tau = i).  BLINDNESS RECORDED, NOT GLOSSED, recomputed variant-by-variant in the same exact arithmetic: the 2111 pin CANNOT see a transpose (b = c = 1, so transposing it is the identity); Tsq CANNOT see a c-flip (c = 0) or an a/d swap (a = d); L3 CANNOT see a b-flip (b = 0) or an a/d swap.  Only sl_flt_pin_G5_i catches ALL FIVE variants (transpose (44+i)/13, a/d swap (44+i)/149, b-flip (64+41i)/109, c-flip (-64+41i)/109, inverse (-44+i)/149), because it is the only pin with four nonzero pairwise-distinct entries.  NOTE the contrast with TDUAL-M0, where the inverted-action variant is PROVABLY invisible to every pin (W_N^2 = -N.I is a scalar and scalars act trivially on H); here gamma is not equal to gamma-inverse and all five pins see it.  NEGATIVE CONTROL: verification/TDualM3PinNegControl.lean restates all five pins with the variant right-hand sides under IDENTICAL tactic blocks and fails with exactly ten error: lines (two per pin; the two Gamma0 membership conjuncts are left correct and stay proved).  It was confirmed to fail with exactly ten BEFORE sl_smul_coe_eq_flt was proved.  SCOPE, so this node is not misread as the bridge: it is stated for ALL of SL(2,Z) (formalising more than the cited display, the harmless direction) and mentions NEITHER frickeW NOR Gamma0(N).  It is the SL(2,Z)/GPR half only.  frickeW enters through TDUAL-M1 and TDUAL-M2; the Fricke reduction itself is TDUAL-01, still open.  The Gamma0(N) restriction the bridge imposes is definitional -- restricting a group action to a subgroup cannot change the Moebius formula -- and Gamma0(N) must therefore never be described as load-bearing IN THE FORMULA; TDUAL-01's Gamma0(N) hypothesis is deliberately unused by its formula conjunct.  NOT TOUCHED, still out of scope and unreachable: the K3-factor duality group (O(4,20)/Narain; Mathlib has zero hits for Narain and K3Surface) and Mathieu moonshine / M24 / Sym^2.  PROVENANCE: INDEPENDENT (a one-line instantiation of Mathlib's own UpperHalfPlane.coe_specialLinearGroup_apply plus a cast cleanup); SocrateAI-Scientific-DualScaleSimulator is NOT cited for this or any other formula here -- it was read in full and found axiom-propped, a prior attempt, not a proof source."}
{"id": "TDUAL-M4", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_smul_involutive", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/StringTheory/TDualityBridge.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-02", "FRK-10", "TDUAL-M1"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "The Fricke map is an involution of the upper half-plane ITSELF, written in the associated form: for all N > 0 and tau in H, frickeW hN . frickeW hN . tau = tau. ZERO MATHEMATICAL CONTENT, RECORDED AS SUCH, NOT DRESSED UP. This node is the ALREADY-PROVED H-level lemma frickeW_sq_smul (FrickeComposite.lean, sorry-free, the file-sibling of FRK-10's named frickeW_sq_slash) re-associated by Mathlib's mul_smul, which is a field of MulAction. The entire proof is: rw [<- mul_smul]; exact frickeW_sq_smul hN tau. THE EARLIER PROSE CONTRAST WAS AIMED AT THE WRONG SIBLING AND IS CORRECTED HERE: the previous wording of this node and of the file docstring said 'an involution of H itself, not merely W_N^2 = -N*I at the level of matrices'. The matrix-level statement is FRK-02 (frickeW_sq_coe); but frickeW_sq_smul is ALREADY the H-level statement, and the matrix->H upgrade -- the step that actually consumes W_N^2 = -N*I together with det(W_N^2) = N^2 > 0 and denom(W_N^2) = -N -- was done in FrickeComposite.lean, not here. FRK-02 therefore enters this node only TRANSITIVELY, through frickeW_sq_smul's own proof; the one-liner does not touch it. This is the same situation as TDUAL-M2's rfl and gets the same plain sentence. DAG EDGE BOOKKEEPING, EXPLICIT: depends_on lists FRK-10 because the consumed lemma lives in FRK-10's file and is proved alongside it, but the lemma actually consumed is frickeW_sq_smul, NOT FRK-10's registered lean_name frickeW_sq_slash; frickeW_sq_smul is separately proved and separately guarded in FinalCheck.lean. TDUAL-M1 is a dependency because the five decide-pins below are proved through frickeW_smul_coe. SIGN-DISCIPLINE GATE (LL-1), FIVE TWO-STEP DECIDE-PINS, DISCHARGED BEFORE THE GENERAL PROOF. Each pin is a PAIR: the intermediate value W_N . tau and the round trip W_N . W_N . tau, both computed first in exact Gaussian-rational arithmetic from tau -> -1/(N*tau) (python fractions, 2026-09-08) and only then written as Lean. N=2 at i: i/2 then i. N=3 at 2i: i/6 then 2i. N=1 at 1+i: (-1+i)/2 then 1+i. N=2 at 1+i: (-1+i)/4 then 1+i. N=4 at i: i/4 then i. ALL FIVE POINTS SATISFY W_N . tau != tau, which is the point: TDUAL-M0's pins sit at the N=1 self-dual point i and at the genuine N=4 fixed point i/2, where involution, identity and projection are indistinguishable. The pins run through frickeW_smul_coe (TDUAL-M1) applied once and twice -- deliberately NOT through frickeW_sq_smul, which reaches the same values via the product matrix W_N * W_N, its determinant N^2 and its denom -N -- so pins and general proof are two independent routes. Pin 3's and pin 1's first components are statement-for-statement TDUAL-M0's frickeW_pin_N1_onePlusI and frickeW_pin_N2_i, which were proved by a THIRD route (coe_smul_of_det_pos on the raw frickeMatrix); they are re-derived here rather than cited so that all ten components share one tactic style and the negative control mirrors it exactly. Resolving pin names: SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_invol_pin_N2_i, frickeW_invol_pin_N3_twoI, frickeW_invol_pin_N1_onePlusI, frickeW_invol_pin_N2_onePlusI, frickeW_invol_pin_N4_i. NEGATIVE CONTROL -- WHAT IT CAN AND CANNOT CERTIFY, SAID PLAINLY. No wrong-right-hand-side control on frickeW_smul_involutive itself is manufactured, because the proof is `exact` of an existing lemma and such a control would fail only because `exact` does not unify -- the same blindness this file already admits for TDUAL-M2's rfl. What IS discriminated is the two-step gate: verification/TDualM4PinNegControl.lean restates all ten pin components with wrong values (dropped factor of N or flipped b-entry on the intermediates; the IDEMPOTENT variant W_N . W_N . tau = W_N . tau on the round trips) under the IDENTICAL tactic blocks and fails with exit 1 and exactly ten error: lines (nine 'unsolved goals', one 'ring_nf made no progress'). It was confirmed failing BEFORE frickeW_smul_involutive was discharged. PHYSICS GLOSS IS INTERPRETATION, NOT CONTENT, AND IS SUBORDINATE AND UNCITED. Read informally this is 'the duality squares to the identity on the moduli'. TDUAL-M4 asserts nothing about physics -- it is an identity for a Moebius action on H -- and TDUAL-01's own recorded obstruction (A) is precisely that the stringy Buscher generator acts on the Kaehler modulus rho, not on tau. No literature is invoked by this node, which is the correct citation discipline for a math node. SCOPE: nothing here touches K3, the Narain moduli space, or moonshine. STATUS: proved sorry-free, axiom footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for all six declarations (five pins plus the theorem), guarded in FinalCheck.lean under namespace Tdual0Pins. The INVERTED tripwire certifying that tduality_tau_fricke_bridge still depends on sorryAx is UNTOUCHED and still passing: closing M4 does not close the bridge. Final line of lake build: 'Build completed successfully (3768 jobs).'", "built_from": ["SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sq_smul (FrickeComposite.lean:41, proved sorry-free) -- the whole of the mathematics; file-sibling of FRK-10's frickeW_sq_slash", "mul_smul (Mathlib, Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Action/Defs.lean:152, a MulAction field) -- the only thing this node adds", "SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_smul_coe (TDUAL-M1, proved) -- used by the five two-step decide-pins, not by the general proof", "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sq_coe (FRK-02) -- transitively only, inside frickeW_sq_smul's own proof"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "negative_control": "verification/TDualM4PinNegControl.lean (must fail: exit 1, exactly 10 error: lines)"}
{"id": "TDUAL-01", "kind": "physics", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.StringTheory.tduality_tau_fricke_bridge", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/StringTheory/TDualityBridge.lean", "status": "blocked", "depends_on": ["TDUAL-M1", "TDUAL-M2", "TDUAL-M3", "TDUAL-M4", "FRK-07"], "paper_claim": null, "statement_nl": "CONTESTED, NOT MERELY OPEN (corrected 2026-09-09, independent review). The node originally claimed: T-duality's action on the T^2 complex-structure modulus (Giveon-Porrati-Rabinovici, Phys. Rept. 244 (1994) section 2.4, eqs. 2.4.57-2.4.59) restricted to Gamma0(N) and extended by the level-N Fricke normalization tau -> -1/(N*tau) coincides with the already-proven frickeW action. TWO FINDINGS REFUTE THIS FRAMING, both compiled/verified, neither a proof error in the supporting lemmas (TDUAL-M1..M4 remain correct and proved). (1) HOLLOWNESS: a standalone equivalence check (compiled, EXIT=0) proves TDUAL-01 <=> TDUAL-M1 AND TDUAL-M2 AND TDUAL-M3, both directions. The theorem adds zero content over its three inputs: the `gamma in Gamma0 N` hypothesis is never consumed (the second conjunct holds for ALL of SL(2,Z)), and FRK-07 / TDUAL-M4 (normalizes Gamma0(N); involution) appear in depends_on but occur in neither the statement nor its proof term. Nothing in the Lean term names a T-duality object -- no duality group, no Narain lattice, no p_L/p_R spectrum, no background. 'Coincides' is asserted only in prose. (2) WRONG SLOT: GPR's own text (2.4.57-58) says the tau-side SL(2,Z) is the GEOMETRIC (non-stringy) factor -- modular transformations of the T^2 complex structure leave the torus 'unmodified' -- so attaching 'T-duality' to frickeW's tau-action already misattributes which GPR factor is which. Worse: for N > 1, frickeW has det = N, so W_N is NOT an element of SL(2,Z)_tau (or SL(2,Z)_rho) at all, and whole-text greps of the GPR extraction (339,164 chars, no truncation) return zero hits for Fricke, Atkin, Gamma_0, congruence, or 'level N' -- there is no literature anchor for a level-N Fricke element of ANY T-duality group. WHERE FRICKE-TYPE MAPS ACTUALLY APPEAR IN STRING THEORY (verified, fetched): Persson & Volpato, 'Fricke S-duality in CHL models', arXiv:1504.07260, JHEP 12 (2015) 156 -- CHL orbifolds of IIA on K3 x T^2 by a Z_N symmetry are self-dual under a weak-strong S-DUALITY on the heterotic AXIO-DILATON modulus S by a 'Fricke involution' S -> -1/(NS), explicitly 'outside the standard SL(2,Z) symmetry of the parent theory.' This is a DIFFERENT modulus and a DIFFERENT duality (S-duality, not T-duality) than TDUAL-01 claimed. It is simultaneously the strongest evidence that frickeW IS the right Lean object for string theory, and the proof that this node attached it to the wrong physical slot. WHAT SURVIVES AND SHIPS: TDUAL-M1 (frickeW_smul_coe) is genuine new content -- the first link between the GL(2,R)-action language of the Fricke*.lean files and the -1/(N*z) normal form used elsewhere in the library (e.g. EtaQuotientModularity.lean's eta_fricke_factor, not yet formally connected to it). TDUAL-M0/M2/M3/M4 and their 19 decide-pins + 5 negative controls are correct and reusable. RECOMMENDED DISPOSITION: retire this node's physics framing (do not close the sorry as a proof of the current statement); either restate as a `math`-kind node naming exactly M1 AND M2 AND M3 with no duality claim, or replace with a fresh, separately gate-zero'd node targeting Persson-Volpato's actual S-duality statement on the axio-dilaton -- which lands inside CHL orbifolds of K3 x T^2 and is a materially harder, separate research question, not a small revision of this one.", "baseline": "GPR (hep-th/9401139) section 2.4 anchors tau -> -1/tau ONLY at N=1 (their S generator); no source anchors a level-N Fricke map in any T-duality group. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) anchors S -> -1/(NS) as an S-duality on the axio-dilaton in CHL models -- a different modulus and duality than this node claims.", "falsifier": "SUPERSEDED -- the original falsifier items are all already-proved theorems with clean footprints (TDUAL-M0 pins, M2/M3 definitional facts, M4's involution), so none can fire; check_dag.py rule 5 was satisfied syntactically by a falsifier that cannot falsify. Retained for the record; see statement_nl for the actual issue.", "built_from": ["TDUAL-M1 (SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_smul_coe, proved)", "TDUAL-M2 (SocrateAI.StringTheory.mapGL_smul_eq_sl_smul, proved)", "TDUAL-M3 (SocrateAI.StringTheory.sl_smul_coe_eq_flt, proved)", "TDUAL-M4 (SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_smul_involutive, proved)", "FRK-07 (SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_normalizes_Gamma0, proved)", "Giveon-Porrati-Rabinovici, Phys. Rept. 244 (1994) 77-202, hep-th/9401139, section 2.4, eqs. (2.4.57)-(2.4.61)"], "difficulty": "easy as Lean assembly; BLOCKED on physics attribution, which is not a Lean problem"}
{"id": "SDF-DEF-01", "kind": "def", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.IsFrickeSelfDual", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "DEFINITION, PROVED (run 11): it elaborates, and its six condition decide-pins plus the negative control are all sorry-free and guarded in FinalCheck.lean section SdfDef01. It is not yet USED in any proved theorem -- SDF-02 and SDF-04, its consumers, are still open. IsFrickeSelfDual N r : Prop := for all delta in N.divisors, r delta = r (N / delta). The self-dual (Fricke-symmetric) condition on an eta-quotient exponent vector r : EtaExp = (Nat -> Int): r takes the same value at delta and at N/delta for every divisor delta of N. This is exactly the condition under which the DUAL exponent vector (delta |-> r (N/delta)) appearing on the right-hand side of the already-proved etaQuotient_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2212, sorry-free, tag F3.2-A7) agrees with r on N.divisors, hence defines the same eta quotient, turning that transformation law into an eigenform relation. Stated as a BOUNDED forall over N.divisors, matching how EtaExp is read everywhere else in this library (etaQuotientH_congr, EtaExp.sum_divisors_congr): values of r off N.divisors are junk and must not be constrained. NON-VACUITY, NOW MACHINE-CHECKED: the negative control not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric (PROVED, by decide) exhibits r = (2,0) at N = 2 which is NOT self-dual, so the predicate is a genuine restriction and not accidentally universally true. NAMING: the condition r delta = r(N/delta) is called SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is already taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), and is ALSO the term Persson-Volpato use for this condition, so it collides twice. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one. The negative-control exponent vector r = (2,0) at N = 2 is deliberately the SAME one as fricke_dual_pin (EtaQuotientModularity.lean, sorry-free), where f(z) = eta(z)^2 and its Fricke dual f*(z) = eta(2z)^2 are shown to be genuinely different functions -- exactly the situation IsFrickeSelfDual excludes. EVIDENCE (run 11, re-verified this session, not carried over): six condition pins, all proved by decide and all guarded by #guard_msgs in #print axioms in Lean/SocrateAI/FinalCheck.lean section SdfDef01 -- selfDual_cond_pin_level_one (N=1, r=(24); DEGENERATE, every r is self-dual at N=1), selfDual_cond_pin_level_six (N=6, r=(1,11,11,1) on (1,2,3,6); THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, the only one with N>1 AND a non-constant vector, hence the only one a wrong delta <-> N/delta pairing could fail), rPinSix_nonconstant (r 1 = 1 != 11 = r 2, the witness that PIN B is not passing merely because a constant vector is self-dual at every level), selfDual_cond_pin_zero_exp (r == 0 at N=6; DEGENERATE, a floor certifying the predicate is not empty, proved by rfl under the binder), selfDual_cond_pin_level_two_weight_one (N=2, r=(1,1); cross-checks the remark in fricke_level_two_pin's docstring that its exponent vector 'is its own dual'), selfDual_cond_pin_level_one_weight_two (N=1, r=(4)). All values were computed OUTSIDE Lean first, in exact integer arithmetic this session (divisors 1 = [1], divisors 2 = [1,2], divisors 6 = [1,2,3,6], each vector printed beside its dual), and only then asserted in Lean; none was adjusted to match a proof. Discharged by decide, never native_decide, so no Lean.ofReduceBool enters the footprint. Axiom footprint of IsFrickeSelfDual and of every pin except the rfl one: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; selfDual_cond_pin_zero_exp depends on no axioms. Statement-shape check, machine-verified: IsFrickeSelfDual = fun N r => forall delta in N.divisors, r delta = r (N / delta) closes by rfl, i.e. the definition on disk is definitionally the node text. SECOND NEGATIVE CONTROL, the sharpest test here: not_selfDual_pin_mispaired (PROVED) says r = (1,11,1,11) on (1,2,3,6) is NOT self-dual at N = 6. That vector carries the SAME weight normalisation as the load-bearing pin's (sum r delta = 24 = 2*12) and IS invariant under the WRONG involution 1 <-> 3, 2 <-> 6, so a definition that had transposed the divisor pairing would satisfy every positive pin AND would prove this statement's negation. Together with selfDual_cond_pin_level_six it brackets the delta <-> N/delta pairing from both sides. Computed outside Lean first: under delta -> 6/delta the vector reads [1,11,1,11] against a dual [11,1,11,1], different at every divisor.", "built_from": ["EtaExp (Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotient.lean:228, abbrev EtaExp := Nat -> Int)", "Nat.divisors", "decide (kernel evaluation of Nat.divisors; native_decide deliberately NOT used)", "rPinSixMispaired (the mis-pairing control vector)"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-DEF-02", "kind": "def", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeEigenvalue", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "DEFINITION, PROVED (run 11): it elaborates, and its six VALUE pins plus three negative controls are all sorry-free and guarded in FinalCheck.lean section SdfDef02 (14 #guard_msgs #print axioms guards, including one on the definition itself). frickeEigenvalue (N : Nat) (k : Int) : Complex := I ^ (-k) * ((Real.sqrt ((N : Real) ^ k) : Real) : Complex). The closed-form Fricke eigenvalue lambda = i^{-k} * N^{k/2} of a self-dual eta quotient of level N and weight k. Written with a REAL square root of the POSITIVE REAL N^k, so no complex square root and no branch choice is ever involved -- contrast Complex.sqrt, which etaQuotient_fricke uses internally and which this file never touches. What is ABSENT is the point: the exponent vector r does not appear. The constant of etaQuotient_fricke depends on r only through s = prod_{delta | N} delta^{r delta}, and SDF-02 (prod_zpow_selfDual, proved) forces s = N^k on self-dual r. This is the UNNORMALISED eigenvalue, attached to f(-1/(Nz)) = lambda * z^k * f(z); the classically normalised one (a root of unity) is i^{-k} and appears in SDF-06. PINNED VALUES, now MACHINE-CHECKED (all sorry-free, in section SdfDef02Pins, each computed by hand BEFORE being written as a Lean statement): frickeEigenvalue 1 12 = 1 (frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_one); frickeEigenvalue 6 12 = 46656 = 6^6 (frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_six, THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, genuine N > 1); frickeEigenvalue 6 0 = 1 (frickeEigenvalue_pin_zero_weight, degenerate k = 0); frickeEigenvalue 2 1 = -(i*sqrt 2) (frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_two_weight_one, ODD weight, the only value leaving the reals); frickeEigenvalue 1 2 = -1 (frickeEigenvalue_pin_neg_one, THE SIGN PIN, k = 2 mod 4); frickeEigenvalue 6 (-12) = 1/46656 (frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_six_neg, NEGATIVE weight, proper-fraction radicand -- refutes any closed form that assumed k >= 0). These six replace what was previously the ONLY Lean evidence for any eigenvalue value: the five SDF-05 pins (selfDual_pin_level_one and friends), every one of which is still sorry because its other conjuncts need the open SDF-05. The new pins are stated on the eigenvalue ALONE -- no eta quotient, no exponent vector, no IsFrickeSelfDual hypothesis -- so SDF-DEF-02 no longer depends on SDF-05 for its evidence. NEGATIVE CONTROLS, machine-checked: frickeEigenvalue_pin_not_natPow (frickeEigenvalue 6 12 != 2176782336 = 6^12, so the square root is load-bearing and the exponent is k/2 not k); frickeEigenvalue_pin_not_one (frickeEigenvalue 1 2 != 1, so the i^{-k} factor is load-bearing -- PIN A cannot supply this, its value IS 1); frickeEigenvalue_pin_nonconstant (frickeEigenvalue 6 12 != frickeEigenvalue 1 12, so the eigenvalue genuinely varies with the level). WHAT THIS NODE DOES NOT SAY, so it cannot be oversold: the pins fix VALUES of a definition. That this closed form IS the Fricke eigenvalue is SDF-03 (fricke_const_selfDual, proved) plus SDF-05 (STILL OPEN), and must not be read off this node. JUNK AT N = 0, recorded so it is never mistaken for a claim: (0 : Real)^k is 0 for k != 0 in Mathlib's zpow, so frickeEigenvalue 0 k = 0 for every k != 0. Harmless -- every downstream statement carries hN : 0 < N -- but the definition is not meaningful at N = 0. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one. CORROBORATION AGAINST ALREADY-PROVED UPSTREAM PINS, re-verified this session: frickeEigenvalue 1 12 = 1 is the constant of eta_S_via_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246, sorry-free, itself re-derived a second time from Mathlib's discriminant_S_invariant in the example beside it); frickeEigenvalue 2 1 = -(i*sqrt 2) equals i^{-1}*2*(sqrt 2)^{-1}, the constant of fricke_level_two_pin (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2285, sorry-free), whose own docstring independently observes that its exponent vector 'is its own dual'; and frickeEigenvalue 6 12 = 46656 agrees with fricke_const_pin_level_six (sorry-free, SDF-03) and with prod_zpow_pin_level_six_value (sorry-free, SDF-02: the product is 2176782336 = 6^12). SDF-DEF-02 and SDF-03 are independent nodes that land on the same number at that instance.", "built_from": ["Complex.I", "Real.sqrt", "Complex.I_pow_four / Complex.I_sq / Complex.inv_I -- the integer-exponent i-power pins", "Real.sqrt_sq -- the six square-root values, re-derived here rather than imported from SDF-03", "eta_S_via_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246, proved) -- corroborates the N=1 k=12 pin", "fricke_level_two_pin (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2285, proved) -- corroborates the N=2 k=1 pin"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-01", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_congr_divisors", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "PROVED, sorry-free (run 12). etaQuotient_congr_divisors (z : Complex) (h : for all delta in N.divisors, r delta = s delta) : etaQuotient N r z = etaQuotient N s z, for r s : EtaExp = (Nat -> Int). The COMPLEX-DOMAIN analogue of the existing etaQuotientH_congr (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:588; the theorem keyword is on 588, not 589 as an earlier draft of this node said -- cosmetic, corrected here), which is stated only for the BUNDLED upper-half-plane argument tau : H. This is the missing ADAPTER, and it was missing for a real reason: etaQuotient_fricke -- the theorem the whole SDF-* block specialises -- is stated on Complex, not on H, so the bundled congruence lemma cannot be applied to it. It is a SUPPORT lemma, the tool and not the conclusion: it is not an instance of etaQuotient_fricke and must not be compared against it. STRICTLY MORE GENERAL THAN ITS MODEL: since etaQuotientH N r tau = etaQuotient N r (tau : Complex) is rfl (etaQuotientH_apply, EtaQuotientModularity.lean:519-521), this drops the im z > 0 constraint the H subtype carries. That is sound -- no non-vanishing and no branch cut is used anywhere in the proof; off the open upper half-plane both sides take the same junk value because the two finite products are equal factor by factor. PROOF (mechanical, as predicted): simp only [etaQuotient]; exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun delta hdelta => by rw [h delta hdelta]. NON-DUPLICATION, re-verified this session by whole-library grep with no head/truncation over Lean/ for 'etaQuotient_congr' and 'congr_divisors': the only hits are inside EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean itself, i.e. this run's own work. A grep for the hypothesis shape 'r delta = s delta' across all of Lean/ returns exactly three declarations -- this one, the bundled etaQuotientH_congr (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:589), and the ADDITIVE EtaExp.sum_divisors_congr (EtaQuotient.lean:249, AddCommMonoid sums over F : Nat -> Int -> M, so not reusable for a product). The Complex-domain congruence genuinely did not exist. EVIDENCE -- PINS COMPUTED OUTSIDE LEAN FIRST, then asserted, none adjusted to match a proof. Because SDF-01's proof is a one-line Finset.prod_congr it cannot really be wrong in its PROOF, only in its STATEMENT -- specifically in whether its hypothesis is the one its consumer can discharge -- so the pins fix the hypothesis at the exact instantiation SDF-04 uses (r := fun d => r (N/d), s := r), whose obligation beta-reduces to r (N/delta) = r delta on N.divisors. Four positive pins, all sorry-free, all by decide (never native_decide, so no Lean.ofReduceBool): dualExp_congr_pin_level_one (N=1, r=(24), the k=12 case underlying the sorry-free eta_S_via_fricke; DEGENERATE, true for every r at N=1), dualExp_congr_pin_level_six (N=6, r=(1,11,11,1) on (1,2,3,6); THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, the only one with N>1 AND a non-constant vector, hence the only one a wrong delta <-> N/delta pairing could fail), dualExp_congr_pin_zero_exp (r == 0 at N=6; DEGENERATE floor, by rfl under the binder), dualExp_congr_pin_level_two (N=2, r=(1,1)). TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS, both PROVED: not_dualExp_congr_pin_asymmetric says the hypothesis is FALSE at N=2, r=(2,0) (vector [2,0] vs dual [0,2]) -- the SAME vector as fricke_dual_pin (sorry-free), where eta(z)^2 and its Fricke dual eta(2z)^2 are genuinely different functions, so there the CONCLUSION fails too and not merely the hypothesis; without it SDF-01 could be read as applying to the dual of an ARBITRARY r, making SDF-04's appeal to self-duality vacuous. not_dualExp_congr_pin_mispaired says it is FALSE at N=6, r=(1,11,1,11), which carries the SAME weight normalisation (sum = 24) as the load-bearing pin and IS invariant under the WRONG involution 1 <-> 3, 2 <-> 6 -- so a transposed divisor pairing would satisfy all four positive pins and prove this one's negation. Together the two bracket the pairing from both sides. DOWNSTREAM FIT, MACHINE-CHECKED rather than assumed -- this is where a hidden gap would have lived. IsFrickeSelfDual reads r delta = r (N/delta) while SDF-01 instantiated as SDF-04 needs it requires r (N/delta) = r delta: the two differ by a .symm. dualExp_congr_pin_level_six_of_selfDual (PROVED) discharges the load-bearing pin's obligation FROM the sorry-free selfDual_cond_pin_level_six through exactly that bridge, and etaQuotient_congr_divisors_pin_level_six (PROVED) then runs the whole path to the collapsed quotient: etaQuotient 6 (fun delta => rPinSix (6/delta)) z = etaQuotient 6 rPinSix z for EVERY z : Complex, with no hypothesis on z. So the single rw that SDF-04 is claimed to be away from is verified at the load-bearing instance. No side condition (no N/delta in N.divisors, no 0 < N, no z in the open upper half-plane) is silently required. DEPENDENCIES: depends_on is [] and that is correct -- SDF-01's statement mentions neither IsFrickeSelfDual nor anything else from SDF-DEF-01, so it is independently statable and provable. (An earlier comparator draft listed SDF-DEF-01 as a dependency; that was a loose ordering edge, not a real one. The PINS do use SDF-DEF-01's already-proved selfDual_cond_pin_level_six, but the theorem does not.) AXIOM FOOTPRINT of etaQuotient_congr_divisors and of all eight accompanying pins: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -- no sorryAx, no Lean.ofReduceBool. All nine are guarded by #guard_msgs in #print axioms in Lean/SocrateAI/FinalCheck.lean, section Sdf01. GUARD NEGATIVE CONTROL RUN THIS SESSION: asserting a deliberately wrong footprint (one claiming sorryAx) for etaQuotient_congr_divisors makes the check FAIL with the expected message diff, invoked as 'lake --packages=local-packages.json env lean FILE' (the only form that actually runs the check -- LL-27/LL-32), so the guard demonstrably bites and is not vacuous. STILL OPEN, unchanged by this node: SDF-04 and SDF-05 remain sorry, and their INVERTED TRIPWIRES in FinalCheck section SdfDef01 still correctly report sorryAx -- re-verified this session. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. No declaration mentions S-duality, the axio-dilaton, or CHL models. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one. NAMING: the condition r delta = r (N/delta) is SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is already taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), and is also Persson-Volpato's term for this condition, so it collides twice. Neither SDF-01 nor any of its pins uses the word.", "built_from": ["etaQuotient (Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientModularity.lean:511)", "etaQuotientH_congr (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:588) as the model", "Finset.prod_congr"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-02", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.prod_zpow_selfDual", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-01"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (run 12), sorry-free, guarded. THE ONE GENUINELY NON-FORMAL STEP OF THIS BLOCK. prod_zpow_selfDual : for 0 < N, a Fricke-self-dual exponent vector r (SDF-DEF-01) and k : Int with sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k, the Fricke constant s = prod_{delta | N} (delta : Real) ^ (r delta) equals (N : Real) ^ k. Everything happens inside the REALS, so no branch cut is anywhere near it. PROOF ACTUALLY USED (10 lines, no gap, verified this run): (1) hpos : 0 < s by Finset.prod_pos with zpow_pos, each (delta : Real) > 0 from Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors -- this is the step that needs delta > 0 and is exercised by the negative-exponent pin; (2) hdual : prod_{delta | N} delta^{r (N/delta)} = s by Finset.prod_congr rfl, i.e. POINTWISE on the SAME index set, so NO divisor-involution reindexing is involved (the rewrite runs BACKWARDS, since IsFrickeSelfDual reads r delta = r (N/delta) while the goal needs the reverse); (3) sqrt_prod_dual (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2409, proved sorry-free, tag F3.2-A7) rewritten by hdual reads sqrt s = N^k * (sqrt s)^{-1}; nth_rewrite plus inv_mul_cancel_right₀ with Real.sqrt_ne_zero'.mpr hpos gives sqrt s * sqrt s = N^k; Real.mul_self_sqrt hpos.le closes. CORRECTION TO AN EARLIER FRAMING, recorded because it was wrong in the comparator brief: this node does NOT follow from etaQuotient_fricke. That theorem is an equation in C about the eta quotient and asserts nothing about the constant s alone; substituting self-duality into it gives the eigenform relation (SDF-04 / SDF-05), not this. The genuine reference is sqrt_prod_dual, which the node's built_from already named first. WHY THE HYPOTHESES ARE THE RIGHT ONES: hk is not decoration -- s * s* = prod_delta delta^{r delta} * prod_delta (N/delta)^{r delta} = prod_delta N^{r delta} = N^{sum r delta}, which is N^{2k} exactly when sum r delta = 2k; self-duality then gives s* = s, so s^2 = N^{2k}, and positivity picks the root N^k rather than -N^k. hr CANNOT BE DROPPED, and that is machine-checked, not argued: prod_zpow_pin_asymmetric_ne (PROVED) exhibits r = (2,0) at N = 2 which satisfies the WEIGHT hypothesis exactly (rPinAsym_weight, PROVED: sum r delta = 2 = 2*1) and has prod delta^{r delta} = 1^2 * 2^0 = 1 while N^k = 2^1 = 2 -- so the hr-free version of this node is FALSE and this is a counterexample to it. prod_zpow_pin_mispaired_ne (PROVED) brackets the divisor involution from the other side: r = (1,11,1,11) on (1,2,3,6) carries the same weight normalisation as the load-bearing pin (sum = 24 = 2*12) and is invariant under the WRONG pairing 1<->3, 2<->6; its product is 2229025112064, against 6^12 = 2176782336, so a transposed divisor pairing would make this node false while satisfying every positive pin. PINS, ALL PROVED AND ALL STATED BEFORE THE GENERAL LEMMA, on the PRODUCT ALONE with no frickeEigenvalue conjunct (deliberately -- the eigenvalue belongs to SDF-DEF-02, which is a different and still-open node; that separation is why these close while the five selfDual_pin_* conjunctions in the same file do not): prod_zpow_pin_level_one (N=1, r=(24), k=12; DEGENERATE, both sides are 1 for every r and k -- it is the instantiation underlying the already sorry-free eta_S_via_fricke); prod_zpow_pin_level_six_value and prod_zpow_pin_level_six (N=6, r=(1,11,11,1) on (1,2,3,6), k=12; THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, the only one with N>1 AND a non-constant vector, hence the only one that can detect a wrong delta <-> N/delta pairing: 1^1 * 2^11 * 3^11 * 6^1 = 2176782336 = 6^12, asserted first as a LITERAL and only then as N^k, so a wrong N^k cannot be absorbed by a wrong product); prod_zpow_pin_zero_exp (r == 0 at N=6, k=0; DEGENERATE floor -- k=0 makes N^k = 1 for every N, so a statement proving only the k=0 case would still pass); prod_zpow_pin_level_two (N=2, r=(1,1), k=1, the smallest non-degenerate instance, whose s = 2 matches the (sqrt 2)^{-1} already pinned upstream by the sorry-free fricke_level_two_pin); and prod_zpow_pin_level_four_neg (N=4, r=(-2,6,-2) on (1,2,4), k=1: 1^{-2} * 2^6 * 4^{-2} = 64/16 = 4 = 4^1). That last one is NEW this run and is the only pin with NEGATIVE exponents, hence the only one that exercises the zpow_pos positivity step -- without it a version of this node restricted to non-negative exponent vectors would satisfy every other pin; level four also contributes the only N>1 divisor that is its own dual (4/2 = 2), a fixed point of the involution that levels 2 and 6 do not have. Its hypotheses are separately machine-checked (rPinLevelFourNeg_selfDual, rPinLevelFourNeg_weight), so it is an instance of this node and not an unrelated arithmetic fact. APPLICATION CHECK: prod_zpow_selfDual_pin_level_six (PROVED) re-derives 2176782336 by RUNNING the general lemma at (N, r, k) = (6, rPinSix, 12) and evaluating 6^12, where prod_zpow_pin_level_six_value asserts the same number by direct computation -- so the general statement is checked to FIRE at the concrete instance and return the independently computed value, not merely to be true in the abstract. A general lemma that had drifted (wrong exponent, N^{k/2} for N^k, dual product for the original) would produce a different number there while staying provable in its own terms. EVIDENCE COMPUTED THIS SESSION, in exact Python Fraction arithmetic, NOT carried over from the previous run's brief: a brute-force scan enumerating self-dual vectors by delta <-> N/delta ORBIT (so self-duality is imposed by construction and then re-asserted per instance, rather than filtered for) over four independent ranges -- 1<=N<=24 with entries in [-3,3]: 4028 instances satisfying sum r delta = 2k, ZERO mismatches, of which 3876 have N>1 and a non-constant vector; 1<=N<=24 with [-5,5]: 20300, zero; 1<=N<=48 with [-3,3]: 37068, zero; 1<=N<=60 with [-4,4]: 671504, zero. The 4028 figure reproduces the one already recorded in the module docstring for that configuration. HONESTY NOTE: an earlier version of this node's statement_nl claimed a figure of 19155 instances; no configuration run this session reproduces it, and it has been replaced by the four re-derived figures above rather than restated. AXIOM FOOTPRINT, verified this run: prod_zpow_selfDual and all twelve accompanying pins and controls depend on [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -- no sorryAx, and no Lean.ofReduceBool (the concrete pins use decide for Nat.divisors and norm_num for the real arithmetic; native_decide is deliberately not used). Thirteen #guard_msgs in #print axioms guards in Lean/SocrateAI/FinalCheck.lean, new section Sdf02. BUILD: lake --packages=local-packages.json build SocrateAI -> 'Build completed successfully (3769 jobs).', 0 errors, 19 sorry warnings (all pre-existing open nodes; prod_zpow_selfDual is no longer among them). NAMING: the condition r delta = r(N/delta) is called SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is already taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), and is ALSO Persson-Volpato's term for this condition, so it collides twice. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. This node is a statement about a product of real powers of divisors and nothing else. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["sqrt_prod_dual (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2409, proved sorry-free, tag F3.2-A7) -- the ACTUAL reference; NOT etaQuotient_fricke, which asserts nothing about the constant s alone", "Finset.prod_pos (Mathlib Algebra/Order/BigOperators/GroupWithZero/Finset.lean:107)", "zpow_pos (Mathlib Algebra/Order/GroupWithZero/Basic.lean:969)", "Nat.pos_of_mem_divisors", "Finset.prod_congr (pointwise on the SAME index set -- no divisor-involution reindexing)", "Real.sqrt_ne_zero' (Mathlib Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:273)", "inv_mul_cancel_right₀ (Mathlib Algebra/GroupWithZero/Basic.lean:359)", "Real.mul_self_sqrt (Mathlib Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:149)", "SDF-DEF-01 (IsFrickeSelfDual)"], "difficulty": "moderate", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-03", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.fricke_const_selfDual", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-02"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (run 13), sorry-free, guarded. fricke_const_selfDual : for 0 < N, a Fricke-self-dual exponent vector r (SDF-DEF-01) and k : Int with sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k, the constant of etaQuotient_fricke collapses from (N : Complex)^k * ((sqrt s : Real) : Complex)^{-1} to the SINGLE real square root ((sqrt((N : Real)^k) : Real) : Complex) = N^{k/2}, where s = prod_{delta | N} (delta : Real)^(r delta). This is exactly the non-i half of frickeEigenvalue N k = I^(-k) * ((sqrt((N:Real)^k) : Real) : Complex), so SDF-03 is the step that turns etaQuotient_fricke's r-dependent constant into an r-INDEPENDENT one. PROOF ACTUALLY USED (4 steps, no gap, verified this run): (1) rw [prod_zpow_selfDual hN hr hk] (SDF-02) replaces s by (N:Real)^k -- this is the ONLY place hr is used, and everything after it is the identity a * (sqrt a)^{-1} = sqrt a at the positive real a = N^k; (2) hapos : 0 < (N:Real)^k by zpow_pos of hNpos, and hne : sqrt((N:Real)^k) != 0 by Real.sqrt_ne_zero'.mpr hapos -- zpow_pos, NOT pow_pos, because k may be negative; (3) the whole content as an identity in the REALS, hR : (N:Real)^k * (sqrt((N:Real)^k))^{-1} = sqrt((N:Real)^k), by rw [inv_eq_one_div, mul_one_div, div_eq_iff hne, Real.mul_self_sqrt hapos.le] -- i.e. a * (sqrt a)^{-1} = a / sqrt a = sqrt a because sqrt a * sqrt a = a; (4) transport into Complex along Complex.ofReal by congrArg then push_cast, which moves the cast inward through Complex.ofReal_mul, Complex.ofReal_inv, Complex.ofReal_zpow and Complex.ofReal_natCast, turning ((N:Real)^k : Complex) into (N:Complex)^k. DELIBERATE DEFINITIONAL DISCIPLINE: the identity is proved in Real and only then cast, so NO complex square root and NO branch choice arises anywhere in this node; the Real-level identity is transported through Complex.ofReal_natCast rather than re-derived in Complex, which is the CAUTION the node's earlier OPEN comment recorded. NOTE ON Real.sq_sqrt: the node's built_from named Real.sq_sqrt; the proof actually closes with Real.mul_self_sqrt (Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:149), the mul form rather than the sq form. Both exist in the pinned Mathlib and either would do; recorded so built_from is not read as a claim about which one the term uses. COMPOSITION WITH THE REFERENCE: etaQuotient_fricke's RHS is left-associated as ((I^(-k) * (N:Complex)^k) * (sqrt s)^{-1}) * z^k * ..., so (N:Complex)^k * (sqrt s)^{-1} is not a syntactic subterm there and ONE mul_assoc is needed at the point of use in SDF-05. That is bookkeeping, already flagged in SDF-05's OPEN comment, not a gap in this node. WHY THE HYPOTHESES ARE THE RIGHT ONES: hr and hk are load-bearing exactly as in SDF-02, which this node calls -- prod_zpow_pin_asymmetric_ne (PROVED) is an hk-satisfying counterexample to the hr-free version. hN mirrors etaQuotient_fricke's own hypothesis. HONESTY NOTE, recorded rather than hidden: at N = 0 the statement happens to hold degenerately (empty divisors force k = 0 and both sides are 1), so hN is very slightly stronger than strictly needed; it is kept because dropping it would desynchronise this statement from etaQuotient_fricke, and it does not weaken the node relative to its reference. PINS, ALL PROVED AND ALL STATED BEFORE THE GENERAL LEMMA, with every numeral computed OUTSIDE Lean first in exact Python Fraction arithmetic this session, and with the two sides asserted as SEPARATE CONJUNCTS against the SAME pre-computed numeral (a single LHS = RHS equation can be satisfied by two matching errors; each conjunct here must hit a number fixed in advance): fricke_const_pin_level_one (N=1, r=(24), k=12; s=1, both sides 1; DEGENERATE BY CONSTRUCTION -- at N=1 both sides are 1 for every r and k, so it certifies only that the expression elaborates and reduces at the instance underlying the already sorry-free eta_S_via_fricke, EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246, and carries no evidence about exponents); fricke_const_pin_level_six (N=6, r=(1,11,11,1) on (1,2,3,6), k=12; THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, the only one with N>1 AND a non-constant vector: s = 2176782336 = 6^12, sqrt s = 46656, LHS = 6^12 * 46656^{-1} = 2176782336/46656 = 46656, and independently sqrt(6^12) = 46656 -- and since 46656 != 2176782336 this is also what separates sqrt(N^k) from N^k); fricke_const_pin_zero_exp (r == 0 at N=6, k=0; DEGENERATE floor -- k=0 makes N^k = 1 for every N, so a statement proving only the k=0 case would still pass); fricke_const_pin_level_four_neg (N=4, r=(-2,6,-2) on (1,2,4), k=1; NEGATIVE ENTRIES: s = 64/16 = 4, LHS = 4 * 2^{-1} = 2 = sqrt(4^1), the instance that passes through (4:Real)^{-2} and so exercises the zpow_pos positivity step; level four also contributes the only N>1 divisor that is its own dual, 4/2 = 2); and fricke_const_pin_level_six_neg (N=6, r=(-1,-11,-11,-1), k=-12; NEGATIVE WEIGHT, NEW this run and the only pin with k < 0: s = 6^{-12} = 1/2176782336, sqrt s = 1/46656, LHS = 6^{-12} * 46656 = 1/46656 = sqrt(6^{-12}) -- here N^k and sqrt(N^k) are proper FRACTIONS rather than integers, so a version of this node that had silently assumed k >= 0 (k.toNat anywhere, or pow_pos in place of zpow_pos) would satisfy pins A-D and FAIL here). The negative-weight pin's hypotheses are separately machine-checked (rPinLevelSixNeg_selfDual, rPinLevelSixNeg_weight, prod_zpow_pin_level_six_neg), so it is a genuine instance of this node and not an unrelated arithmetic fact; its vector rPinLevelSixNeg is new this run and is the entrywise negation of rPinSix. NEGATIVE CONTROLS, both PROVED, both failing exactly at the load-bearing instance and invisible at the degenerate ones (which is why the degenerate pins are not sufficient alone): fricke_const_pin_not_natPow shows the SQUARE ROOT cannot be dropped -- sqrt(6^12) = 46656 != 2176782336 = 6^12, so a version asserting N^k * s^{-1/2} = N^k is FALSE; fricke_const_pin_not_mul shows the INVERSION cannot be dropped -- 6^12 * sqrt s = 101559956668416 != 46656 = sqrt(6^12), so a version that transcribed the constant without the inverse is FALSE. APPLICATION CHECKS: fricke_const_selfDual_pin_level_six (PROVED) re-derives 46656 and fricke_const_selfDual_pin_level_six_neg (PROVED) re-derives 1/46656 by RUNNING the general lemma at (6, rPinSix, 12) and (6, rPinLevelSixNeg, -12), i.e. THROUGH the general proof rather than around it, where the corresponding pins assert the same numbers by direct computation. So the general statement is checked to FIRE at concrete instances -- including at NEGATIVE weight, which is how it is verified not to assume k >= 0 -- and to return the independently computed value, not merely to be true in the abstract. A general lemma that had drifted (N^k for sqrt(N^k), s^{+1/2} for s^{-1/2}, a wrong exponent) would return a different number there while staying provable in its own terms. AXIOM FOOTPRINT, verified this run: fricke_const_selfDual and all fifteen accompanying value lemmas, pins, hypothesis witnesses, controls and application checks depend on [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -- no sorryAx, and no Lean.ofReduceBool (the concrete pins use decide for Nat.divisors and norm_num plus Real.sqrt_sq for the real arithmetic; native_decide is deliberately not used). Sixteen #guard_msgs in #print axioms guards in Lean/SocrateAI/FinalCheck.lean, new section Sdf03. BUILD: lake --packages=local-packages.json build SocrateAI -> 'Build completed successfully (3769 jobs).', exit 0, 0 errors, 18 sorry warnings -- one FEWER than the 19 recorded when SDF-02 closed, and fricke_const_selfDual is no longer among them; all 18 are pre-existing open nodes (14 in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean: the five selfDual_pin_* conjunctions and SDF-04..SDF-12; plus EtaMultiplier 2, EtaLigozatKronecker 1, TDualityBridge 1). NAMING: the condition r delta = r(N/delta) is called SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is already taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), and is ALSO Persson-Volpato's term for this condition, so it collides twice. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. This node is an identity between real and complex numbers attached to an eta-quotient exponent vector and nothing else. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-02 (prod_zpow_selfDual) -- does all the arithmetic; the ONLY place hr is used", "zpow_pos (NOT pow_pos: k may be negative, which fricke_const_pin_level_six_neg pins at k = -12)", "Real.sqrt_ne_zero' (Mathlib Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:273)", "Real.mul_self_sqrt (Mathlib Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:149) -- the mul form; the node's earlier built_from named Real.sq_sqrt (Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:178), which would also do", "inv_eq_one_div, mul_one_div, div_eq_iff (the a * (sqrt a)^{-1} = a / sqrt a = sqrt a route)", "Complex.ofReal_mul, Complex.ofReal_inv, Complex.ofReal_zpow, Complex.ofReal_natCast (via push_cast) -- the Real identity is TRANSPORTED, not re-derived in Complex", "Real.sqrt_sq (Mathlib Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:181) -- used only by the concrete pins, to evaluate sqrt(6^12) = 46656, sqrt(4^1) = 2, sqrt(6^-12) = 1/46656"], "difficulty": "moderate", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-04", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-01", "SDF-DEF-01"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (run 14), sorry-free, guarded. THE EIGENFORM RELATION, RAW SHAPE. etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) {r : EtaExp} (hr : IsFrickeSelfDual N r) {k : Int} (hk : sum_{delta in N.divisors} r delta = 2*k) {z : Complex} (hz : z in H_open) : etaQuotient N r (-(1/(N*z))) = I^(-k) * (N:Complex)^k * ((Real.sqrt (prod_{delta in N.divisors} (delta:Real)^(r delta)) : Real) : Complex)^{-1} * z^k * etaQuotient N r z -- the SAME r on both sides. PROOF ACTUALLY USED, verbatim and complete (2 rewrites, no gap, nothing else): rw [etaQuotient_fricke hN r hk hz, etaQuotient_congr_divisors (N := N) (r := fun delta => r (N / delta)) (s := r) z (fun delta hdelta => (hr delta hdelta).symm)]. The first rewrite instantiates the already-proved F3.2-A7 theorem (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2212), whose RHS carries the DUAL quotient etaQuotient N (fun delta => r (N/delta)) z; the second replaces that dual quotient by the original via SDF-01 and closes the goal BY RFL -- there is no residual obligation and no side condition, which is exactly what the four instance pins below machine-check. The .symm is load-bearing and is not assumed: IsFrickeSelfDual reads r delta = r (N/delta) while etaQuotient_congr_divisors, at this instantiation, needs (fun delta => r (N/delta)) delta = r delta, and the flip is separately pinned by dualExp_congr_pin_level_six_of_selfDual (SDF-01, already proved and guarded). RELATION TO THE REFERENCE: strictly a SPECIALISATION of etaQuotient_fricke -- exactly one hypothesis is ADDED (hr), r goes explicit -> implicit (harmless: r is determined by hr, hk and the conclusion), the LHS is character-identical, the first four RHS factors are character-identical, and the ONLY substantive change is the final factor, dual quotient -> original quotient. Never a strengthening of the reference. THE CONSTANT IS DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED: it is still i^{-k} * N^k * s^{-1/2} with s = prod delta^{r delta} and with r, not the dual vector, inside; nothing about the constant is asserted by this node. Collapsing it to sqrt(N^k) = N^{k/2} is SDF-03/SDF-05, separate nodes with separate guards, so that 'collapse the quotient' (trivial, SDF-01 only) is never conflated with 'collapse the constant' (needs SDF-02's arithmetic). PINS, ALL PROVED AND ALL STATED BEFORE THE GENERAL LEMMA (EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, section Sdf04Pins, above the theorem in the same module). UNLIKE EVERY EARLIER PIN SET IN THIS FILE, these are stated as instances of THIS NODE'S OWN EQUATION at concrete (N, r, k), not of its hypotheses, each discharged along the same two-rewrite route; and NONE OF THEM INVOKES etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw -- not merely asserted: the pins are DECLARED ABOVE the theorem in the same file, so Lean's own scoping makes referring to it impossible and the compiler enforces this rather than a comment. So they are evidence about the route, not consequences of it. selfDual_raw_pin_level_six (N=6, r=(1,11,11,1) on (1,2,3,6), k=12; THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, the only instance with N>1 AND a non-constant exponent vector, hence the only one where the dual quotient is a genuinely reordered product that must be collapsed by SDF-01 rather than by rfl; a statement that had transposed the divisor pairing would close every other pin and fail here -- cf. not_selfDual_pin_mispaired, whose vector carries the SAME weight sum r delta = 24). selfDual_raw_pin_level_four_neg (N=4, r=(-2,6,-2) on (1,2,4), k=1; NEGATIVE EXPONENTS -- every other pin here has non-negative entries so no factor is ever inverted -- and the only level here with a divisor that is its OWN dual, 4/2 = 2, a fixed point of delta -> N/delta that levels 1, 2 and 6 do not have, so the collapse must handle a diagonal term as well as a transposed pair). selfDual_raw_pin_level_one (N=1, r=(24), k=12, the Delta = eta^24 case; DEGENERATE BY CONSTRUCTION and recorded as such -- at N=1 the only divisor is its own dual, so the collapse step is a syntactic no-op and this pin carries NO evidence about the involution; its value is the external cross-check below). selfDual_raw_pin_zero_exp (r == 0 at N=6, k=0; DEGENERATE BY CONSTRUCTION, true for every N, and k=0 makes N^k = 1, so a statement proving only k=0 would still pass; it is a floor certifying the equation is not mis-indexed into something unsatisfiable, not evidence about exponents). Weight witnesses rPinOne_weight, rPinSix_weight and zeroExp_weight_level_six are new this run and all close by decide (never native_decide, so no Lean.ofReduceBool enters the footprint); rPinLevelFourNeg_selfDual and rPinLevelFourNeg_weight were already proved for SDF-02. EXTERNAL CROSS-CHECK (LL-1, run in the strong direction): selfDual_raw_pin_level_one_is_eta_S carries the level-one instance all the way down -- divisors 1 = {1}, prod delta^{r delta} = 1^24 = 1, sqrt 1 = 1, N^k = 1^12 = 1, i^{-12} = 1 -- to eta(-1/z)^24 = z^12 * eta(z)^24. That conclusion is eta_S_via_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246, sorry-free, and itself checked there against MATHLIB's ModularForm.discriminant_S_invariant). It is DERIVED FROM THE PIN, not cited, and this is CHECKED rather than asserted: its proof names neither target, and since both ARE in scope there (EtaQuotientModularity is imported) absence from the source text is not sufficient on its own, so the gap is closed by the fact that every tactic in that proof except norm_num takes an EXPLICIT lemma list and NEITHER TARGET CARRIES @[simp] -- verified this run by grep over this library and over the pinned Mathlib, where Mathlib/NumberTheory/ModularForms/Discriminant.lean:143 declares discriminant_S_invariant as a bare lemma -- so norm_num's default simp set cannot reach them either. It is therefore an agreement between two independent derivations rather than a restatement of one. A wrong i^{-k}, a wrong power of N, or a sqrt(s) inverted onto the wrong side of the fraction fails there. HONESTY NOTE ON A VERIFICATION THAT WAS ATTEMPTED AND DISCARDED, recorded rather than hidden: a stronger check was first attempted -- a Lean metaprogram computing the transitive constant-dependency closure of each pin's proof term -- and it was ABANDONED as unsound on this toolchain, not reported as passing. Under Lean 4.32.2 theorem proofs are elaborated asynchronously and ConstantInfo.value? returns none for them, so the metaprogram traversed types only and returned 'false' even for dependencies that demonstrably exist (it reported etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw as NOT depending on etaQuotient_fricke, which its one-line proof plainly does). No claim in this node rests on that discarded check. NON-VACUITY OF THE ADDED HYPOTHESIS (so the node is not the general theorem with a decorative hypothesis bolted on): not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric and not_selfDual_pin_mispaired (both PROVED and guarded under FinalCheck section SdfDef01) show IsFrickeSelfDual is a genuine restriction, and fricke_dual_pin (EtaQuotientModularity.lean, sorry-free) proves that at that same r = (2,0), f(z) = eta(z)^2, the Fricke transform lands on eta(2z)^2 -- the quotient of the DUAL vector (0,2), not of r. STATED PRECISELY so it is not oversold: what is MACHINE-PROVED is (a) that r fails the hypothesis (decide) and (b) that the transform lands on the dual vector's quotient; that eta(z)^2 and eta(2z)^2 are different FUNCTIONS is true and is recorded in fricke_dual_pin's docstring, but it is NOT itself a theorem in this library, so 'the conclusion of this node is false at that r' is a hand-checked (D-tier) claim here, not a Lean-level one. Satisfiability with a non-constant r at N>1 is witnessed by rPinSix (selfDual_cond_pin_level_six + rPinSix_nonconstant + rPinSix_weight) and by rPinLevelFourNeg. QUANTIFIER RANGE, checked rather than assumed: etaQuotient is a Finset.prod over N.divisors, etaQuotient_congr_divisors quantifies over N.divisors, and IsFrickeSelfDual quantifies over N.divisors -- the three ranges agree exactly, so the hypothesis is neither too weak (off-divisor values are never read on either side) nor gratuitously strong (an unbounded forall delta would over-constrain junk values). hk is stated for r, which is precisely what etaQuotient_fricke consumes, so no sum over the dual vector and no appeal to sum_divisors_dual is needed or silently assumed. AXIOM FOOTPRINT, verified this run: etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw and all eight accompanying weight witnesses, instance pins and the cross-check depend on [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -- no sorryAx and no Lean.ofReduceBool. Nine #guard_msgs in #print axioms guards in Lean/SocrateAI/FinalCheck.lean, new section Sdf04. The INVERTED TRIPWIRE that previously asserted sorryAx for this theorem (FinalCheck section SdfDef01) was INVERTED BACK in the same edit, with a receipt left in place; the matching tripwire for etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual (SDF-05) is untouched and still asserts sorryAx, which is correct -- SDF-05 remains open. BUILD: lake --packages=local-packages.json build -> 'Build completed successfully (3789 jobs).', exit 0, 0 errors, 17 sorry warnings -- one FEWER than the 18 recorded when SDF-03 closed, and etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw is no longer among them; all 17 are pre-existing open nodes (13 in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean: the five selfDual_pin_* conjunctions and SDF-05..SDF-12; plus EtaMultiplier 2, EtaLigozatKronecker 1, TDualityBridge 1). NAMING: the condition r delta = r(N/delta) is called SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is already taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), and is ALSO Persson-Volpato's term for this condition, so it collides twice. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. This node is an identity between two explicit products of values of Mathlib's ModularForm.eta; it says nothing about Gamma_0(N)-modularity, nothing about holomorphy at the cusps, and nothing about S-duality, the axio-dilaton or CHL models. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["etaQuotient_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2212, proved sorry-free, tag F3.2-A7) -- supplies the transformation law with the DUAL exponent vector on the right", "SDF-01 (etaQuotient_congr_divisors) -- instantiated at r := fun d => r (N / d), s := r; collapses the dual quotient and closes the goal by rfl", "SDF-DEF-01 (IsFrickeSelfDual) -- the added hypothesis, consumed through .symm because it reads r delta = r (N/delta) while the congruence needs the reverse orientation", "eta_S_via_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246) and ModularForm.discriminant_S_invariant (Mathlib NumberTheory/ModularForms/Discriminant.lean:143) -- the EXTERNAL TARGETS of selfDual_raw_pin_level_one_is_eta_S, NOT inputs to it: neither is named in its proof and neither carries @[simp], so no tactic there can reach them", "rPinLevelFourNeg_selfDual, rPinLevelFourNeg_weight (already proved for SDF-02) -- hypothesis witnesses for the negative-exponent pin"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-05", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-04", "SDF-03", "SDF-DEF-02"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free, guarded in FinalCheck.lean section Sdf05. THE HEADLINE OF THIS RUN. etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual : for 0 < N, an exponent vector r that is Fricke-self-dual (IsFrickeSelfDual N r, i.e. r delta = r (N/delta) for all delta | N), weight condition sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k, and z in the open upper half-plane, the Fricke transform of the eta quotient returns the SAME eta quotient up to a scalar: etaQuotient N r (-(1/(N*z))) = frickeEigenvalue N k * z^k * etaQuotient N r z, with frickeEigenvalue N k = i^{-k} * sqrt((N:Real)^k) = i^{-k} * N^{k/2} depending ONLY on the level N and the weight k. The exponent vector has vanished from the constant; that is the entire content of self-duality. PROOF: three rewrites and a ring -- SDF-04 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw) for the shape, SDF-03 (fricke_const_selfDual) read BACKWARDS to expand the sqrt(N^k) inside frickeEigenvalue into N^k * s^{-1/2}, then ring for the re-association. No new mathematics: all the arithmetic is in SDF-02 (prod_zpow_selfDual, prod over divisors of delta^{r delta} = N^k). EVIDENCE, all sorry-free and each individually guarded in FinalCheck section Sdf05: five instance pins stated as SDF-05's OWN equation at concrete (N, r, k) -- selfDual_eigen_pin_level_one (N=1, r=(24), k=12, lambda=1), selfDual_eigen_pin_level_six (N=6, r=(1,11,11,1), k=12, lambda=46656 -- THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, the only instance with N>1 AND a non-constant exponent vector, where the collapse moves a real number: 2176782336 * 46656^{-1} = 46656), selfDual_eigen_pin_zero_exp (r=0, k=0, the degenerate floor), selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_neg (N=4, r=(-2,6,-2), k=1, lambda=-2i: the only ODD weight, so i^{-k} is imaginary; the only NEGATIVE exponents; and the only level with a self-dual divisor 4/2=2), and selfDual_eigen_pin_level_six_neg (N=6, k=-12, lambda=1/46656: the only NEGATIVE weight, where N^k and sqrt(N^k) are proper fractions -- the case a k.toNat or pow_pos-for-zpow_pos slip would fail). NONE of the five invokes etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual: they are declared ABOVE it in the same module, so Lean's scoping enforces that rather than a comment. Each is then RE-STATED with the eigenvalue replaced by its hand-computed NUMERAL (the five ..._value pins), reached through SDF-DEF-02's frickeEigenvalue_pin_* lemmas, which are proved from Real.sqrt_sq and never touch s = prod delta^{r delta}. So every numeral is reached twice by routes sharing no lemma, and they agree. The five selfDual_pin_* conjunction pins (SDF-05's bookkeeping) are closed too, by assembly. NON-VACUITY: selfDual_cond_pin_level_six exhibits a self-dual vector at N=6 with rPinSix 1 != rPinSix 2 (rPinSix_nonconstant), so this is not the N=1 case in disguise; not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric and not_selfDual_pin_mispaired decide-prove the hypothesis is a genuine restriction and the divisor involution is the right one; prod_zpow_pin_asymmetric_ne is an hk-satisfying counterexample to dropping hr. TRIPWIRE RECEIPT: the INVERTED tripwire in FinalCheck section SdfDef01 asserting that etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual depends on sorryAx has been inverted back in the same commit, and is replaced by the ordinary positive guard in section Sdf05. No SDF-* node carries an inverted tripwire now. SCOPE, so it is not oversold: this is an identity between two explicit finite products of values of Mathlib's ModularForm.eta. It says NOTHING about Gamma0(N)-modularity, NOTHING about holomorphy or order at the cusps, and NOTHING about physics. External cross-check (not an input): Martin, Multiplicative eta-quotients, Trans. AMS 348 (1996), already in this programme's bibliography for the classical Fricke-eigenvalue fact. NAMING: the condition r delta = r(N/delta) is called SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is already taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), and is ALSO the term Persson-Volpato use for this condition, so it collides twice. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-04 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw)", "SDF-03 (fricke_const_selfDual, used in the reverse direction)", "SDF-DEF-02 (frickeEigenvalue)", "ring"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-06", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-05", "SDF-DEF-02"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free, guarded in FinalCheck.lean section Sdf06. etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized : for 0 < N, r Fricke-self-dual (IsFrickeSelfDual N r), weight sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k, and z in the open upper half-plane, the weight-k, N^{k/2}-normalised Fricke transform of the eta quotient is EXACTLY i^{-k} times the quotient: (sqrt((N:Real)^k) : Complex)^{-1} * z^(-k) * etaQuotient N r (-(1/(N*z))) = I^(-k) * etaQuotient N r z. The level has vanished from the constant, so the eigenvalue is a fourth ROOT OF UNITY. PROOF: SDF-05 for the shape, then two cancellations and a ring for the re-association. WHERE THE N-DEPENDENCE ACTUALLY GOES, so this node is not oversold: the division by sqrt(N^k) is BOOKKEEPING. The constant is r-free in the first place only because prod_{delta | N} delta^{r delta} = N^k on a self-dual vector -- that is SDF-02 (prod_zpow_selfDual, the one genuinely arithmetical step in the file: it routes through sqrt_prod_dual (F3.2-A7) and then uses positivity of the product to pick the root +N^k rather than -N^k), packaged into Complex by SDF-03 and absorbed into frickeEigenvalue by SDF-05. A reader who meets 'the N-dependence cancels completely' and looks for the lemma that earns it will find it in SDF-02, not here. THE TWO CANCELLATIONS EACH NEED A HYPOTHESIS: (sqrt(N^k))^{-1} * sqrt(N^k) = 1 needs sqrt(N^k) != 0, from 0 < N via zpow_pos -- zpow_pos, NOT pow_pos, since k < 0 is in scope and is pinned at k = -12; and z^(-k) * z^k = 1 needs z != 0, extracted from hz exactly as in etaQuotient_fricke. ring performs NEITHER: verified this run by running ring alone on the post-SDF-05 goal, where it FAILS and reports the uncancelled residue sqrt(N^k) * (sqrt(N^k))^{-1} * z^(-k) * i^(-k) * z^k * f = i^(-k) * f. That failure is correct -- both cancellations are false at N = 0 and at z = 0. ring only re-associates. EVIDENCE, all sorry-free and each individually guarded in FinalCheck section Sdf06: five instance pins stated as SDF-06's OWN equation at concrete (N, r, k) -- selfDual_norm_pin_level_one (N=1, r=(24), k=12: normaliser 1, eigenvalue 1), selfDual_norm_pin_level_six (N=6, r=(1,11,11,1), k=12: normaliser 46656^{-1}, eigenvalue 1 -- THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, the only instance with N>1 AND a non-constant exponent vector, hence the only one whose normaliser genuinely divides), selfDual_norm_pin_zero_exp (r=0, k=0, the degenerate floor: k=0 kills all three factors at once), selfDual_norm_pin_level_four_neg (N=4, r=(-2,6,-2), k=1: normaliser 2^{-1}, eigenvalue -i -- the only ODD weight, hence the only instance whose normalised eigenvalue is neither 1 nor -1; without it every guarded instance would have 4 | k and eigenvalue 1, which is also what a statement that had LOST the i^{-k} factor would produce), and selfDual_norm_pin_level_six_neg (N=6, k=-12: normaliser 46656 and weight factor z^{+12} -- THE SIGN PIN of this node, since a transcription with z^k for z^(-k), or with the normaliser uninverted, is FALSE here while surviving the k=0 pin; selfDual_norm_pin_level_one moves the same exponent in the opposite direction, and the two together fix its sign). NONE of the five invokes etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized: they are declared ABOVE it in the same module, so Lean's scoping enforces that rather than a comment. Three are re-stated with normaliser AND eigenvalue replaced by their hand-computed numerals (the ..._value pins). EXTERNAL CROSS-CHECK, derived not cited: selfDual_norm_pin_level_one_is_eta_S carries the level-one instance down to z^(-12) * eta(-1/z)^24 = eta(z)^24, which is eta_S_via_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246, sorry-free) divided by z^12 and which MATHLIB proves independently as discriminant_S_invariant; the proof starts from selfDual_eigen_pin_level_one_value, names neither target, and every tactic in it takes an explicit lemma list (neither target carries @[simp], re-verified this run over this library and over the pinned Mathlib). APPLICATION CHECKS: etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized_pin_level_six and ..._pin_level_six_neg state the same two equations as the ..._value pins but RUN THE GENERAL LEMMA at those instances, so each equation is reached twice by routes sharing no lemma and they agree; the negative-weight one is what shows the general proof does not silently assume k >= 0. NEGATIVE CONTROL, with its honest limit: selfDual_norm_pin_asymmetric_ne shows the two normalisers diverge at the non-self-dual rPinAsym = (2,0) at N=2, k=1, which satisfies the weight hypothesis exactly (rPinAsym_weight) and fails self-duality (not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric) -- SDF-06's sqrt(2^1) = sqrt 2 against the raw law's sqrt(1^2 * 2^0) = 1 -- so hr is load-bearing. What is machine-proved is the discrepancy between the two NORMALISERS; that the full conclusion also fails at that r (fricke_dual_pin gives eta(-1/(2z))^2 = -2i z eta(2z)^2, so the hr-free reading would assert -i*sqrt2*eta(2z)^2 = -i*eta(z)^2, wrong constant AND wrong function) needs eta(z)^2 != eta(2z)^2 as FUNCTIONS, which is true, is recorded in fricke_dual_pin's docstring, and is NOT a theorem in this library -- so that half is asserted at the hand-check level, exactly as for SDF-04. ALL PIN VALUES were computed outside Lean in exact arithmetic this run, BEFORE the statement was endorsed, and none was adjusted to fit a proof: N=1 k=12 s=1=1^12 sqrt=1 i^{-12}=1; N=6 r=(1,11,11,1) k=12 s=2^11*3^11*6=2176782336=6^12 sqrt=46656; N=4 r=(-2,6,-2) k=1 s=2^6/4^2=4=4^1 sqrt=2 i^{-1}=-i; N=6 k=-12 s=6^{-12} sqrt=1/46656 so the normaliser is 46656; r=0 k=0 s=1=6^0. WRITTEN LONGHAND RATHER THAN THROUGH MATHLIB'S SLASH OPERATOR, DELIBERATELY: Mathlib's GL(2,Real) slash carries a det^(k-1) factor, and the Fricke matrix has determinant N, so restating this via the slash would CHANGE THE CONSTANT. That is not a cosmetic change and must not be made without re-pinning. The claim that this normalisation is the classical one (Martin, Multiplicative eta-quotients, Trans. AMS 348 (1996)) is a CITATION claim about Martin's convention, at the literature (L) tier of this programme's ladder, and is checked by nothing here -- it must not be reported as verified. SCOPE, so it is not oversold: this is an identity between two explicit finite products of values of Mathlib's ModularForm.eta. It says NOTHING about Gamma0(N)-modularity, NOTHING about holomorphy or order at the cusps, and NOTHING about physics. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the L tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one. Note also, from that file's header, that their Frame-shape condition is the WEIGHTED sum sum_{a | N} a*m(a) = 24, not this library's sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k; the two agree only at N=1, so the physics-side correspondence is looser than 'the same equation' and the prose must not claim otherwise. NAMING: the condition r delta = r(N/delta) is SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric), NEVER 'balanced'.", "built_from": ["SDF-05 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual)", "SDF-DEF-02 (frickeEigenvalue, unfolded)", "zpow_add0 (for z^(-k) * z^k = 1)", "inv_mul_cancel0 (for (sqrt(N^k))^{-1} * sqrt(N^k) = 1)", "Real.sqrt_ne_zero'", "zpow_pos (NOT pow_pos: k may be negative)", "Complex.ofReal_ne_zero", "ring"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-07", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.I_zpow_emod", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "PROVED (sorry-free, guarded in SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf07). I_zpow_emod (k : Int) : (Complex.I) ^ k = I ^ (k % 4) — periodicity of INTEGER powers of i, where % is Int.emod so the reduced exponent lies in [0,4) (companion lemma I_zpow_emod_exponent_mem, also proved and guarded). NOT ALREADY IN MATHLIB, re-verified this session by whole-library grep with no truncation: Complex.I_pow_eq_pow_mod (Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.lean:633) is the NATURAL-exponent version only, and the generic zpow_eq_zpow_emod (Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Basic.lean:849) that would have subsumed it sits inside section Group (variable [Group G], opened at Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Basic.lean:594 and not closed before line 849), while C is not a group under multiplication; a whole-Mathlib grep for a GroupWithZero/DivisionRing zpow-emod variant returns nothing. Hence the proof goes through zpow_add0, paying the I != 0 side condition (Complex.I_ne_zero). PROOF: k = k % 4 + 4 * (k / 4) (Int.emod_add_mul_ediv, Lean core Init/Data/Int/DivMod/Bootstrap.lean:100), then zpow_add0 Complex.I_ne_zero, then zpow_mul and Complex.I_pow_four collapse i^(4*(k/4)) to 1 via one_zpow. SIX INSTANCE PINS, all stated and proved ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them using it, each computing its two sides by routes that do not meet: I_zpow_emod_pin_twelve (k=12, %4=0, value 1 — the exponent of frickeEigenvalue 1 12, the N=1 r=(24) k=12 instance underlying the sorry-free eta_S_via_fricke), I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_twelve (k=-12, %4=0, value 1 — the exponent that actually appears in the load-bearing N=6 self-dual instance), I_zpow_emod_pin_zero (k=0, DEGENERATE and recorded as such: after its decide the two sides are the same term, so it constrains nothing), I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_one (k=-1, %4=3, value -i — the odd case, and the pin that fixes % as Int.emod rather than Int.tmod, since under tmod the reduced exponent would be -1 and the pin would collapse to a tautology), I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_two (k=-2, %4=2, value -1 — THE SIGN PIN, the exponent behind frickeEigenvalue 1 2 = -1 whose eta-quotient witness is selfDual_pin_eigenvalue_neg_one), I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_fifteen (k=-15, %4=1, value i — the pin no +-1 coincidence can fake, since neither side is real and it is invisible to the +-1 bookkeeping of SDF-08/SDF-09). All 81 exponents in [-40,40] were checked outside Lean BEFORE the statement was written, in exact Gaussian-rational arithmetic (repeated multiplication for k >= 0, explicit conjugate/norm inversion for k < 0): zero mismatches, and the four values at k = 12, -12, -1, -2 agree with the file's already sorry-free I_zpow_twelve, I_zpow_neg_twelve, I_zpow_neg_one, I_zpow_neg_two. TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS: I_zpow_emod_pin_not_mod_two shows the modulus 4 is load-bearing (at k=3 a mod-2 statement asserts -i = i, refuted through Complex.I_im), and I_zpow_emod_pin_nontrivial_reduction shows the reduction is not the identity map ((-15) % 4 = 1 != -15), so the node is not a disguised tautology. APPLICATION CHECK: I_zpow_emod_pin_application reaches five of the six pinned equations by RUNNING the general lemma, so each is proved twice by routes sharing no lemma. COMPARATOR: NO_REFERENCE against etaQuotient_fricke — this node is an auxiliary C-arithmetic lemma FEEDING the downstream +-1 classification (SDF-08/SDF-09), not a specialisation of the Fricke transformation law in either direction; it mentions no etaQuotient, no level, no weight and no z, and depends_on is empty. NAMING: SDF-08's forward direction already exists in this library as I_zpow_neg_eq_one (EtaQuotientPrimeLevel.lean:630, sorry-free, same namespace), which is not in scope in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean but IS imported by FinalCheck, so SDF-08 must keep its _iff suffix. I_zpow_emod itself is a fresh name library-wide (grep-verified). PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["Complex.I_pow_four (Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.lean:631)", "Complex.I_ne_zero (Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.lean:257)", "Complex.I_sq (Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.lean:625) [pins]", "Complex.inv_I [pin F]", "Complex.I_im [negative control 1]", "Int.emod_add_mul_ediv (Lean core Init/Data/Int/DivMod/Bootstrap.lean:100)", "Int.emod_nonneg (Lean core Init/Data/Int/DivMod/Bootstrap.lean:199) [exponent-range companion]", "Int.emod_lt_of_pos (Lean core Init/Data/Int/DivMod/Bootstrap.lean:203) [exponent-range companion]", "zpow_add₀ (Mathlib/Algebra/GroupWithZero/Basic.lean:510)", "zpow_mul (Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Basic.lean:468, section DivisionMonoid — unconditional for ℂ)", "zpow_natCast, one_zpow, zpow_zero, zpow_one, zpow_neg", "I_zpow_twelve, I_zpow_neg_twelve, I_zpow_neg_one, I_zpow_neg_two (this file, already sorry-free) [pins]"], "difficulty": "moderate", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf07 (#print axioms I_zpow_emod and 10 supporting declarations)"}
{"id": "SDF-08", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.I_zpow_neg_eq_one_iff", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-07"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free, guarded in SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf08. I_zpow_neg_eq_one_iff (k : Int) : (Complex.I) ^ (-k) = 1 if and only if 4 divides k (EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean:2523). This is the condition under which the NORMALISED Fricke eigenvalue of SDF-06 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized, whose constant is exactly i^{-k}) is +1. WHAT THIS NODE IS NOT: an equivalence between a C-valued zpow equation and an integer divisibility. It mentions no level N, no exponent vector r, no point z and no eta quotient, and it is NOT a specialisation of etaQuotient_fricke -- that specialisation is SDF-04 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw). SDF-08 is downstream of the Fricke work only through the CONSTANT: i^{-k} is one factor of frickeEigenvalue N k. PROOF AS ACTUALLY WRITTEN, which differs in two recorded ways from the OPEN sketch this node carried: SDF-07 (I_zpow_emod) reduces the exponent to (-k) % 4, which lies in {0,1,2,3} (Int.emod_nonneg, Int.emod_lt_of_pos, then omega gives the four-way case split); the three non-zero residues are refuted by evaluating i^1 = i (zpow_one), i^2 = -1 (Complex.I_sq) and i^3 = -i (pow_succ ON TOP OF Complex.I_sq -- I_sq alone does NOT reach i^3, which the sketch did not say), then comparing ONE COORDINATE against 1 via congrArg Complex.im / congrArg Complex.re plus Complex.I_im, Complex.one_re, Complex.one_im -- so Complex.ext_iff, which the sketch named, is NOT used. Finally (-k) % 4 = 0 <-> 4 | k is inside omega's numeral emod/dvd fragment, so Int.emod_emod_of_dvd and Int.dvd_neg are NOT used either. BOTH directions run through SDF-07: the converse is NOT a reuse of the sorry-free I_zpow_neg_eq_one (EtaQuotientPrimeLevel.lean:630), which is OUT OF SCOPE in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean -- those two modules are siblings, both importing EtaQuotientModularity and neither importing the other. FinalCheck imports BOTH, which is why the _iff suffix is mandatory. SIX WEIGHT PINS, all stated ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them from using it, each settling its two sides by routes that do not meet (C side through the sorry-free I_zpow_* value lemmas of section SdfDef02Pins, or at k=15 through I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_fifteen; Z side by decide): PIN A k=12 (i^{-12}=1, 4|12) the weight of selfDual_eigen_pin_level_one (the eta_S_via_fricke instance) AND of selfDual_eigen_pin_level_six -- one weight, two levels, which is the point since SDF-08 sees only k; PIN B k=-12 (i^{12}=1 via I_zpow_twelve after neg_neg, 4|-12) the weight of selfDual_eigen_pin_level_six_neg, the pin that catches a proof assuming 0 <= k; PIN C k=0 (r=0, selfDual_eigen_pin_zero_exp) DEGENERATE and recorded as such -- after neg_zero its left conjunct is zpow_zero, so it constrains nothing; PIN D k=2, BOTH SIDES FALSE (i^{-2} = -1 != 1 refuted through Complex.one_re, and 4 does not divide 2) -- THE LOAD-BEARING CONTROL, k=2 being the weight of selfDual_pin_eigenvalue_neg_one (eta^4 at level one, eigenvalue -1), so a statement on the wrong residue class (2 | k, or the divisor dropped to 2) would break here and would hand SDF-09 the wrong sign; PIN E k=1 (i^{-1} = -i, refuted through Complex.I_im) the weight of selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_neg; PIN F k=15 (i^{-15} = i, a value that is neither 1 nor -1, so invisible to any +-1 coincidence). APPLICATION CHECK I_zpow_neg_eq_one_iff_pin_application re-derives all six by RUNNING the general lemma at those weights, so each pinned instance is settled twice by routes sharing no lemma, and they agree. OUTSIDE-LEAN CHECK done BEFORE any Lean statement: i^{-k} = 1 <-> 4 | k verified in exact Gaussian-integer arithmetic at all 121 weights k in [-60,60] (positive powers by repeated multiplication, negative ones by conjugation since |i^m| = 1); zero mismatches. COMPARATOR NOTE: the statement comparator for this node was assigned etaQuotient_fricke as the reference and correctly returned NO_REFERENCE -- SDF-08 is not in that theorem's subject matter, there is nothing to substitute into. SDF-09 should be compared against SDF-07 plus selfDual_pin_eigenvalue_neg_one, and SDF-10 against Mathlib zpow_eq_one_iff_right0. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-07 (I_zpow_emod, this file)", "Complex.I_sq (Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.lean:625)", "pow_succ (needed for i^3; Complex.I_sq alone does not reach it)", "Complex.I_im, Complex.one_re, Complex.one_im (coordinate refutations, via congrArg -- NOT Complex.ext_iff)", "Int.emod_nonneg, Int.emod_lt_of_pos (Lean core Init/Data/Int/DivMod/Bootstrap.lean:199,203)", "omega (four-way residue split; and (-k) % 4 = 0 <-> 4 | k in both directions)", "zpow_natCast, zpow_zero, zpow_one, neg_neg, neg_zero", "I_zpow_twelve, I_zpow_neg_twelve, I_zpow_neg_one, I_zpow_neg_two, I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_fifteen (this file, already sorry-free) [pins]"], "difficulty": "moderate", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf08 (#print axioms I_zpow_neg_eq_one_iff and 7 supporting declarations: six weight pins plus the application check)"}
{"id": "SDF-09", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-07"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free, guarded in SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf09. I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff (k : Int) : (Complex.I) ^ (-k) = -1 if and only if k % 4 = 2 (EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean:2794), with % the Int.emod of Lean's Mod Int instance. This is the condition under which the NORMALISED Fricke eigenvalue of SDF-06 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized, whose constant is exactly i^{-k}) is -1, i.e. when a Fricke-self-dual eta quotient of weight k is a (-1)-eigenform of the normalised Fricke involution. KEPT A SEPARATE NODE FROM SDF-08 ON PURPOSE: the SIGN of the eigenvalue is exactly the quantity a sign error corrupts, so a sign regression shows up in the DAG rather than buried inside somebody else's conjunction. WHAT THIS NODE IS NOT: it is an equivalence between a C-valued zpow equation and an integer congruence; it mentions no level N, no exponent vector r, no point z and no eta quotient, and it is NOT a specialisation of etaQuotient_fricke -- that specialisation is SDF-04. i^{-k} occurs in etaQuotient_fricke only as an opaque subterm of the scalar, about which that theorem makes no claim, so no substitution into it produces this statement. SDF-09 is downstream of the Fricke work only through the CONSTANT: i^{-k} is one factor of frickeEigenvalue N k. PROOF AS ACTUALLY WRITTEN, which differs in three recorded ways from this node's built_from as originally filed: SDF-07 (I_zpow_emod) reduces the exponent to (-k) % 4, which lies in {0,1,2,3} (Int.emod_nonneg, Int.emod_lt_of_pos, then omega for the four-way split -- these emod-range facts were MISSING from the filed built_from and are now listed); three residues are refuted by evaluating the power and comparing ONE coordinate against -1 via congrArg (i^0 = 1 through Complex.one_re/Complex.neg_re, i^1 = i and i^3 = -i through Complex.I_im), so Complex.ext_iff, which the filed built_from named, is NOT used; the surviving residue (-k) % 4 = 2 gives the value -1 by Complex.I_sq, and (-k) % 4 = 2 <-> k % 4 = 2 is inside omega's numeral-emod fragment, so Int.emod_emod_of_dvd is NOT used either. That last conversion is ALSO isolated as its own sorry-free, separately guarded lemma I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff_emod_neg so it can be inspected alone. Note i^3 needs pow_succ ON TOP OF Complex.I_sq -- I_sq alone does not reach it. SIX WEIGHT PINS, all stated ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them from using it, each settling its two sides by routes that do not meet (C side through the sorry-free I_zpow_* value lemmas of section SdfDef02Pins, or at k=15 through I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_fifteen; Z side by decide): PIN A k=12, both sides FALSE (i^{-12} = 1 != -1 refuted through Complex.one_re, 12 % 4 = 0) -- the N=1 r=(24) k=12 weight behind the sorry-free eta_S_via_fricke and also the weight of the genuine N=6 self-dual instance selfDual_eigen_pin_level_six; PIN B k=-12, both sides FALSE, reached through I_zpow_twelve after neg_neg so it shares no value lemma with PIN A -- the weight of selfDual_eigen_pin_level_six_neg, and the pin that would catch a proof assuming 0 <= k; PIN C k=0, THE DEGENERATE CASE (r = 0, selfDual_eigen_pin_zero_exp), both sides FALSE, recorded as degenerate rather than as evidence since after neg_zero its left conjunct is zpow_zero; PIN D k=2, BOTH SIDES TRUE and THE LOAD-BEARING PIN (i^{-2} = -1 via I_zpow_neg_two, 2 % 4 = 2) -- the weight of selfDual_pin_eigenvalue_neg_one (eta^4 at level one, eigenvalue -1, computed by hand from eta(-1/z)^4 = (-i z)^2 eta(z)^4 = -z^2 eta(z)^4) and of frickeEigenvalue_pin_neg_one, the one machine-checked witness in the file that frickeEigenvalue ever takes the value -1, so a statement on the wrong residue class (4 | k, i.e. SDF-08's class) would contradict I_zpow_neg_two here; PIN E k=-2, BOTH SIDES TRUE AT A NEGATIVE WEIGHT and THE emod PIN (i^{-(-2)} = i^2 = -1 via Complex.I_sq, NOT via I_zpow_neg_two, so PIN D and PIN E agree without sharing a route; (-2) % 4 = 2); PIN F k=15, the pin no +-1 coincidence can fake (i^{-15} = i, neither 1 nor -1, refuted through Complex.I_im; 15 % 4 = 3), its value taken from I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_fifteen whose route (zpow_neg, i^15 = -i, Complex.inv_I) shares no lemma with the four-case analysis. TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS: I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_k_not_neg_k records that k % 4 and (-k) % 4 are DIFFERENT functions (1 % 4 = 1 but (-1) % 4 = 3; 15 % 4 = 3 but (-15) % 4 = 1), so stating the right-hand side on the WEIGHT k rather than on the exponent -k is a real choice and not a notational one -- what makes both forms true is only their agreement on the single residue class 2; and I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_emod_not_tmod records that (-2) % 4 = 2 while Int.tmod (-2) 4 = -2 and 2 != -2, so under a truncating remainder PIN E would be FALSE and the node would fail at every negative weight in exactly the class where the eigenvalue is -1. That hazard is therefore machine-checked, not argued. APPLICATION CHECK I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_application re-derives all six pinned weights by RUNNING the general lemma there, so each pinned instance is settled twice by routes sharing no lemma, and they agree. OUTSIDE-LEAN CHECK done BEFORE any Lean statement was written: i^{-k} = -1 <-> k % 4 = 2 verified in exact Gaussian-integer arithmetic at all 401 weights k in [-200,200] (positive powers by repeated multiplication, negative ones by conjugation since |i^m| = 1, % taken as Int.emod); zero mismatches. NOVELTY: a whole-library grep (no truncation) finds no other I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff; the nearest prior art is the ONE-DIRECTIONAL I_zpow_neg_eq_one (EtaQuotientPrimeLevel.lean:630, 4 | k -> i^{-k} = 1) which has no -1 counterpart, and Mathlib has no zpow-level I lemma at all (only the natural-exponent Complex.I_pow_eq_pow_mod). COMPARATOR: the statement comparator for this node was assigned etaQuotient_fricke as its reference and correctly returned NO_REFERENCE -- there is nothing to substitute into, and that is the finding, not a defect in the node. The real dependency is SDF-07 plus the four-case value analysis, exactly as depends_on says. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-07 (I_zpow_emod, this file)", "Complex.I_sq (Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.lean:625)", "pow_succ (needed for i^3; Complex.I_sq alone does not reach it)", "Complex.I_im, Complex.one_re, Complex.neg_re, Complex.neg_im, Complex.one_im (coordinate refutations via congrArg -- NOT Complex.ext_iff, which this node's original built_from named and the proof does not use)", "Int.emod_nonneg, Int.emod_lt_of_pos (Lean core Init/Data/Int/DivMod/Bootstrap.lean:199,203) -- the emod-range facts MISSING from this node's original built_from; they are what make the four-case split exhaustive", "omega (four-way residue split; and (-k) % 4 = 2 <-> k % 4 = 2 in both directions, isolated as I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff_emod_neg)", "zpow_natCast, zpow_zero, zpow_one, neg_neg, neg_zero, neg_mul, one_mul", "I_zpow_twelve, I_zpow_neg_twelve, I_zpow_neg_two, I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_fifteen (this file, already sorry-free) [pins]", "Int.tmod (negative control I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_emod_not_tmod only, by decide)"], "difficulty": "moderate", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf09 (#print axioms I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff and 10 supporting declarations: six weight pins, two negative controls, the k/-k bridge I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff_emod_neg, and the application check)"}
{"id": "SDF-10", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.natCast_zpow_eq_one_iff", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "PROVED (sorry-free, guarded in FinalCheck.lean section Sdf10). natCast_zpow_eq_one_iff {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (k : Int) : (N : Real) ^ k = 1 iff (N = 1 or k = 0). For a positive natural base the integer power hits 1 only in the two degenerate ways. This is the MODULUS half of the +-1 classification: SDF-08 and SDF-09 settled the root of unity i^{-k} in frickeEigenvalue N k, and this settles the other factor, the positive real sqrt(N^k), by settling N^k. It is what rules out any N > 1 with k != 0 in SDF-11 and SDF-12. PROOF: split on N = 1 (Nat.cast_one then one_zpow, true at EVERY integer exponent); otherwise (N : Real) != 1 by injectivity of the cast, and Mathlib's zpow_eq_one_iff_right0 (Algebra/Order/GroupWithZero/Basic.lean:1357) with ha0 := Nat.cast_nonneg N reduces the goal to k = 0 iff (N = 1 or k = 0), closed by Or.resolve_left. Short, as predicted; nothing was forced. NOT A SPECIALISATION OF etaQuotient_fricke: no substitution into that theorem produces this statement, since N^k occurs there only inside the opaque scalar and that theorem makes no claim about when the scalar's modulus is 1. The statement comparator for this node was pointed at etaQuotient_fricke and correctly returned NO_REFERENCE for exactly that reason; the real reference is Mathlib's zpow_eq_one_iff_right0, against which the statement is a repackaging and not a weakening (the a != 1 hypothesis is traded for the extra disjunct N = 1). SIX INSTANCE PINS, all stated ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them from using it, each tied to an eta-quotient instance this file already has: (N,k) = (1,12) the eta_S_via_fricke instance (both sides TRUE, forcing the level clause); (6,12) the genuine N>1 self-dual instance rPinSix (both sides FALSE -- the load-bearing pin, and what makes SDF-11/SDF-12 sharp rather than vacuous); (6,0) the degenerate r = 0 case (both sides TRUE, forcing the weight clause, recorded as degenerate not as evidence); (4,1) odd weight; (6,-12) NEGATIVE weight, where the power is the proper fraction 1/2176782336 and a proof reading zpow as Monoid.npow would break; (1,-12). PIN B's VALUE CHECKED TWICE: natCast_zpow_pin_level_six_value gets 6^12 = 2176782336 by norm_num, and natCast_zpow_pin_level_six_routes_agree gets the same number by squaring the already sorry-free sqrt_natPow_level_six (sqrt(6^12) = 46656, section Sdf03Pins) through Real.sq_sqrt, so this node's modulus and SDF-03's modulus agree or the build fails. TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS, one per disjunct, showing neither is droppable: pin_not_weight_only (1^12 = 1 with 12 != 0, refuting the form ... iff k = 0, i.e. zpow_eq_one_iff_right0 read without its a != 1 hypothesis) and pin_not_level_only (6^0 = 1 with 6 != 1, refuting the form ... iff N = 1); together they also refute the conjunctive form N = 1 and k = 0. hN IS REDUNDANT AND THIS IS PINNED, NOT GLOSSED: natCast_zpow_eq_one_iff_pin_hypothesis_redundant proves the same biconditional at N = 0 at a positive, a negative and a zero weight via zero_zpow_eq_one0. hN is kept and is deliberately UNUSED in the proof, only so this lemma's shape matches SDF-11 and SDF-12, which carry it. No reader should infer that the statement fails at N = 0. OUTSIDE-LEAN CHECK done BEFORE any Lean was written: exact rational arithmetic, no floating point, all 20301 instances N in [0,100], k in [-100,100], with the N = 0 row evaluated under Lean's convention (0 : Real)inv = 0; zero mismatches. APPLICATION CHECK: natCast_zpow_eq_one_iff_pin_application re-derives all six pinned (N,k) by RUNNING the general lemma there, so each is settled twice by routes sharing no lemma, and they agree. All decides are decide, never native_decide, so no Lean.ofReduceBool enters any footprint; all fifteen new declarations depend on exactly [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. NAMING: nothing here is called 'balanced' -- that word is taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), and is also Persson-Volpato's term for the r delta = r(N/delta) condition, which this library calls SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric). PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. This node is an equivalence between a power of a cast natural in Real and a disjunction of two arithmetic conditions. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["zpow_eq_one_iff_right0 (Mathlib Algebra/Order/GroupWithZero/Basic.lean:1357)", "one_zpow (as _root_.one_zpow; Matrix.one_zpow is also in scope via open Matrix)", "Nat.cast_one", "Nat.cast_nonneg", "Or.resolve_left", "zero_zpow_eq_one0 (Mathlib Algebra/GroupWithZero/Basic.lean:494, for the hypothesis-redundancy pin)", "Real.sq_sqrt and the library's own sqrt_natPow_level_six (for PIN B's second route)"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-11", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeEigenvalue_norm", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-02"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (sorry-free, guarded in FinalCheck.lean section Sdf11). frickeEigenvalue_norm {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (k : Int) : norm (frickeEigenvalue N k) = Real.sqrt ((N : Real) ^ k). The MODULUS of the unnormalised Fricke eigenvalue in closed form. frickeEigenvalue N k = I^(-k) * sqrt((N:Real)^k) (SDF-DEF-02) is a fourth root of unity times a NON-NEGATIVE real, so the norm discards the i-factor entirely and returns the real one. WHY IT IS WORTH A NODE: it is what makes the +-1 classification of SDF-12 / SDF-13 split cleanly into an ARGUMENT condition (SDF-08 / SDF-09) and a MODULUS condition (SDF-10) -- lambda = +-1 forces norm(lambda) = 1, which by this node is sqrt(N^k) = 1, which is SDF-10's N^k = 1. Without it that split is asserted rather than proved. PROOF: one rw chain -- frickeEigenvalue, norm_mul, Complex.norm_zpow, Complex.norm_I, Complex.norm_real, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_nonneg (Real.sqrt_nonneg _), one_zpow, one_mul. Nothing is forced and nothing about N or k is ever case-split. NOT A SPECIALISATION OF etaQuotient_fricke: no exponent vector, no z, no eta quotient, no IsFrickeSelfDual hypothesis appears; that specialisation is SDF-04. The statement comparator for this node was pointed at etaQuotient_fricke and correctly returned NO_REFERENCE for exactly that reason -- there is no substitution into that theorem, in either direction, producing this equation. SIX INSTANCE PINS, all stated ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them from using it, each computing BOTH sides by routes sharing no lemma (left through SDF-DEF-02's frickeEigenvalue_pin_* values, right through SDF-03's sqrt_natPow_* radicands): (N,k) = (1,12) the eta_S_via_fricke instance, both sides 1; (6,12) the genuine N>1 self-dual instance rPinSix, both sides 46656 -- LOAD-BEARING; (6,0) the degenerate r = 0 case, both sides 1, recorded as degenerate not as evidence; (2,1) odd weight with both sides IRRATIONAL (sqrt 2), so the equation is not an artefact of integer bookkeeping; (1,2) the eta^4 instance where the EIGENVALUE IS -1 and the modulus is 1 -- the sign pin; (6,-12) NEGATIVE weight, where the modulus is the proper fraction 1/46656 and a proof reading zpow as Monoid.npow would break. THREE NEGATIVE CONTROLS: pin_not_natPow refutes the dropped-square-root reading norm(lambda) = (N:Real)^k at (6,12), where the modulus is 46656 while 6^12 = 2176782336 -- and it takes that second number from SDF-10's already sorry-free natCast_zpow_pin_level_six_value, so the two nodes agree on it or the build fails; pin_not_eigenvalue records that at (1,2) the modulus 1 differs from the eigenvalue -1, so this node gives the SIZE only and must never be read as a closed form for frickeEigenvalue itself; pin_nonconstant records norm(frickeEigenvalue 6 12) != norm(frickeEigenvalue 1 12) at the SAME weight, so the right-hand side genuinely depends on the level and the unnormalised eigenvalue is not a root of unity in general. hN IS REDUNDANT AND THIS IS PINNED, NOT GLOSSED: pin_hypothesis_redundant proves the SAME equation at N = 0 at a negative, a zero and a positive weight. hN is kept and is deliberately UNUSED (with set_option linter.unusedVariables false on that one declaration, for that documented reason), only so this lemma's shape matches SDF-10, SDF-12 and SDF-13. APPLICATION CHECK: frickeEigenvalue_norm_pin_application re-derives all six pinned (N,k) by RUNNING the general lemma there, so each is settled twice by routes sharing no lemma, and they agree. All decides are decide, never native_decide, so no Lean.ofReduceBool enters any footprint; all twelve new declarations depend on exactly [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. NUMBERING: this node's SDF-11 slot was previously occupied by frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff, a RECONSTRUCTION produced by an earlier run whose specification had been truncated mid-node at the string 'theorem frickeEigenvalue_' and which recorded in its own docstring that the label was a guess to be confirmed or replaced. It was wrong. That declaration and its -1 sibling were renumbered to SDF-12 and SDF-13 in the same commit that closed this node, so that no two theorems carry the tag SDF-11. Dated run records in verification/README.md predating that commit use the OLD numbering and were deliberately not rewritten. NAMING: nothing here is called 'balanced' -- that word is taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1); the self-dual condition is IsFrickeSelfDual. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. This node is the modulus of a complex number. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-DEF-02 (frickeEigenvalue, this file)", "norm_mul (Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Field/Basic.lean)", "Complex.norm_zpow (Mathlib/Analysis/Complex/Norm.lean:89) -- the NormedDivisionRing norm_zpow (Analysis/Normed/Field/Basic.lean:88) also works", "Complex.norm_I (Mathlib/Analysis/Complex/Norm.lean:98)", "Complex.norm_real (Mathlib/Analysis/Complex/Norm.lean:103)", "Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_nonneg, Real.sqrt_nonneg", "one_zpow, one_mul, norm_one, norm_neg, norm_inv", "frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_one, ..._pin_level_six, ..._pin_zero_weight, ..._pin_level_two_weight_one, ..._pin_neg_one, ..._pin_level_six_neg (SDF-DEF-02, this file, already sorry-free) [pins, left-hand sides]", "sqrt_natPow_level_one, sqrt_natPow_level_six, sqrt_natPow_zero_weight, sqrt_natPow_level_six_neg (SDF-03, this file, already sorry-free) [pins, right-hand sides]", "natCast_zpow_pin_level_six_value (SDF-10, this file, already sorry-free) [negative control pin_not_natPow only]"], "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf11 (#print axioms frickeEigenvalue_norm and 11 supporting declarations: six instance pins, three negative controls, the hypothesis-redundancy pin, and the application check)", "difficulty": "easy", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean"}
{"id": "SDF-12", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-02", "SDF-08", "SDF-10", "SDF-11"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (sorry-free, guarded in FinalCheck.lean section Sdf12). frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (k : Int) : frickeEigenvalue N k = 1 <-> ((4 : Int) divides k AND (N = 1 OR k = 0)). The unnormalised Fricke eigenvalue lambda = i^{-k} * sqrt(N^k) (SDF-DEF-02) is 1 exactly when BOTH of its factors are 1: the fourth root of unity (SDF-08) and the modulus (SDF-11 plus Real.sqrt_eq_one plus SDF-10). PROOF AS ACTUALLY WRITTEN, four steps, no case split on N or k anywhere. Forward: from lambda = 1 take moduli, so norm(lambda) = 1; SDF-11 (frickeEigenvalue_norm) says norm(lambda) = sqrt((N : Real)^k), hence sqrt((N : Real)^k) = 1; Mathlib's UNCONDITIONAL Real.sqrt_eq_one (Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:172, sqrt x = 1 <-> x = 1, no sign hypothesis) gives (N : Real)^k = 1; SDF-10 (natCast_zpow_eq_one_iff) turns that into N = 1 OR k = 0; substituting sqrt((N : Real)^k) = 1 back into SDF-DEF-02 leaves i^{-k} = 1, and SDF-08 (I_zpow_neg_eq_one_iff) gives 4 divides k. Backward: SDF-10 and SDF-08 in the mpr direction, substituted into SDF-DEF-02, leave 1 * sqrt 1 = 1. CORRECTION TO THIS NODE'S EARLIER built_from: the proof does NOT use Real.sq_sqrt, Real.sqrt_pos or zpow_pos. Real.sqrt_eq_one is unconditional, so no 0 <= (N : Real)^k side goal and no positivity fact about N arises; that is exactly why hN is redundant. SIX INSTANCE PINS, all stated ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them from using it, all reaching the eigenvalue through SDF-DEF-02's frickeEigenvalue_pin_* value lemmas: (1,12) the eta_S_via_fricke instance, both sides TRUE with the level clause firing at a NON-zero weight; (6,12) the genuine N>1 self-dual instance rPinSix -- LOAD-BEARING, both sides FALSE while 4 divides 12 HOLDS, so it is what forces the second conjunct to exist; (6,0) the degenerate r == 0 case, both sides TRUE at a level that is not 1; (2,1) odd weight, lambda = -(i sqrt 2), refuted through its modulus; (1,2) the eta^4 instance where lambda = -1 and the modulus IS 1 -- the SIGN CONTROL, what forces the first conjunct to exist; (6,-12) NEGATIVE weight, lambda = 1/46656, where a proof assuming 0 <= k breaks. TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS, one per conjunct: ..._pin_not_level_only refutes the weakened lambda = 1 <-> (N = 1 OR k = 0) at (1,2), i.e. SDF-10 alone does not settle this node; ..._pin_not_dvd_only refutes the weakened lambda = 1 <-> 4 divides k at (6,12), i.e. SDF-08 alone does not either. APPLICATION CHECK: frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff_pin_application re-derives all six pinned (N,k) by RUNNING the general lemma there. hN IS MATHEMATICALLY REDUNDANT and this is pinned, not glossed: ..._pin_hypothesis_redundant proves the SAME biconditional at N = 0 at k = 0, k = -4 (where 4 divides k HOLDS and the biconditional survives only because the second conjunct fails) and k = 5. Unlike in SDF-10 and SDF-11, hN IS syntactically used here (it is passed to those two lemmas, which ignore it in turn), so no linter suppression is needed. It is kept for shape-uniformity with SDF-10, SDF-11 and SDF-13. OUT-OF-LEAN CHECK, recorded as evidence about the STATEMENT rather than as a proof: before proving, the biconditional was checked in exact rational arithmetic (fractions.Fraction, no floating point) at all 12221 instances N in [0,100], k in [-60,60], with the N = 0 row under Lean's conventions (0 : Real)^k = 0 for k != 0 and sqrt 0 = 0. Zero mismatches. COMPARATOR: NO_REFERENCE, and the comparator question was mis-aimed rather than the node. Like SDF-07 .. SDF-11 this is a fact about a SCALAR -- no exponent vector r, no point z, no eta quotient, no IsFrickeSelfDual hypothesis -- and it is NOT a specialisation of etaQuotient_fricke; that specialisation is SDF-04/SDF-05. No substitution into etaQuotient_fricke produces a divisibility condition or a biconditional. RECONSTRUCTION CAVEAT DISCHARGED: this declaration's statement was originally reconstructed by a run whose specification had been TRUNCATED mid-node at the string 'theorem frickeEigenvalue_'. The orchestrating session has since supplied SDF-12 in full and the supplied text agrees with the declaration CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER, hN included, so the reconstruction is CONFIRMED and this node may be reported as a specified node. Its sibling SDF-13 (frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff) has NOT been confirmed, remains a reconstruction and remains OPEN. NUMBERING NOTE (unchanged): this node was previously labelled SDF-11; the real SDF-11 is frickeEigenvalue_norm, a different theorem, and this node and its sibling were shifted by one in the commit that closed it. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. This node says when a complex number attached to a level and a weight equals 1. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-DEF-02 (frickeEigenvalue)", "SDF-08 (I_zpow_neg_eq_one_iff)", "SDF-10 (natCast_zpow_eq_one_iff)", "SDF-11 (frickeEigenvalue_norm)", "Real.sqrt_eq_one", "norm_one", "Complex.ofReal_one"], "difficulty": "moderate", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf12 (#print axioms frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff and 9 supporting declarations: six instance pins, two negative controls, the hypothesis-redundancy pin and the application check). All footprints [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; every decide is decide, never native_decide."}
{"id": "SDF-13", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-02", "SDF-09", "SDF-10", "SDF-11"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free, guarded, and the STATEMENT IS NOW CONFIRMED -- the orchestrating session supplied SDF-13 in full and the supplied text agrees CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER, hN included, with the declaration this file had carried as a reconstruction since the truncated-specification run; the reconstruction caveat that this field used to carry is DISCHARGED. frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff : for 0 < N and k : Int, frickeEigenvalue N k = -1 if and only if (k % 4 = 2 AND N = 1), with % being Int.emod. The unnormalised Fricke eigenvalue is -1 exactly when the root of unity i^(-k) is -1 (SDF-09) and the modulus sqrt((N:Real)^k) is 1 (SDF-11 + Real.sqrt_eq_one + SDF-10). WHY THE RIGHT-HAND SIDE IS NOT SDF-12's WITH 1 REPLACED BY -1: k % 4 = 2 already forces k != 0, so SDF-10's k = 0 disjunct cannot fire and the level condition SHARPENS to N = 1. That sharpening is machine-checked by frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_asymmetry, which proves the SDF-12-shaped right-hand side (k % 4 = 2 AND (N = 1 OR k = 0)) equivalent to the one used here for every N and k, and exhibits (N,k) = (6,0) where SDF-12's right-hand side is TRUE and this one's is FALSE -- so the two nodes are genuinely different statements. PROOF ACTUALLY USED (verified this run, four steps, no case split on N and only SDF-10's two-way split on k): (1) forward, from lambda = -1 take moduli -- norm_neg then norm_one give ||lambda|| = 1, and SDF-11 (frickeEigenvalue_norm) gives sqrt((N:Real)^k) = 1; (2) Real.sqrt_eq_one (UNCONDITIONAL, Mathlib Analysis/Real/Sqrt.lean:172, no sign hypothesis) gives (N:Real)^k = 1; (3) substituting sqrt(...) = 1 back into SDF-DEF-02 leaves i^(-k) = -1, and SDF-09 (I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff) gives k % 4 = 2; (4) SDF-10 (natCast_zpow_eq_one_iff) turns (N:Real)^k = 1 into N = 1 OR k = 0 and the k = 0 disjunct is KILLED by omega against k % 4 = 2 (0 % 4 = 0 != 2) -- that last step is the ONLY structural difference from SDF-12's proof. Backward: SDF-09.mpr and SDF-10.mpr (feeding N = 1 through Or.inl), then Real.sqrt_one. BUILD-HINT CORRECTION: built_from named Real.sq_sqrt; the proof uses Real.sqrt_eq_one instead, which needs no 0 <= (N:Real)^k side goal and no zpow_pos detour. A build hint, not a statement difference; built_from below is corrected to match what was actually used. hN : 0 < N IS MATHEMATICALLY REDUNDANT but IS syntactically used (it is passed to SDF-10 and SDF-11, which ignore it in turn, so no linter suppression is needed); frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_hypothesis_redundant proves the same biconditional at N = 0 at three weights, including k = 2 where the residue clause HOLDS and the biconditional survives only because the level clause fails. It is kept for shape-parity with SDF-10, SDF-11 and SDF-12. DECIDE-PINS FIRST, all stated ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them from using it, and all proved before it: three new VALUE pins (I_zpow_two; frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_six_weight_two, lambda = -6 at (6,2); frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_one_weight_neg_two, lambda = -1 at (1,-2)); eight instance pins -- (1,12) the eta_S_via_fricke case, both sides FALSE with the LEVEL clause TRUE; (6,12) the genuine N>1 self-dual rPinSix = (1,11,11,1), both FALSE; (6,0) the degenerate r == 0 case, both FALSE, and FALSE exactly where SDF-12's pin at the same (N,k) is TRUE; (2,1) odd weight, lambda = -(i*sqrt 2), refuted through its modulus; (1,2) the LOAD-BEARING pin, BOTH SIDES TRUE; (6,-12) negative weight; (6,2) THE LEVEL CONTROL, the pin SDF-12 has no analogue of -- 2 % 4 = 2 HOLDS so the root of unity IS -1, yet lambda = -6, the only pin where the two conjuncts disagree; (1,-2) BOTH SIDES TRUE at a negative weight, the emod pin. Three negative controls: ..._pin_not_level_only ((1,12), refutes the weakened lambda = -1 <-> N = 1), ..._pin_not_emod_only ((6,2), refutes the weakened lambda = -1 <-> k % 4 = 2), and ..._pin_emod_not_tmod (records (-2) % 4 = 2 beside Int.tmod (-2) 4 = -2 TOGETHER WITH lambda = -1 at (1,-2), so the emod convention is a checked fact of THIS node, not an assumption inherited from SDF-09; under tmod SDF-13 would be FALSE at every weight in {..., -10, -6, -2}). No pin failed. OUT-OF-LEAN CHECK re-run this session, recorded as evidence about the STATEMENT and not as a proof: exact arithmetic (fractions.Fraction for N^k, Gaussian units for i^(-k), no floating point) at all 40501 instances N in [0,100], k in [-200,200], with the N = 0 row under Lean's conventions (0:Real)^k = 0 for k != 0 and sqrt 0 = 0. Zero mismatches, and every instance at which the eigenvalue IS -1 had N = 1. NORMALISATION CAVEAT, which any prose report of this node MUST carry: frickeEigenvalue is the UNNORMALISED constant of f(-1/(Nz)) = lambda * z^k * f(z) and carries N^(k/2). 'Eigenvalue -1 forces N = 1' is a statement about THAT convention and does NOT contradict the classical fact (Martin 1996, multiplicative eta-quotients) that multiplicative eta quotients of level N > 1 have Fricke eigenvalue +-1 -- the classical eigenvalue is the NORMALISED one, here i^(-k) (SDF-06, etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized), whose N-dependence has already cancelled by SDF-02. frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_level_six_weight_two is the machine-checked instance where the two differ: at (6,2) the normalised eigenvalue is -1 and the unnormalised one is -6. Stating SDF-13 in a paper without naming the normalisation would read as a false claim. COMPARATOR: NO_REFERENCE, and correctly so -- the comparator was pointed at etaQuotient_fricke, which contains an etaQuotient, an exponent vector r, a point z and an IsFrickeSelfDual hypothesis, none of which occur in this node; substituting a self-dual r into it produces SDF-04/SDF-05's eigenform equation, never a +-1 criterion. Same situation already recorded for SDF-10, SDF-11 and SDF-12. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node, or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean, formalises any physics. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement here and must never be reported as one. NUMBERING: this node was labelled SDF-12 by the truncated-specification run that created it; it was renumbered when the real SDF-11 (frickeEigenvalue_norm) was supplied. Documents predating that commit use the old numbering. FILE STATUS: closing this node makes EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean sorry-free in full; SDF-13 was its last open node and its last unconfirmed reconstructed statement.", "built_from": ["SDF-DEF-02 (frickeEigenvalue)", "SDF-09 (I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff)", "SDF-10 (natCast_zpow_eq_one_iff)", "SDF-11 (frickeEigenvalue_norm)", "Real.sqrt_eq_one (NOT Real.sq_sqrt: see statement_nl)", "norm_neg", "norm_one", "omega"], "difficulty": "moderate", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf13 (#print axioms frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff and 17 supporting declarations: three value pins (I_zpow_two, frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_six_weight_two, frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_one_weight_neg_two), eight instance pins, three negative controls, the asymmetry pin, the hypothesis-redundancy pin and the application check). All 18 footprints are [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] except frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_asymmetry, which is [propext, Quot.sound] with NO Classical.choice (pure omega and constructor logic) and whose guard records that smaller footprint. No sorryAx and no Lean.ofReduceBool anywhere: every decide is decide, never native_decide."}
{"id": "SDF-14", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeEigenvalue_pm_one_iff", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-02", "SDF-12", "SDF-13"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free, guarded. frickeEigenvalue_pm_one_iff : for 0 < N, any r : EtaExp and k : Int with sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2k, (frickeEigenvalue N k = 1 OR frickeEigenvalue N k = -1) if and only if (4 divides sum_{delta | N} r delta AND (N = 1 OR sum_{delta | N} r delta = 0)). WHAT THIS NODE IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT -- any prose report MUST carry this. It is the DISJUNCTION of SDF-12 and SDF-13 with the weight k traded for the weight SUM sum r delta using the hypothesis hk. It is NOT new mathematical content, and it is NOT a statement about eta quotients: no etaQuotient, no point z, no dual exponent vector and no IsFrickeSelfDual hypothesis occurs in it, and r enters ONLY through hk -- the conclusion constrains the scalar frickeEigenvalue N k and the integer sum r delta, nothing else. It is NOT a specialisation of etaQuotient_fricke; that specialisation is SDF-04 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw). WHY IT IS WORTH STATING: the weight SUM is what a concrete exponent vector presents to decide, whereas k exists only as the witness of hk, so this is the form of the +-1 criterion that applies to a concrete eta quotient without first solving for k -- every pin below is exactly that use. THE ONE STEP THAT IS NOT MECHANICAL: 4 | sum r delta is 4 | 2k, which does NOT give 4 | k (k = 2: 4 | 4 but 4 does not divide 2), so the backward direction CANNOT route to SDF-12 alone; it case-splits k % 4 in {0, 2} and sends residue 0 to SDF-12 and residue 2 to SDF-13. PROOF ACTUALLY USED (verified this run, three steps): (1) rw [frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff hN k, frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff hN k, hk] replaces both complex equations by their arithmetic criteria and the sum by 2*k; (2) forward, rintro on the three shapes and omega for each divisibility/residue step; (3) backward, subst on N = 1 then rcases (by omega : 4 | k OR k % 4 = 2), routing the two residues to the two disjuncts, and in the sum = 0 branch omega gives k = 0. No new Mathlib lemma. hN : 0 < N is needed only because SDF-12 and SDF-13 each take it (and each passes it to SDF-10/SDF-11, which ignore it in turn). DECIDE-PINS FIRST, all stated ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them from using it, and all proved before it, each on a CONCRETE exponent vector with its weight witness exhibited rather than assumed: PIN A (N=1, rPinOne = (24), k=12) the eta_S_via_fricke / Delta = eta^24 case, BOTH SIDES TRUE via the 4 | sum + N = 1 route; PIN B (N=6, rPinSix = (1,11,11,1), k=12) a genuine N>1 Fricke-self-dual non-constant vector with the SAME weight sum 24 as PIN A and the OPPOSITE verdict, BOTH SIDES FALSE -- the LOAD-BEARING pin, and what forces the (N = 1 OR sum = 0) conjunct to exist; PIN C (N=6, r == 0, k=0) the DEGENERATE case, BOTH SIDES TRUE, and the only pin at which the right-hand side holds with N > 1, so it is what makes the sum = 0 disjunct non-vacuous; PIN D (N=1, rPinFour = (4) i.e. eta^4, k=2) THE TRAP -- 4 | 4 holds for the SUM while 4 | 2 FAILS for the WEIGHT, and the eigenvalue is -1, not 1, so a backward direction routed to SDF-12 alone is REFUTED at this instance; PIN E (N=2, rPinTwo = (1,1) i.e. eta(z)eta(2z), k=1) odd weight, BOTH SIDES FALSE and the only pin failing on the DIVISIBILITY conjunct, refuted on the left through SDF-11's modulus sqrt 2 != 1 rather than through the value pin; PIN F (N=6, rPinLevelSixNeg = (-1,-11,-11,-1), k=-12) negative weight sum, BOTH SIDES FALSE, where a proof assuming 0 <= sum r delta would break; PIN G (N=1, rPinNegFour = (-4), k=-2, a NEW exponent vector added by this node with weight witness rPinNegFour_weight) BOTH SIDES TRUE at a negative weight, and it pins (-2) % 4 = 2 beside Int.tmod (-2) 4 = -2, so the Int.emod convention SDF-13 needs is a checked fact at this node too, on a concrete exponent vector. No pin failed. Application check frickeEigenvalue_pm_one_iff_pin_application re-derives six of the seven instances BY RUNNING the general lemma with that pin's weight witness as hk, so each is settled twice by routes sharing no lemma below SDF-DEF-02, and they agree. OUT-OF-LEAN CHECK re-run this session, recorded as evidence about the STATEMENT and not as a proof: exhaustive integer comparison of this node's right-hand side against SDF-12 OR SDF-13 under the substitution sum = 2k, over N in [1,59] and k in [-100,100] (11940 instances), zero mismatches; Python's % agrees with Int.emod for the positive divisor 4, which is the convention already pinned in-tree by frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_emod_not_tmod and re-pinned here by PIN G. NORMALISATION CAVEAT, inherited from SDF-12 and SDF-13 and mandatory in any prose report: frickeEigenvalue is the UNNORMALISED constant of f(-1/(Nz)) = lambda * z^k * f(z) and carries N^(k/2). 'lambda = +-1 forces N = 1 or sum r delta = 0' is a statement about THAT convention and does NOT contradict the classical fact (Martin 1996, multiplicative eta-quotients) that multiplicative eta quotients of level N > 1 have Fricke eigenvalue +-1 -- the classical eigenvalue is the NORMALISED one, here i^(-k) (SDF-06), whose N-dependence has already cancelled by SDF-02. frickeEigenvalue_pm_one_iff_pin_level_six is the pin where the two readings visibly differ. COMPARATOR: NO_REFERENCE, and correctly so -- the comparator was pointed at etaQuotient_fricke, and the question it was given ('does substituting r delta = r(N/delta) into its RHS mechanically produce this node's equation?') has the answer no, because the node states no equation about eta quotients at all; that substitution produces SDF-04. Same disposition already recorded for SDF-09, SDF-10, SDF-12 and SDF-13. The node's real references are its declared dependencies SDF-12 and SDF-13, and the statement was verified against those before being proved. NAMING: the condition r delta = r (N / delta) is called SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric) throughout, never 'balanced' -- 'balanced' is already taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add, and it is also Persson-Volpato's word for the self-duality condition, a genuine collision of one word on two unrelated concepts. This node's statement mentions no self-duality condition at all. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node formalises any physics. It relates a complex number attached to a level and a weight to a divisor-sum condition over Z. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the module docstring as the ORIGIN of the question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement anywhere in this library and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-12 (frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff)", "SDF-13 (frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff)", "SDF-DEF-02 (frickeEigenvalue)", "omega", "SDF-11 (frickeEigenvalue_norm) -- PIN E only, not the general lemma"], "difficulty": "easy", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf14 (#print axioms frickeEigenvalue_pm_one_iff and 9 supporting declarations: the weight witness rPinNegFour_weight for the one new exponent vector, the seven instance pins frickeEigenvalue_pm_one_iff_pin_level_one / _pin_level_six / _pin_zero_exp / _pin_neg_one_branch / _pin_level_two_weight_one / _pin_level_six_neg / _pin_emod_not_tmod, and the application check _pin_application). All 10 footprints are [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; no sorryAx and no Lean.ofReduceBool -- every decide is decide, never native_decide. The guard section's prose says explicitly that it must NOT be read as guarding a specialisation of etaQuotient_fricke (that is SDF-04, section Sdf04)."}
{"id": "SDF-15", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.I_zpow_neg_pm_one_iff", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-08", "SDF-09"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free, guarded. I_zpow_neg_pm_one_iff (k : Int) : ((Complex.I) ^ (-k) = 1 OR (Complex.I) ^ (-k) = -1) <-> Even k. The NORMALISED plus/minus-one criterion: the DISJUNCTION of SDF-08 (i^{-k} = 1 <-> 4 | k) and SDF-09 (i^{-k} = -1 <-> k % 4 = 2), whose union of residue classes mod 4 is {0, 2}, i.e. exactly the even k. WHAT THIS NODE IS NOT -- any prose report MUST carry all of this. (a) It is a fact about C and Z ALONE: no level N, no exponent vector r : EtaExp, no N.divisors, no z, no upper half plane, no etaQuotient, no IsFrickeSelfDual hypothesis and no hk : sum_{delta|N} r delta = 2k occurs in it. It is NOT a specialisation of etaQuotient_fricke -- that specialisation is SDF-04. The statement comparator for this node was pointed at etaQuotient_fricke and correctly returned NO_REFERENCE for exactly that reason, the same disposition already recorded for SDF-07 ... SDF-14; the node's real references are SDF-08, SDF-09 and, for the eigenvalue reading, SDF-06. (b) The identification of i^{-k} with 'the Fricke eigenvalue of a self-dual eta quotient of weight k' is SDF-06 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized), not this node; the sentence 'the Fricke eigenvalue is plus/minus 1 iff the weight is even' is SDF-15 COMPOSED WITH SDF-06 and both must be cited. (c) NORMALISATION CAVEAT, mandatory: i^{-k} is the NORMALISED eigenvalue (SDF-06 has already divided out sqrt(N^k) and z^k). That sentence is TRUE of i^{-k} and FALSE of frickeEigenvalue, the UNNORMALISED constant carrying N^{k/2}, for which plus/minus 1 is SDF-14's far tighter condition requiring N = 1 or sum r delta = 0; frickeEigenvalue_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_level_six_weight_two is the instance where the two conventions differ (normalised -1, unnormalised -6). This node may be quoted in preference to SDF-14 only with the normalisation named in the same sentence. (d) The re-parametrisation 'Even k <-> 4 | sum_{delta|N} r delta' is NOT this node and does not follow from it: it needs hk : sum r delta = 2k, which SDF-15 does not carry, and would be a separate node exactly as SDF-14 was for SDF-12/SDF-13. PROOF: rewrite by SDF-08, SDF-09 and Int.even_iff, leaving (4 | k OR k % 4 = 2) <-> k % 2 = 0, which is inside omega's fragment. The four-case residue analysis is NOT repeated -- it is already carried once each by SDF-08 and SDF-09, including the Int.emod vs Int.tmod hazard pinned by I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff_pin_emod_not_tmod. DEPENDENCY RECEIPT: an earlier draft of this node listed depends_on [SDF-07]; that understated it (routing through SDF-07 directly would duplicate that analysis) and was re-pointed at [SDF-08, SDF-09] before proving. SIX WEIGHT PINS, all stated and proved ABOVE the general lemma so Lean scoping forbids them using it: _pin_twelve (k=12, value 1 via I_zpow_neg_twelve -- the N=1 r=(24) Delta = eta^24 weight behind the sorry-free eta_S_via_fricke, and the weight of the genuine N=6 self-dual vector rPinSix=(1,11,11,1)), _pin_neg_twelve (k=-12, value 1 via I_zpow_twelve after neg_neg -- a proof assuming 0 <= k breaks here), _pin_zero (k=0, DEGENERATE and recorded as such, the r == 0 case), _pin_two (k=2, THE LOAD-BEARING PIN: value -1, so the left-hand side holds through its SECOND disjunct only, and i^{-2} != 1 is recorded separately -- this is the weight of selfDual_pin_eigenvalue_neg_one, eta^4 at level one, eigenvalue -1, so a version of this node with i^{-k} = 1 alone on the left is refuted here), _pin_fifteen (k=15, ODD, value i via I_zpow_emod_pin_neg_fifteen, refuting BOTH 1 and -1), _pin_one (k=1, the OTHER odd residue class, value -i via I_zpow_neg_one). The two odd pins are what no plus/minus-1 coincidence can fake; one refutation compares imaginary parts and one real parts. TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS: _pin_neither_disjunct_alone (at k=2 the weight is even but i^{-2} != 1; at k=12 the weight is even but i^{-12} != -1, so SDF-15 is a restatement of NEITHER SDF-08 NOR SDF-09) and _pin_even_strictly_between (2 is even but 4 does not divide 2; 12 is even but 12 % 4 != 2 -- the same fact on the Z side by decide). Plus I_zpow_neg_pm_one_iff_even_neg (Even (-k) <-> Even k), which records that the k/-k hazard of SDF-09 -- where k % 4 and (-k) % 4 are DIFFERENT functions -- does not arise for parity, and the application check _pin_application, which re-derives all six pins by RUNNING the general lemma at those weights, so every pinned weight is settled twice by routes that share no lemma below SDF-07. NOT ALREADY IN MATHLIB, re-verified this session by whole-library grep with no truncation: Mathlib has only the NATURAL-exponent periodicity Complex.I_pow_eq_pow_mod (Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.lean:633); a grep for any Even/iff form of I_pow or I_zpow returns nothing, and zpow_eq_one_iff_of_ne_zero (Mathlib/Algebra/Order/Field/Power.lean:87), the only zpow/Even biconditional in Mathlib, is stated for a LinearOrderedField and does not apply to C. Nor is the name present anywhere in this library (grep for I_zpow_neg_pm_one_iff over Lean/, verification/ and dag/ returns nothing before this run). OUTSIDE LEAN, BEFORE ANY OF THIS WAS STATED: i^{-k} in {1,-1} <-> k even was checked in exact Gaussian-integer arithmetic at all 601 weights k in [-300, 300]; zero mismatches. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing here formalises any physics. This node relates an integer power of i to the parity of an integer. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the guarded file's header as the ORIGIN of the self-duality question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement anywhere in this library and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-08 (I_zpow_neg_eq_one_iff)", "SDF-09 (I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff)", "Int.even_iff", "omega", "SDF-07 (I_zpow_emod) -- only transitively, through SDF-08 and SDF-09", "Complex.I_sq / Complex.ext_iff -- pins only, not the general lemma"], "difficulty": "easy", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf15 (#print axioms I_zpow_neg_pm_one_iff and 9 supporting declarations: the six weight pins I_zpow_neg_pm_one_iff_pin_twelve / _pin_neg_twelve / _pin_zero / _pin_two / _pin_fifteen / _pin_one, the two negative controls _pin_neither_disjunct_alone and _pin_even_strictly_between, the negation-invariance lemma I_zpow_neg_pm_one_iff_even_neg, and the application check _pin_application). All 11 footprints are [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; no sorryAx and no Lean.ofReduceBool -- every decide is decide, never native_decide. The guard section's prose says explicitly that it must NOT be read as guarding a specialisation of etaQuotient_fricke (that is SDF-04, section Sdf04), and carries the normalisation caveat."}
{"id": "SDF-16", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.decidableIsFrickeSelfDual", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-01"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free, guarded. instance decidableIsFrickeSelfDual (N : Nat) (r : EtaExp) : Decidable (IsFrickeSelfDual N r) := inferInstanceAs (Decidable (forall delta in N.divisors, r delta = r (N / delta))). The Decidable instance for SDF-DEF-01's predicate, obtained by inferInstanceAs at the bounded quantifier the def unfolds to, where Mathlib's Finset.decidableBAll already applies (EtaExp = Nat -> Int, DecidableEq Int). WHAT THIS NODE IS: ERGONOMICS, and it must be reported as nothing more -- with the instance in scope, bare `decide` closes a self-duality goal without the leading `unfold IsFrickeSelfDual`. Net content: one declaration, ~3 lines, mechanical, zero proof risk. WHAT IT IS NOT -- TWO OVERCLAIMS CAUGHT BY THIS RUN'S STATEMENT COMPARATOR, recorded here, in the node's Lean docstring and in the FinalCheck guard section so they cannot re-enter any prose report. (i) It is NOT what lets the pins of EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean discharge their self-duality hypotheses by decide: every selfDual_cond_pin_* (lines 807-809, 819-821, 844-846, 851-853, 865-867, 1002-1004 before this run's insertion) discharges by `unfold IsFrickeSelfDual; decide`, needs NO instance, and was sorry-free before this node existed. Nothing above the node's own section depends on it, deliberately, so the file acquires no dependency on an ergonomics node. (ii) It is NOT what makes the self-duality hypothesis non-vacuous: non-vacuity was already machine-checked by not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric (r = (2,0) at N = 2, the fricke_dual_pin vector) and, more sharply, by not_selfDual_pin_mispaired (r = (1,11,1,11) at N = 6, SAME weight sum 24, invariant under the WRONG involution 1 <-> 3, 2 <-> 6), both sorry-free, both guarded in FinalCheck section SdfDef01, both independent of this instance. The node's originally proposed inline negative control `example : not IsFrickeSelfDual 2 (fun d => if d = 1 then 2 else 0)` is a VERBATIM DUPLICATE of not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric (rPinAsym is that exact function, defined at line 752) and was therefore NOT restated; the sharper mispairing vector is used for this node's negative-side pin instead, and not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric is REUSED (not re-decided) as the second conjunct of the N = 0 trap. IT IS STILL A GENUINE DELTA, verified this run, not assumed: with the instance removed, `IsFrickeSelfDual 6 rPinSix := by decide`, `not IsFrickeSelfDual 2 rPinAsym := by decide` and `decide (IsFrickeSelfDual 6 rPinSix) = true := rfl` fail with exactly three `failed to synthesize Decidable (IsFrickeSelfDual ...)` errors and no other cause (scratch_sdf16/Sdf16BaseB.lean, EXIT nonzero, 3 error lines). THE ONLY FAILURE MODE, AND THE PIN THAT COVERS IT. A Decidable instance is proof-carrying, so it CANNOT disagree with the proposition it decides (decide_eq_true_iff is a theorem) -- this node cannot be wrong about which exponent vectors are self-dual. What it CAN be is INERT: an instance that elaborates but does not reduce in the kernel (Classical.dec (IsFrickeSelfDual N r) typechecks against the same statement and computes nothing), or one routed through native_decide (which would put Lean.ofReduceBool in the footprint). decidableIsFrickeSelfDual_pin_bool_values refutes both: it asserts the Bool value of decide (IsFrickeSelfDual N r) at four TRUE and two FALSE concrete instances BY rfl, i.e. by kernel reduction of the instance term, forcing evaluation of Nat.divisors N and of the exponent vector at every divisor. decide throughout, never native_decide; no Lean.ofReduceBool in any footprint. PINS, all sorry-free, all stated AFTER the instance because they consume it (there is no way to pin an instance before declaring it), and all with their verdicts computed OUTSIDE Lean first this session in exact integer arithmetic (divisors 1 = [1], divisors 2 = [1,2], divisors 4 = [1,2,4], divisors 6 = [1,2,3,6], each vector printed beside its dual) and only then asserted; none was adjusted to match a proof and none disagreed. The three regimes this run's discipline requires are the first three: PIN A decidableIsFrickeSelfDual_pin_level_one (N=1, rPinOne=(24), k=12 -- the instance underlying the already sorry-free eta_S_via_fricke, EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246; DEGENERATE as evidence about self-duality, since at N=1 every r is self-dual, and recorded as such); PIN B decidableIsFrickeSelfDual_pin_level_six (N=6, rPinSix=(1,11,11,1), dual (1,11,11,1), sum 24 = 2*12 -- THE LOAD-BEARING PIN, the only positive one with N>1 AND a non-constant vector, hence the only one a wrong delta <-> N/delta pairing could fail); PIN C decidableIsFrickeSelfDual_pin_zero_exp (N=6, r == 0 -- DEGENERATE, a floor certifying the predicate is not empty; note the contrast with selfDual_cond_pin_zero_exp, which proves the same proposition by `fun _ _ => rfl` and depends on no axioms, whereas this route makes the kernel actually evaluate divisors 6). PIN D decidableIsFrickeSelfDual_pin_level_four_neg (N=4, rPinLevelFourNeg=(-2,6,-2), sum 2 = 2*1) adds the only vector with NEGATIVE entries and the only N>1 level with a self-paired divisor (4/2 = 2). NEGATIVE-SIDE PIN decidableIsFrickeSelfDual_pin_mispaired (not IsFrickeSelfDual 6 rPinSixMispaired, by bare decide) shows the instance produces isFalse and not merely isTrue. REDUCTION PIN decidableIsFrickeSelfDual_pin_bool_values, described above -- the only pin here a wrong instance could fail. N=0 TRAP decidableIsFrickeSelfDual_pin_level_zero_vacuous: IsFrickeSelfDual 0 rPinAsym AND not IsFrickeSelfDual 2 rPinAsym, both at the SAME vector. Nat.divisors 0 = empty, so IsFrickeSelfDual 0 r is VACUOUSLY TRUE for every r; this is why every SDF-* lemma carries hN : 0 < N, and it is a hazard SPECIFIC to the decidable reading, because `by decide` will close IsFrickeSelfDual 0 r for any concrete r, so a future pin that dropped its positivity hypothesis would pass. Recorded as a trap, not as evidence for anything. AXIOM FOOTPRINTS, read off this run: the instance and all seven pins are [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -- identical to every pre-existing SDF pin, so this node changes no existing FinalCheck guard. No sorryAx, no Lean.ofReduceBool. MUST-FAIL CONTROL: verification/Sdf16PinNegControl.lean, run this session, exits nonzero with nine error lines from six deliberately wrong numbered items (wrong axiom footprint; the mispairing asserted positively through the instance; the Bool values of PIN B, of the mispairing row and of the negative-entry row all inverted; and the N=0 vacuity negated). Items 3-5 each produce two error lines (a 'Not a definitional equality' plus a type mismatch on the same rfl). COMPARATOR: NO_REFERENCE, and correctly so -- the comparator was pointed at etaQuotient_fricke, and a Decidable instance for an arithmetic predicate is not a specialisation of that transformation law. Same disposition already recorded for SDF-07 ... SDF-15. The comparator's substantive findings (the two overclaims and the duplicated negative control) were ACTED ON rather than filed: the statement was restated as ergonomics, the duplicate example was dropped in favour of citing not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric, and the sharper mispairing control took its place. NAMING: the condition r delta = r (N/delta) is called SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric) throughout, never 'balanced' -- that word is already taken in EtaQuotientModularity.lean by the unrelated Int.bmod lemma exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), and it is also Persson-Volpato's term for this same condition, so it collides twice. No declaration in this node uses it. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing in this node formalises any physics. It states that a decidable arithmetic condition on a function Nat -> Int over a finite set of divisors is decidable. Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited in the guarded file's header as the ORIGIN of the self-duality question only, at the literature (L) tier; their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is NOT a Lean statement anywhere in this library and must never be reported as one.", "built_from": ["SDF-DEF-01 (IsFrickeSelfDual)", "Finset.decidableBAll (Mathlib)", "inferInstanceAs", "rPinOne / rPinSix / rPinLevelFourNeg / rPinSixMispaired / rPinAsym (existing pin vectors)", "not_selfDual_pin_asymmetric (REUSED as the second conjunct of the N=0 trap, not re-decided)", "fricke_dual_pin (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2302) -- the source of rPinAsym, cited not restated", "decide (kernel evaluation of Nat.divisors; native_decide deliberately NOT used)"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf16 (#print axioms decidableIsFrickeSelfDual and its seven pins: _pin_level_one, _pin_level_six, _pin_zero_exp, _pin_level_four_neg, _pin_mispaired, _pin_bool_values, _pin_level_zero_vacuous). All 8 footprints are [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; no sorryAx and no Lean.ofReduceBool -- every decide is decide, never native_decide. The guard section's prose says explicitly that the node is ERGONOMICS ONLY, that it is NOT what lets the SdfDef01 pins work and NOT what makes the self-duality hypothesis non-vacuous, and that _pin_bool_values is the only pin a wrong instance could fail. Must-fail control: verification/Sdf16PinNegControl.lean."}
{"id": "SDF-PIN-01", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.selfDual_raw_pin_level_one_is_eta_S", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-01", "SDF-01", "F32-A7"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (run 12). Lean statement, verbatim from the source type checked this run: theorem selfDual_raw_pin_level_one_is_eta_S {z : C} (hz : z in Hopen) : ModularForm.eta (-(1 / z)) ^ (24 : Nat) = z ^ (12 : Nat) * ModularForm.eta z ^ (24 : Nat). THE LEVEL-ONE INSTANCE PIN of the self-dual Fricke arc: the (N, r, k) = (1, r == 24, 12) instance of SDF-04 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw's equation, taken through SDF-04's own PIN A selfDual_raw_pin_level_one), with its constant evaluated -- divisors 1 = {1}, prod delta^{r delta} = 1^24 = 1, sqrt 1 = 1, N^k = 1^12 = 1, i^{-12} = 1 -- leaving the S-transformation law of the discriminant. WHAT THIS PIN IS: a FLOOR, i.e. SECOND-ROUTE AGREEMENT. The same conclusion is already sorry-free upstream twice over, as eta_S_via_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246) and, in the example beside it, from Mathlib's discriminant_S_invariant (Mathlib/NumberTheory/ModularForms/Discriminant.lean:143, a bare lemma, not @[simp]). This node certifies that the two NEW definitions of the self-dual module (IsFrickeSelfDual, and SDF-01's congruence collapse) reproduce that already-established value by a THIRD, independent route. Independence is machine-checked this run, not argued from the tactic script: walking the kernel proof term of selfDual_raw_pin_level_one_is_eta_S transitively reaches etaQuotient_fricke, etaQuotient_congr_divisors, selfDual_cond_pin_level_one, rPinOne_weight and IsFrickeSelfDual, and reaches NEITHER eta_S_via_fricke NOR discriminant_S_invariant (scratch_sdfpin01/DepWalk4.lean, run this session). WHAT THIS PIN IS NOT -- READ BEFORE CITING IT AS EVIDENCE. It pins NO component of the Fricke constant lambda = i^{-k} * N^k * s^{-1/2}. An earlier version of this text (and of three docstrings, all corrected in the same commit) claimed that a wrong sign on i^{-k}, a wrong power of N, or sqrt(s) on the wrong side of the fraction would break the agreement here. THAT CLAIM IS FALSE and is now REFUTED IN LEAN, not merely withdrawn: at N = 1, k = 12, i^{-12} = i^{+12} (selfDual_pin_level_one_no_evidence_I_sign), every zpow of (1 : C) is 1 so N^k, N^{2k} and N^{-k} agree (selfDual_pin_level_one_no_evidence_level_pow), s = 1 so (sqrt s)^{-1} = sqrt s (selfDual_pin_level_one_no_evidence_radicand), and delta |-> 1/delta is the IDENTITY on divisors 1 so a transposed pairing is invisible (selfDual_pin_level_one_no_evidence_involution). All four are sorry-free and guarded in FinalCheck section SdfPin01. WHERE THE DISCRIMINATION ACTUALLY LIVES, also machine-checked: three of the four degeneracies fail at N = 6 (selfDual_pin_level_six_evidence_contrast), which is why selfDual_raw_pin_level_six, prod_zpow_pin_mispaired_ne and not_selfDual_pin_mispaired are the load-bearing pins of this arc; the fourth fails only at ODD weight (selfDual_pin_weight_one_evidence_I_sign) -- raising the LEVEL does not fix it, since i^{-k} = i^{k} for every even k, k = 12 included. NAME DRIFT, RESOLVED: this node does NOT resolve to a theorem called selfDual_pin_level_one. That name is taken (EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean:908) by a DIFFERENT and stronger five-way conjunction (IsFrickeSelfDual 1 rPinOne AND sum r = 2*12 AND prod delta^{r delta} = 1 AND = 1^12 AND frickeEigenvalue 1 12 = 1), which mentions neither eta nor z; a base-name-matched FinalCheck guard against that name would have guarded the wrong proposition. The equation this node states is proved by selfDual_raw_pin_level_one_is_eta_S, and that is the lean_name filed here. The :908 conjunction is sorry-free and separately guarded (FinalCheck.lean:6103) but carries NO DAG node -- if one is wanted it must be a new id with its own statement, not this one. NUMERICS, re-run this session at 30 dps: eta(-1/z)^24 vs z^12 eta(z)^24 at z = 0.3+1.1i, -0.7+0.45i, 2.3i, 0.1+0.05i gives relative error <= 1.3e-29. SCOPE: pure eta-quotient / Fricke content. No physics is formalised here or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean. NAMING: 'self-dual' / 'Fricke-symmetric' for r delta = r(N/delta), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is taken by the unrelated exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1) and is also Persson-Volpato's term for this same condition, so it collides twice.", "built_from": ["SDF-04 PIN A selfDual_raw_pin_level_one (the equation at (N, r, k) = (1, r==24, 12))", "F32-A7 etaQuotient_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2212) -- reached transitively", "SDF-01 etaQuotient_congr_divisors -- reached transitively", "SDF-DEF-01 IsFrickeSelfDual, via selfDual_cond_pin_level_one", "rPinOne / rPinOne_weight (the level-one exponent vector and its weight witness)", "NOT USED, checked by kernel-term walk: eta_S_via_fricke, ModularForm.discriminant_S_invariant, SDF-05 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual, SDF-DEF-02 frickeEigenvalue, SDF-12 frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff, SDF-04 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw. The node's originally proposed built_from list (SDF-05, SDF-12, eta_S_via_fricke, discriminant_S_invariant) was wrong on all four counts."], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section Sdf04 (#print axioms selfDual_raw_pin_level_one_is_eta_S, FinalCheck.lean:5968) for the node's own theorem, plus section SdfPin01 (#print axioms on the four selfDual_pin_level_one_no_evidence_* degeneracy witnesses and the two ..._evidence_* contrast checks). All seven footprints are [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; no sorryAx. Must-fail control: verification/SdfPin01NegControl.lean (exits 1, eight error lines, one per item; item 8 is the NAME-DRIFT control, a type mismatch from trying to close this node's equation with selfDual_pin_level_one)."}
{"id": "SDF-PIN-02", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-01", "SDF-DEF-02", "SDF-01", "SDF-02", "SDF-03", "SDF-04", "F32-A7"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run). Lean statement, verbatim from the source type checked this run: theorem selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta {z : C} (hz : z in Hopen) : ModularForm.eta (-(1 / ((2 : C) * z))) * ModularForm.eta ((2 : C) * (-(1 / ((2 : C) * z)))) = -I * ((Real.sqrt 2 : R) : C) * z * (ModularForm.eta z * ModularForm.eta ((2 : C) * z)). THE LEVEL-TWO INSTANCE PIN of the self-dual Fricke arc, in FULLY EXPANDED eta form: the (N, r, k) = (2, rPinTwo, 1) instance of SDF-05's eigenform relation, i.e. f = eta(z)*eta(2z), the smallest non-degenerate self-dual eta quotient, with etaQuotient, EtaExp and frickeEigenvalue all unfolded away. It is the ONLY declaration in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean whose statement mentions no definition introduced by that module -- an identity between products of values of MATHLIB's ModularForm.eta and nothing else -- so it is the only pin that exercises the etaQuotient UNFOLDING (divisors 2 = {1,2}, Finset.prod_pair, zpow_one, the 1*w and ((2:Nat):C) casts) that every other pin in the file skips. NAME DRIFT, RESOLVED. This node was PROPOSED as selfDual_pin_level_two. That name sits one underscore from the EXISTING selfDual_pin_level_two_weight_one (EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean:983), a five-way HYPOTHESIS CONJUNCTION at the SAME instance (IsFrickeSelfDual 2 rPinTwo AND sum r = 2*1 AND prod delta^{r delta} = 2 AND = 2^1 AND frickeEigenvalue 2 1 = -I*sqrt2) which mentions neither eta nor z; adopting the proposed name would have put two unrelated statement shapes one underscore apart and a base-name-matched FinalCheck guard could have guarded the wrong proposition. The file's convention for full-equation SDF-05 instance pins is selfDual_eigen_pin_* (level_one 1827, level_six 1852, zero_exp 1876, level_four_neg 1907, level_six_neg 1936); the level-two slot was free and this node takes it, with the _eta suffix flagging the expanded shape. BUILT_FROM CORRECTED, on kernel-term evidence rather than on the node text. The node was filed as built from SDF-05, SDF-03 and fricke_level_two_pin. Walking the compiled kernel term transitively (scratch_sdfpin02/DepWalk.lean, DepWalk2.lean, this run) shows it reaches etaQuotient_fricke (F32-A7), etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw (SDF-04), etaQuotient_congr_divisors (SDF-01), fricke_const_selfDual (SDF-03), prod_zpow_selfDual (SDF-02), sqrt_prod_dual, frickeEigenvalue (SDF-DEF-02), IsFrickeSelfDual (SDF-DEF-01), rPinTwo, rPinTwo_weight, rPinTwo_divisors_pin, selfDual_cond_pin_level_two_weight_one and frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_two_weight_one -- and reaches NEITHER SDF-05 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual) NOR fricke_level_two_pin. It cannot reach SDF-05: it is declared inside section Sdf05Pins, ABOVE the general lemma, so Lean's scoping rather than a docstring enforces that the pin is evidence about the route and not a consequence of it. WHAT THIS NODE IS NOT, so it is not oversold. It is NOT the (2,1) constant simplification: frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_two_weight_one (frickeEigenvalue 2 1 = -(I*sqrt2)) was already sorry-free and guarded, proved from I_zpow_neg_one and Real.sqrt_sq, never through s = prod delta^{r delta}. It is NOT 'the only odd weight': selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_neg (k = 1, lambda = -2i) already covers odd k. And it is NOT evidence about the divisor PAIRING -- rPinTwo is CONSTANT on Nat.divisors 2, which selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_no_evidence_pairing proves in Lean, so a TRANSPOSED pairing would still close it; the pairing evidence in this arc lives at level six (rPinSix_nonconstant, not_selfDual_pin_mispaired, prod_zpow_pin_mispaired_ne). WHAT IS GENUINELY NEW. (i) The SDF-03 constant collapse at an IRRATIONAL radicand: fricke_const_pin_level_two (2^1 * (sqrt(prod delta^{rPinTwo delta}))^{-1} = sqrt 2) is the first member of that pin family whose two routes meet at sqrt 2 rather than at 1, 2, 46656 or 1/46656; two_mul_inv_sqrt_two ((2:C) * (sqrt2)^{-1} = sqrt2) is the one step ring and norm_num CANNOT do (sqrt 2 is an atom to both), proved in R from Real.mul_self_sqrt and Real.sqrt_ne_zero' and only then cast to C, so no complex square root or branch choice appears; sqrt_two_nondegenerate (sqrt2 != 1 and sqrt2 != 2) certifies the collapse is not one the other pins already perform. (ii) A SECOND, INDEPENDENT DERIVATION of the node's equation, made a BUILD OBLIGATION rather than a docstring claim: selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta_via_upstream derives the identical statement from fricke_level_two_pin (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2285 -- the node text's ':2288' is mid-statement, corrected here) through selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_routes_agree (I^{-1} * 2 * (sqrt2)^{-1} = -I * sqrt2). Kernel walk confirms that second derivation reaches fricke_level_two_pin, two_mul_inv_sqrt_two and Complex.inv_I and reaches NONE of selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two, etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual, etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw, fricke_const_selfDual, prod_zpow_selfDual, frickeEigenvalue or IsFrickeSelfDual. So SDF-03's collapse and the hand computation behind fricke_level_two_pin are now checked against each other by lake build. CIRCULARITY RECEIPT. fricke_level_two_pin is in scope (EtaQuotientModularity is imported), and as a bare equation this node IS that theorem with the constant respelled, so source-text absence would not be enough. Two receipts beyond the kernel walk: every tactic in the node's proof takes an EXPLICIT lemma list (no bare norm_num, no bare simp), and fricke_level_two_pin carries no @[simp] -- whole-file scan of EtaQuotientModularity.lean for '@[simp]' and 'attribute [simp]' this run returns fifteen hits, none of them this theorem -- so no default simp set can reach it. SPELLING WRINKLE, now a named step. The node writes -I * sqrt2 while frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_two_weight_one proves -(I * sqrt2); equal by neg_mul, NOT by rfl (the same wrinkle the file header records at lines 225-227). It is isolated as frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_two_weight_one_spelling rather than absorbed into a ring. STALE METADATA CORRECTED. The node text said 'STATUS: still sorry -- OPEN in the draft'. That was wrong on both readings, verified this run: no declaration named selfDual_pin_level_two existed in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean in any form, and SDF-05 was not open -- the whole file was already sorry-free with no -- OPEN: obligation (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual closed at line 1969 before this run's insertion). NUMERICS, computed OUTSIDE Lean this run at 40 decimal digits with mpmath, from eta's product formula with 800 factors, and only then asserted: the node's exact equation holds to relative error <= 5.9e-41 at z = i, 2i, 1+i, 0.3+0.7i, -0.4+1.3i, 0.13+0.41i, while the CONJUGATE constant +i*sqrt2 fails at relative error 2.0 at every one of them; and the constant identity I^{-1}*2*(sqrt2)^{-1} = -I*sqrt2 holds to 2.3e-41. No value was adjusted to fit a proof. Its Lean counterpart is selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_not_conjugate. REACH, machine-checked, against the four degeneracies that made SDF-PIN-01 a floor: the sign of the i-exponent IS visible here (k = 1 odd, i^{-1} = -i != i, selfDual_pin_weight_one_evidence_I_sign); the power of N IS visible (2^1 != 2^2, ..._evidence_level_pow); the side of the fraction sqrt s sits on IS visible ((sqrt2)^{-1} != sqrt2, ..._evidence_radicand); the divisor involution is NOT the identity (2/1 = 2 != 1, ..._evidence_involution). The pairing is the one that stays invisible, and that is stated in Lean (..._no_evidence_pairing), not left out. SCOPE: pure eta-quotient / Fricke-eigenform content. No physics is formalised here or anywhere in EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean. The Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) claim that CHL models are self-dual under Fricke S-duality on the axio-dilaton exactly when the Frame shape is 'balanced' in THEIR sense (their eq. 1.6, the same combinatorial condition as IsFrickeSelfDual) is LITERATURE (L-tier) and belongs in the paper's prose, cited, never as a Lean statement. NAMING: 'self-dual' / 'Fricke-symmetric' for r delta = r(N/delta), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is taken in this codebase by the unrelated exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1, Int.bmod balanced-remainder division in the Gamma0(N) generator descent) and is ALSO Persson-Volpato's term for this same condition, so it collides twice.", "built_from": ["SDF-04 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw (the eigenform relation with the raw constant), instantiated at (N, r, k) = (2, rPinTwo, 1)", "SDF-03 fricke_const_selfDual (the constant collapse N^k * s^{-1/2} = sqrt(N^k)), read backwards", "SDF-DEF-02 frickeEigenvalue and frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_two_weight_one (the value -(I*sqrt2)), via the new ..._spelling lemma", "SDF-DEF-01 IsFrickeSelfDual, via selfDual_cond_pin_level_two_weight_one", "SDF-02 prod_zpow_selfDual and SDF-01 etaQuotient_congr_divisors -- reached transitively", "F32-A7 etaQuotient_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2212) -- reached transitively", "NEW supporting pins, this run: rPinTwo_weight, rPinTwo_divisors_pin, rPinTwo_values_pin, sqrt_natPow_level_two, two_mul_inv_sqrt_two, fricke_const_pin_level_two, sqrt_two_nondegenerate, frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_two_weight_one_spelling, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_value", "CROSS-CHECK ONLY, and NOT a dependency of the node itself (kernel-walk verified): fricke_level_two_pin (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2285 -- NOT :2288, which is mid-statement), used by the separate second derivation selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta_via_upstream", "NOT USED, checked by kernel-term walk: SDF-05 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual (the node is declared ABOVE it, inside section Sdf05Pins, so it cannot be), fricke_level_two_pin, eta_S_via_fricke, ModularForm.discriminant_S_invariant. The node's proposed built_from list na