{"id": "SDF-PIN-03", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_four_eta", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-01", "SDF-DEF-02", "SDF-01", "SDF-02", "SDF-03", "SDF-04", "SDF-05", "SDF-16", "F32-A7"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run). Lean statement, verbatim from the source type checked this run: theorem selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_four_eta {z : C} (hz : z in Hopen) : ModularForm.eta (-(1 / ((4 : C) * z))) ^ (2 : Z) * ModularForm.eta ((2 : C) * (-(1 / ((4 : C) * z)))) ^ (4 : Z) * ModularForm.eta ((4 : C) * (-(1 / ((4 : C) * z)))) ^ (2 : Z) = (16 : C) * z ^ (4 : Z) * (ModularForm.eta z ^ (2 : Z) * ModularForm.eta ((2 : C) * z) ^ (4 : Z) * ModularForm.eta ((4 : C) * z) ^ (2 : Z)). THE LEVEL-FOUR, WEIGHT-FOUR INSTANCE PIN of the self-dual Fricke arc, in FULLY EXPANDED eta form: the (N, r, k) = (4, rPinLevelFourWeightFour, 4) instance of SDF-05's eigenform relation, i.e. f = eta(z)^2 * eta(2z)^4 * eta(4z)^2, with etaQuotient, EtaExp, frickeEigenvalue and IsFrickeSelfDual all unfolded away. Arithmetic, computed by hand before any Lean was written: divisors 4 = {1,2,4}; r = (2,4,2); self-dual since r(4/1) = r4 = 2 = r1, r(4/2) = r2 = 4, r(4/4) = r1 = 2 = r4; sum r delta = 8 = 2*4 so k = 4; s = prod delta^{r delta} = 1^2 * 2^4 * 4^2 = 256 = 4^4 = N^k (SDF-02 agrees); lambda = i^{-4} * sqrt(256) = 1 * 16 = 16. VERBATIM-STATEMENT RECEIPT. The node text as supplied names the theorem selfDual_pin_level_four. That exact statement string, transcribed character for character with only the NAME changed, was type checked this run (scratch_sdfpin03/VerbatimCheck.lean) and closed by 'selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_four_eta hz' as a bare term application -- so the two are the SAME proposition, not merely equivalent, and this node resolves the supplied statement exactly. NAME DRIFT, RESOLVED -- TWO SEPARATE COLLISIONS. (i) selfDual_pin_* (no 'eigen') is the SDF-PIN-01 family (selfDual_pin_level_one, _level_six, _zero_exp, _level_two_weight_one, _eigenvalue_neg_one), every member of which is a five-way HYPOTHESIS CONJUNCTION mentioning neither z nor eta; this node is an eta-level EQUATION, whose existing analogue is selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta, so it takes the selfDual_eigen_pin_* slot with the _eta suffix. (ii) the suffix _level_four ALONE already denotes a DIFFERENT instance throughout this library -- N = 4, r = (-2, 6, -2), k = 1: rPinLevelFourNeg, frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_four = -(2*I), sqrt_natPow_level_four = 2, natCast_zpow_pin_level_four_value = 4. This node needs sqrt(4^4) = 16, not sqrt(4^1) = 2, so every new name carries the WEIGHT as well as the level (_level_four_weight_four) and the new radicand lemma is sqrt_natPow_level_four_weight_four. Kernel walk confirms the separation is real: the node does NOT reach sqrt_natPow_level_four. Items 5 and 6 of the negative control are the two name-drift controls. STALE METADATA CORRECTED. The node text said 'STATUS: still sorry -- OPEN in the draft'. That is wrong, verified this run: no declaration named selfDual_pin_level_four existed in either repository in any form (grep over SocrateAI-Lean-Lib and foundationpaper2, excluding .lake, returns nothing), and EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean was already entirely sorry-free with no -- OPEN: obligation. SDF-PIN-03 is a new node, not a resumption. WHAT IS GENUINELY NEW, and what is not. It is NOT the first eta-unfolded pin: selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta (SDF-PIN-02) is, at N = 2, k = 1. It is NOT the first pin to discriminate SDF-02's s = N^k: selfDual_pin_level_six / prod_zpow_pin_level_six_value already pin s = 6^12 = 2176782336 = N^k, a strictly stronger instance. What it genuinely adds is the FIRST eta-unfolded eigenform identity at N > 2, at EVEN weight, and on a NON-CONSTANT exponent vector -- that last is the degeneracy selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_no_evidence_pairing records in Lean (rPinTwo is constant on divisors 2, so a TRANSPOSED pairing would still close SDF-PIN-02); here r 1 = 2 != 4 = r 2, so this is the first eta-unfolded pin in the file carrying evidence about the divisor PAIRING. Second new structural feature: at N = 4 the involution delta -> 4/delta has a FIXED POINT (4/2 = 2), so self-duality is a mixture of one swap constraint (r 1 = r 4) and one automatically-satisfied constraint (r 2 = r 2) -- a shape no level-one or level-two pin exercises. STATED LIMITATION, in Lean, so the node cannot be oversold (selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_four_no_evidence_level_weight). At this instance the LEVEL and the WEIGHT are the SAME NUMBER, N = 4 = k. A constant that had confused the two -- sqrt(k^N) for sqrt(N^k), or N^{k/2} for k^{N/2} -- reads 16 either way and is INVISIBLE here (both equal 16, checked numerically, rel. err 1.4e-15 for both). So the claim 'any wrong power of the level shows up as a wrong integer here' is too strong. The degeneracy is broken inside the same section by TWO further eta-unfolded companion pins, which is why they were stated: selfDual_eigen_pin_level_nine_weight_four_eta (N = 9, r = (1,6,1), k = 4, s = 6561 = 9^4, lambda = 81) moves the LEVEL at fixed weight -- sqrt(9^4) = 81 while sqrt(4^9) = 512, and only 81 closes it -- and selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_two_eta (N = 4, r = (1,2,1), k = 2, s = 16 = 4^2, lambda = -4) moves the WEIGHT at fixed level, with a NEGATIVE constant, so i^{-k} is doing visible work there in a way it cannot at k = 4 where i^{-4} = 1. Neither alone breaks the degeneracy. PINS BEFORE THE NODE, per this run's sign/definitional discipline, in the three named regimes. (A) N = 1, r == 24, k = 12: selfDual_eigen_pin_level_one_eta_calibration re-derives, along THIS file's SDF-05/SDF-04/SDF-03/SDF-02 route, the exact statement eta_S_via_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246) proves independently and with no self-duality anywhere; kernel walk confirms the calibration does NOT reach eta_S_via_fricke, and ..._agrees pairs the two proofs of that one proposition so the agreement is a build obligation rather than a docstring claim. (B) degenerate r == 0, stated at the NODE'S OWN level N = 4, k = 0, lambda = 1 (selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_zero_exp), so it certifies that the 16 comes from the EXPONENTS and not from the level. (C) a genuine N > 1 self-dual non-constant vector: the node itself, plus the level-nine and weight-two companions above. Supporting decide-pins: divisors_four_pin, divisors_nine_pin, self-duality by TWO routes (selfDual_cond_pin_level_four_weight_four by bare decide through SDF-16's instance, and ..._unfolded by unfold IsFrickeSelfDual; decide, needing no instance), the four weight witnesses, rPinLevelFourWeightFour_values_pin, and the NON-VACUITY control not_selfDual_pin_level_four_mispaired (rPinLevelFourMispaired = (4,4,0) has the SAME weight sum 8 = 2*4, so hk accepts it and only hr rejects it). TWO-ROUTE PRODUCT CHECK: prod_zpow_pin_level_four_weight_four computes s = 256 DIRECTLY from divisors 4 = {1,2,4} while prod_zpow_selfDual_pin_level_four_weight_four reaches the same number through SDF-02's general collapse s = N^k; the two must agree, and neither is a dependency of the node (kernel-walk verified), so they are cross-checks rather than plumbing. NUMERICS, computed OUTSIDE Lean this run at 60 decimal digits with mpmath, from eta's product formula with 1200 factors, and only then asserted: the node's exact equation holds to relative error <= 3.5e-60 at z = i, 0.3+0.7i, -0.11+0.45i, 0.25+0.9i, -0.4+1.3i, 0.05+0.31i. Negative controls at z = 0.3+0.7i: lambda = 256 fails at rel. err 9.4e-1, lambda = 4 at 3.0, lambda = 8 at 1.0, lambda = 32 at 5.0e-1, lambda = -16 at 2.0, lambda = 16i at 1.4, z^2 in place of z^4 at 1.5, z^6 at 2.5. The four calibration/companion pins hold to <= 1.5e-59 at z = 0.3+0.7i. No value was adjusted to fit a proof. SCOPE: pure eta-quotient / Fricke-eigenform content. An identity between products of values of Mathlib's ModularForm.eta. Nothing about Gamma0(N)-modularity, holomorphy at cusps, or physics. The Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) claim that CHL models are self-dual under Fricke S-duality on the axio-dilaton exactly when the Frame shape is 'balanced' in THEIR sense (their eq. 1.6, the same combinatorial condition as IsFrickeSelfDual) is LITERATURE (L-tier) and belongs in the paper's prose, cited, never as a Lean statement. NAMING: 'self-dual' / 'Fricke-symmetric' for r delta = r(N/delta), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is taken in this codebase by the unrelated exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1, Int.bmod balanced-remainder division in the Gamma0(N) generator descent) and is ALSO Persson-Volpato's term for this same condition, so it collides twice.", "built_from": ["SDF-05 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual, instantiated at (N, r, k) = (4, rPinLevelFourWeightFour, 4) -- the node's single load-bearing step", "SDF-DEF-02 frickeEigenvalue, via the new numeral pin frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_four_weight_four (= 16), itself I_zpow_neg_four (i^{-4} = 1) and sqrt_natPow_level_four_weight_four (sqrt(4^4) = 16) -- a route that never touches s", "SDF-16 decidableIsFrickeSelfDual, via selfDual_cond_pin_level_four_weight_four (bare decide); the second discharge ..._unfolded uses unfold IsFrickeSelfDual; decide and needs no instance", "SDF-DEF-01 IsFrickeSelfDual, SDF-04 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw, SDF-03 fricke_const_selfDual, SDF-02 prod_zpow_selfDual, SDF-01 etaQuotient_congr_divisors -- all reached transitively through SDF-05 (kernel-term walk, scratch_sdfpin03/DepWalk.lean, this run)", "F32-A7 etaQuotient_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2212) -- reached transitively", "NEW supporting declarations, this run (40 in section SdfPin03): divisors_four_pin, divisors_nine_pin, rPinLevelFourWeightFour, rPinLevelNineWeightFour, rPinLevelFourWeightTwo, rPinLevelFourMispaired, selfDual_cond_pin_level_four_weight_four(+_unfolded), not_selfDual_pin_level_four_mispaired, selfDual_cond_pin_level_nine_weight_four, selfDual_cond_pin_level_four_weight_two, selfDual_cond_pin_level_four_zero_exp, the five weight witnesses, rPinLevelFourWeightFour_values_pin, the four product pins, the three radicand pins, I_zpow_neg_four, the three frickeEigenvalue pins, the calibration pair, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_zero_exp, the two companion eta pins, the node, four evidence lemmas and one no_evidence limitation", "CROSS-CHECK ONLY, NOT a dependency (kernel-walk verified absent from the node's term): eta_S_via_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246), used only by the separate calibration selfDual_eigen_pin_level_one_eta_calibration_agrees; and prod_zpow_pin_level_four_weight_four / prod_zpow_selfDual_pin_level_four_weight_four, the two-route product check", "NOT USED, checked by kernel-term walk: selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta (SDF-PIN-02), fricke_level_two_pin, etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized (SDF-06), sqrt_natPow_level_four (the WEIGHT-ONE radicand lemma whose name this node deliberately does not reuse)"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section SdfPin03 (#print axioms on all thirty-six new theorems, including the node's own selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_four_eta, the two companion eta pins and the calibration pair). Thirty-four footprints are [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; two (rPinLevelFourWeightFour_values_pin, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_four_evidence_pairing, both closed by decide on a decidable proposition about the exponent vector alone) are 'does not depend on any axioms'. No sorryAx. Must-fail control: verification/SdfPin03NegControl.lean (exits 1, TWELVE error lines, one per item -- item 2 the wrong constant 256 (the radicand, not its square root) as a type mismatch, item 5 the name-drift control that sqrt_natPow_level_four (sqrt(4^1) = 2) does NOT close sqrt(4^4) = 16, item 6 the name-drift control that the selfDual_pin_* CONJUNCTION family does NOT close this equation, item 8 the stated pairing evidence inverted, item 9 the degeneracy control that the level-nine companion is NOT blind to the level/weight swap (residual goal 81 = sqrt 262144), item 10 the sign control that pin D's constant is -4 and not 4)."}
{"id": "SDF-PIN-04", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_eta", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-01", "SDF-DEF-02", "SDF-01", "SDF-02", "SDF-03", "SDF-04", "SDF-05", "SDF-16", "F32-A7"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run). Lean statement, verbatim from the source type checked this run: theorem selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_eta {z : C} (hz : z in Hopen) : ModularForm.eta (-(1 / ((4 : C) * z))) ^ (-2 : Z) * ModularForm.eta ((2 : C) * (-(1 / ((4 : C) * z)))) ^ (4 : Z) * ModularForm.eta ((4 : C) * (-(1 / ((4 : C) * z)))) ^ (-2 : Z) = ModularForm.eta z ^ (-2 : Z) * ModularForm.eta ((2 : C) * z) ^ (4 : Z) * ModularForm.eta ((4 : C) * z) ^ (-2 : Z). THE LEVEL-FOUR, WEIGHT-ZERO INSTANCE PIN of the self-dual Fricke arc, in FULLY EXPANDED eta form: the (N, r, k) = (4, rPinLevelFourWeightZero, 0) instance of SDF-05's eigenform relation, i.e. f = eta(2z)^4 / (eta(z)^2 eta(4z)^2), with etaQuotient, EtaExp, frickeEigenvalue and IsFrickeSelfDual all unfolded away. Arithmetic, computed by hand before any Lean was written: divisors 4 = {1,2,4}; r = (-2,4,-2); self-dual since r(4/1) = r4 = -2 = r1, r(4/2) = r2 = 4, r(4/4) = r1 = -2 = r4; sum r delta = -2+4-2 = 0 = 2*0 so k = 0; s = prod delta^{r delta} = 1^-2 * 2^4 * 4^-2 = 16 * (1/16) = 1 = 4^0 = N^k (SDF-02 agrees, and the two routes to s are both stated: prod_zpow_pin_level_four_weight_zero directly, prod_zpow_selfDual_pin_level_four_weight_zero through SDF-02); lambda = i^{-0} * sqrt(4^0) = 1. Because lambda = 1 and k = 0 the eigenvalue and the z^k factor are BOTH ABSENT from the statement, which is why the node's equation has the bare shape f(-1/(4z)) = f(z): the quotient is INVARIANT under the Fricke involution. VERBATIM-STATEMENT RECEIPT. The node text as supplied names the theorem selfDual_pin_weight_zero. That exact statement string, transcribed character for character with only the NAME changed, was type checked this run (scratch_sdfpin04/VerbatimCheck.lean, exit 0) and closed by 'selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_eta hz' as a bare term application -- so the two are the SAME proposition, not merely equivalent, and this node resolves the supplied statement exactly. NAME DRIFT, RESOLVED -- TWO COLLISIONS. (i) selfDual_pin_* (no 'eigen') is the SDF-PIN-01 family (selfDual_pin_level_one, _level_six, _zero_exp, _level_two_weight_one, _eigenvalue_neg_one), every member of which is a five-way HYPOTHESIS CONJUNCTION mentioning neither z nor eta; a base-name-matched FinalCheck guard against the proposed name could therefore have guarded the wrong proposition. This is an eta-level EQUATION, so it takes the selfDual_eigen_pin_* slot with the _eta suffix, exactly as SDF-PIN-02 and SDF-PIN-03 did. Item 6 of the negative control is the matching name-drift control. (ii) _weight_zero is NOT _zero_exp: selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_zero_exp is the r == 0 pin at the SAME level, the SAME weight k = 0 and the SAME eigenvalue lambda = 1. The two are different vectors and rPinLevelFourWeightZero_ne_zero_pin is the Lean receipt. BUILT_FROM CORRECTED, on kernel-term evidence rather than on the node text. The node was filed as built from [SDF-05, SDF-12, SDF-16]. Walking the compiled kernel term transitively (scratch_sdfpin04/DepWalk.lean, this run) shows the node reaches etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual (SDF-05), etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw (SDF-04), fricke_const_selfDual (SDF-03), prod_zpow_selfDual (SDF-02), etaQuotient_congr_divisors (SDF-01), frickeEigenvalue (SDF-DEF-02), IsFrickeSelfDual (SDF-DEF-01), decidableIsFrickeSelfDual (SDF-16), etaQuotient_fricke (F32-A7), and the new frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_four_weight_zero / sqrt_natPow_level_four_weight_zero / selfDual_cond_pin_level_four_weight_zero -- and reaches NEITHER frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff (SDF-12, the declared dependency, NOT used: the eigenvalue numeral is reached through frickeEigenvalue and Real.sqrt_one, never through SDF-12's iff) NOR eta_S_via_fricke NOR ModularForm.discriminant_S_invariant. Both of the latter two names were confirmed to EXIST by #check in the same session, so 'absent' is a receipt and not a typo. TWO INDEPENDENT DERIVATIONS, made a BUILD OBLIGATION rather than a docstring claim. Besides the node theorem (through SDF-05's packaged frickeEigenvalue 4 0), selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_eta_via_fricke derives the IDENTICAL statement straight from etaQuotient_fricke (F32-A7, EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2212) with the raw constant i^{-k} * N^k * s^{-1/2} evaluated in place; the dual-vector collapse is carried by the hand-written etaQuotient_dual_pin_level_four_weight_zero (a Finset.prod_congr over the bare decide fact rPinLevelFourWeightZero_dual_eq_pin), so the second route touches NONE of etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual, etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw, fricke_const_selfDual, prod_zpow_selfDual, etaQuotient_congr_divisors, frickeEigenvalue, IsFrickeSelfDual or decidableIsFrickeSelfDual -- kernel-walk verified. selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_routes_agree pairs the two, so this module's packaged constant agreeing with the upstream raw constant at this instance is a lake build obligation. WHAT THIS PIN IS NOT -- THE SUBSTANTIVE CAVEAT, READ BEFORE CITING IT AS EVIDENCE. At k = 0 EVERY component of the Fricke constant lambda = i^{-k} * N^k * s^{-1/2} collapses to 1 for a reason that survives any misspelling of it: i^{-0} = i^{+0}; N^0 = 1 for EVERY level (4^0 = 9^0); s = 1 so (sqrt s)^{-1} = sqrt s; and z^0 = 1 for every z. THIS PIN THEREFORE PINS NO COMPONENT OF THE FRICKE CONSTANT and cannot discriminate a wrong sign of the i-power, a wrong power of N, an inverted square root, or a wrong z-exponent. That is stated in Lean, not left out, as selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_no_evidence_constant, and item 9 of the negative control INVERTS it and must fail, so the honesty claim is itself machine-checked. It is the same accounting selfDual_pin_level_one_no_evidence_* gives the N = 1 pin. This node must NOT be counted toward this arc's constant-pinning instances; those are selfDual_eigen_pin_level_six (N=6, k=12, lambda=46656), selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_neg (N=4, k=1, lambda=-2i), selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_eta (N=2, k=1, lambda=-i*sqrt2) and selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_two_eta (N=4, k=2, lambda=-4). WHAT IT GENUINELY ADDS. (a) It is the FIRST eta-unfolded pin in the file with NEGATIVE exponents (..._evidence_negative_exponents: r1 < 0, r4 < 0, 0 < r2); selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_neg has them but is stated on etaQuotient, and the three existing eta-unfolded pins all have r > 0 throughout. So both signs of zpow occur in one eta-level identity. (b) s = 1 arises by CANCELLATION (2^4 = 16, 4^-2 = 1/16, and 16 != 1; ..._evidence_radicand_cancels), not because every factor is separately 1 as in the r == 0 pin at the same level -- which is what makes this more than a respelling of selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_zero_exp. (c) The exponent vector is NON-CONSTANT (..._evidence_pairing: r1 = -2 != 4 = r2), so the transposed-pairing degeneracy selfDual_eigen_pin_level_two_no_evidence_pairing records at level two does not apply here. NON-VACUITY: rPinLevelFourWeightZeroMispaired = (0,4,-4) carries the SAME weight sum 0 = 2*0 (rPinLevelFourWeightZeroMispaired_weight), so hk accepts it and only hr rejects it (not_selfDual_pin_level_four_weight_zero_mispaired); item 10 of the negative control instantiates SDF-05 there with the node's own tactic block and fails on hr alone. (d) The identity is not vacuous: rPinLevelFourWeightZero_ne_zero_pin proves the vector is not zero, and numerically f is not identically 1 (f(i) = 1.6944, f(0.3+0.7i) = 1.4192 - 0.1907i). PINS BEFORE THE NODE, per this run's sign/definitional discipline, in the three named regimes, conjoined as ONE build obligation (selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_regime_battery) so the discipline is machine-checked rather than asserted: (A) N = 1, r == 24, k = 12 -- selfDual_eigen_pin_level_one_eta_calibration, whose statement is character-for-character eta_S_via_fricke's (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2246); (B) the degenerate r == 0 case at the NODE'S OWN level, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_zero_exp; (C) a genuine N > 1 self-dual NON-CONSTANT vector at NON-zero weight, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_nine_weight_four_eta (N=9, r=(1,6,1), k=4, lambda=81) -- which is where the constant actually is pinned, since it is not pinned here. Plus this section's own decide-pins: the three values, the weight sum, the dual values, self-duality by TWO routes (bare decide through SDF-16's instance, and unfold IsFrickeSelfDual; decide needing no instance), the mis-paired control and its weight, and the two-route product check. NUMERICS, computed OUTSIDE Lean this run at 60 decimal digits with mpmath, from eta's product formula with 1500 factors, and only then asserted: the node's exact equation holds to relative error <= 2.9e-60 at z = 0.3+0.7i, -0.11+0.45i, 0.9+1.3i, i, 0.05+0.31i, -0.4+1.3i. Negative controls at z = 0.3+0.7i: lambda = -1 fails at relative error 2.0, lambda = i at 1.41, lambda = 16 at 0.94, lambda = 1/16 at 15.0, an inserted z^1 at 1.30, an inserted z^-1 at 0.99, and the mis-paired vector at 0.73; the mis-paired vector also fails the equation outright at three points (relative error 0.58 to 1.06). No value was adjusted to fit a proof. SCOPE: pure eta-quotient / Fricke-eigenform content. An identity between products of values of Mathlib's ModularForm.eta. Nothing about Gamma0(N)-modularity, holomorphy at cusps, or physics. The Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) claim that CHL models are self-dual under Fricke S-duality on the axio-dilaton exactly when the Frame shape is 'balanced' in THEIR sense (their eq. 1.6, the same combinatorial condition as IsFrickeSelfDual) is LITERATURE (L-tier) and belongs in the paper's prose, cited, never as a Lean statement. NAMING: 'self-dual' / 'Fricke-symmetric' for r delta = r(N/delta), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is taken in this codebase by the unrelated exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1, Int.bmod balanced-remainder division in the Gamma0(N) generator descent) and is ALSO Persson-Volpato's term for this same condition, so it collides twice.", "built_from": ["SDF-05 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual, instantiated at (N, r, k) = (4, rPinLevelFourWeightZero, 0) -- the node's single load-bearing step", "SDF-DEF-02 frickeEigenvalue, via the new numeral pin frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_four_weight_zero (= 1), itself sqrt_natPow_level_four_weight_zero (sqrt(4^0) = 1) -- a route that never touches s", "SDF-16 decidableIsFrickeSelfDual, via selfDual_cond_pin_level_four_weight_zero (bare decide); the second discharge ..._unfolded uses unfold IsFrickeSelfDual; decide and needs no instance", "SDF-DEF-01 IsFrickeSelfDual, SDF-04 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_raw, SDF-03 fricke_const_selfDual, SDF-02 prod_zpow_selfDual, SDF-01 etaQuotient_congr_divisors -- all reached transitively through SDF-05 (kernel-term walk, scratch_sdfpin04/DepWalk.lean, this run)", "F32-A7 etaQuotient_fricke (EtaQuotientModularity.lean:2212) -- reached transitively by the node, and DIRECTLY and alone by the second derivation ..._eta_via_fricke", "NEW supporting declarations, this run (23 in section SdfPin04): rPinLevelFourWeightZero, rPinLevelFourWeightZeroMispaired, rPinLevelFourWeightZero_values_pin, rPinLevelFourWeightZero_weight, rPinLevelFourWeightZero_dual_eq_pin, selfDual_cond_pin_level_four_weight_zero(+_unfolded), rPinLevelFourWeightZeroMispaired_weight, not_selfDual_pin_level_four_weight_zero_mispaired, rPinLevelFourWeightZero_ne_zero_pin, prod_zpow_pin_level_four_weight_zero, prod_zpow_selfDual_pin_level_four_weight_zero, sqrt_natPow_level_four_weight_zero, frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_four_weight_zero, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_regime_battery, the node, etaQuotient_dual_pin_level_four_weight_zero, ..._eta_via_fricke, ..._routes_agree, three evidence lemmas and one no_evidence limitation", "CROSS-CHECK ONLY, NOT dependencies of the node itself (kernel-walk verified absent from its term): prod_zpow_pin_level_four_weight_zero and prod_zpow_selfDual_pin_level_four_weight_zero (the two-route product check), and the whole ..._eta_via_fricke second derivation", "NOT USED, checked by kernel-term walk: SDF-12 frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff (the node text DECLARED it; it is absent -- the eigenvalue numeral is reached through frickeEigenvalue and Real.sqrt_one), eta_S_via_fricke, ModularForm.discriminant_S_invariant, selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_four_eta (SDF-PIN-03), selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_zero_exp (used only by the regime battery, not by the node)"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "SocrateAI.FinalCheck section SdfPin04 (#print axioms on all twenty-one new theorems, including the node's own selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_weight_zero_eta, the second derivation ..._eta_via_fricke, the pairing ..._routes_agree and the regime battery). Seventeen footprints are [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; three (rPinLevelFourWeightZero_values_pin, ..._evidence_pairing, ..._evidence_negative_exponents, all closed by decide on a decidable proposition about the exponent vector alone) are 'does not depend on any axioms'; one (rPinLevelFourWeightZero_ne_zero_pin) is [propext]. No sorryAx. The guard blocks were GENERATED from the captured #print axioms output (scratch_sdfpin04/ax.out -> guards.txt), not hand-written. Must-fail control: verification/SdfPin04NegControl.lean (exits 1, TWELVE error lines, one per item -- item 6 the NAME-DRIFT control that selfDual_eigen_pin_level_four_zero_exp (the r == 0 pin at the same level, same weight, same eigenvalue) does NOT close this equation, item 9 the HONESTY control that inverts the section's own stated limitation i^{-0} = i^{+0} and must fail, item 10 the LOAD-BEARING-HYPOTHESIS control that instantiates SDF-05 at the same-weight mis-paired vector and fails on hr alone, item 11 the radicand with the 4^-2 factor dropped, residual goal False)."}
{"id": "SDF-PIN-05", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.selfDual_pin_zero_exp", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-DEF-01", "SDF-DEF-02"], "statement_nl": "ALREADY CLOSED BEFORE THIS RUN; RETARGETED, NOT NEWLY PROVED. This node was filed with the statement 'theorem selfDual_pin_zero_exp {N : N} (hN : 0 < N) {z : C} (hz : z in Hopen) : etaQuotient N 0 (-(1 / ((N : C) * z))) = etaQuotient N 0 z'. That statement was NOT added. Two independent reasons, both machine-checked this run (lake --packages=local-packages.json env lean, exit 0; probe kept at scratchpad/pin05_verify.lean). (1) NAME COLLISION WITH A STRICTLY STRONGER, ALREADY-GUARDED THEOREM. selfDual_pin_zero_exp already exists at EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean:1060, sorry-free, and is already guarded at FinalCheck.lean:6109-6110 inside the section headed 'The five conjunction pins -- SDF-05's bookkeeping, now closed'. Its actual type, printed this run: IsFrickeSelfDual 6 0 AND sum_{d | 6} 0 d = 2*0 AND prod_{d | 6} d^(0 d) = 1 AND prod_{d | 6} d^(0 d) = 6^0 AND frickeEigenvalue 6 0 = 1. That is the file's 'PIN 3 -- the degenerate vector r == 0', in the same five-way conjunction shape as its four siblings. Declaring the filed statement under this name would be a duplicate declaration; declaring it under a fresh name would add a SECOND, WEAKER r == 0 pin beside a stronger one already closed and guarded, and the DAG's base-name FinalCheck match would in any case resolve to the existing theorem. (2) THE FILED STATEMENT PINS NOTHING AND DOES NOT USE THE REFERENCE THEOREM. It drops both the Fricke constant and the z^k factor, so BOTH SIDES ARE LITERALLY THE CONSTANT 1: verified this run, 'theorem node_is_constant_one (N : N) (w : C) : etaQuotient N 0 w = 1 := by simp [etaQuotient]' typechecks with NO hypotheses whatsoever, hence so does the node's equation with hN and hz both deleted (node_without_hypotheses). Lean's own linters certify the hypotheses are decorative: on the verbatim transcription both 'hN' and 'hz' fire 'Variable name is not explicitly referenced', and deriving it through the reference theorem (etaQuotient_fricke at r = 0, k = 0) fires unnecessarySimpa -- i.e. the goal closes WITHOUT the specialization. The underlying reason is only zpow_zero: etaQuotient N 0 w = prod_{d | N} eta(dw)^(0:Z) = prod 1 = 1. Such a statement cannot discriminate a wrong sign in i^(-k), a wrong power of N, an inverted square root, or a wrong d <-> N/d pairing. NOTE the degeneracy is inherent to r == 0 at EVERY statement shape, not an artifact of dropping the constant: the eigenvalue-RETAINING form 'etaQuotient N 0 (-(1/(N z))) = frickeEigenvalue N 0 * z^(0:Z) * etaQuotient N 0 z' is likewise closed by simp [etaQuotient, frickeEigenvalue] (node_strong_still_trivial). THEREFORE THIS NODE MUST NOT BE COUNTED toward the arc's 3+ independently computed decide-pin instances; the constant-pinning load is carried by SDF-PIN-02 (N=2, k=1, lambda=-i sqrt2), SDF-PIN-03 (N=4, k=4, lambda=16) and the shipped selfDual_eigen_pin_level_six (N=6, k=12, lambda=46656) / selfDual_eigen_pin_level_nine_weight_four_eta (N=9, k=4, lambda=81). This is the same accounting SDF-PIN-04's entry gives itself, one degree more severe. DERIVATION IS NEVERTHELESS GAP-FREE, checked so that 'trivial' is not confused with 'unproved': 'have h := etaQuotient_fricke hN (0 : EtaExp) (k := 0) (by simp) hz; simpa using h' typechecks (node_via_fricke) -- hk becomes sum 0 = 2*0, the dual vector (fun d => (0 : EtaExp) (N/d)) is DEFEQ to 0, and i^(-0) = N^0 = (sqrt 1)^-1 = z^0 = 1. AN N=6 INSTANCE OF THE FILED EQUATION IS ALREADY SHIPPED AND GUARDED: selfDual_eigen_pin_zero_exp_value : etaQuotient 6 0 (-(1 / (6 * z))) = etaQuotient 6 0 z (EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean:1989), axioms [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. So even the transformation-law-shaped reading of this node is not new content. DECLARED DEPENDENCIES CORRECTED ON KERNEL EVIDENCE, and a prior review's claim REVERSED. The node was filed as built from [SDF-05, SDF-12, SDF-DEF-01], and it was suggested that retargeting to the existing theorem would make both real because its type mentions frickeEigenvalue 6 0 = 1. A kernel-term walk this run (scratchpad/DepWalk2.lean, adapted from scratch_sdfpin04/DepWalk.lean and VALIDATED on a control root that correctly reaches SDF-01/-02/-03/F32-A7) shows that is FALSE: selfDual_pin_zero_exp reaches 11253 constants, among them IsFrickeSelfDual (SDF-DEF-01) and frickeEigenvalue (SDF-DEF-02) plus its two discharges frickeEigenvalue_pin_zero_weight and selfDual_cond_pin_zero_exp -- and reaches NEITHER etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual (SDF-05) NOR frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff (SDF-12), nor even etaQuotient or ModularForm.eta, and no sorryAx. The eigenvalue numeral is reached through frickeEigenvalue and Real.sqrt_one, never through SDF-12's iff. SDF-12 is unreached by EVERY candidate statement for this node, so that edge is decorative under any retarget and has been dropped rather than recorded. depends_on is therefore [SDF-DEF-01, SDF-DEF-02] exactly. (METHOD NOTE, recorded because it nearly produced a wrong entry: a first dependency walk built on ConstantInfo.value? silently returned none for every theorem, so it traversed TYPES ONLY and reported spurious 'absent' results; it was caught by a control root and discarded. The numbers above are from the validated walker only.) SCOPE: pure eta-quotient / Fricke-eigenform bookkeeping. No Gamma0(N)-modularity, no cusp behaviour, NO PHYSICS. The Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) claim that CHL models are self-dual under Fricke S-duality on the axio-dilaton exactly when the Frame shape is 'balanced' in THEIR sense (their eq. 1.6, the same combinatorial condition as IsFrickeSelfDual) is LITERATURE (L-tier), belongs in the paper's prose, cited, and is NOT formalized here or anywhere in this arc. NAMING: 'self-dual' / 'Fricke-symmetric' for r d = r(N/d), NEVER 'balanced' -- that word is taken in this codebase by the unrelated exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1, Int.bmod balanced-remainder division in the Gamma0(N) generator descent) and is ALSO Persson-Volpato's term for this same condition, so it collides twice.", "built_from": ["SDF-DEF-01 IsFrickeSelfDual, via selfDual_cond_pin_zero_exp (r == 0 is self-dual at every level by rfl) -- kernel-walk confirmed reached", "SDF-DEF-02 frickeEigenvalue, via frickeEigenvalue_pin_zero_weight (frickeEigenvalue 6 0 = 1) -- kernel-walk confirmed reached", "NO NEW DECLARATIONS WERE ADDED THIS RUN. The resolving theorem predates this run; this entry records the node as closed by it and corrects the filed statement and dependency edges.", "NOT USED, kernel-walk verified absent from the resolving theorem's term: SDF-05 etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual and SDF-12 frickeEigenvalue_eq_one_iff (both DECLARED by the node text), F32-A7 etaQuotient_fricke, SDF-04, SDF-03, SDF-02, SDF-01, SDF-16, etaQuotient, ModularForm.eta, sorryAx", "CROSS-CHECK ONLY, not dependencies: selfDual_eigen_pin_zero_exp_value (the shipped N=6 instance of the filed equation) and node_via_fricke (the scratchpad derivation of the filed statement from F32-A7), both typechecked this run"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/EtaQuotientFrickeSelfDual.lean", "guard": "PRE-EXISTING, NOT ADDED THIS RUN. SocrateAI.FinalCheck lines 6109-6110, section 'The five conjunction pins -- SDF-05's bookkeeping, now closed': #guard_msgs in #print axioms selfDual_pin_zero_exp, footprint [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Base-name match against lean_name selfDual_pin_zero_exp holds (2 occurrences in FinalCheck.lean, the expected-output docstring and the command). Re-verified this run by direct #print axioms on all five conjunction pins plus selfDual_eigen_pin_zero_exp_value: all six [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. Full build green: 'Build completed successfully (3720 jobs).'"}
{"id": "SDF-GUARD", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_statement_pin", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-05", "SDF-06", "SDF-16"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (this run), sorry-free. THE GUARD/PIN NODE for the SDF block: it proves no new mathematics and must never be reported as if it did. Two halves. HALF 1 -- AXIOM GUARDS. Every SDF node carries exactly one `#guard_msgs in #print axioms <name>` in FinalCheck.lean, in the style of the F3.2-A7 block (FinalCheck.lean:1604-1646). Re-verified THIS run by regex over FinalCheck.lean, base-name matched against each node's resolving lean_name rather than assumed: all 23 SDF nodes -- SDF-DEF-01 (IsFrickeSelfDual), SDF-DEF-02 (frickeEigenvalue), SDF-01 ... SDF-16, and SDF-PIN-01 ... SDF-PIN-05 -- have a guard, exactly one each, count 1 for every node. They live in namespaces SdfDef01, SdfDef02, Sdf01 ... Sdf16; the five SDF-PIN nodes are guarded inside Sdf05 alongside the SDF-05 instance pins. Note the two DEF nodes: they are kind='def' and so are exempt from check_dag rule 7, but they are guarded anyway, and the node enumeration must include them. HALF 2 -- THE TWO LONGHAND STATEMENT PINS, which are the only work this node actually added. etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_statement_pin and etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized_statement_pin restate SDF-05 and SDF-06 with EVERY SocrateAI abbreviation removed: level as a POSITIVE natural (PNat) rather than a bare Nat with a positivity hypothesis, point as a bundled z : UpperHalfPlane rather than a raw Complex plus a membership hypothesis, exponent vector as the bare (Nat -> Int) rather than the EtaExp abbreviation, IsFrickeSelfDual UNFOLDED to the bounded quantifier (forall delta in N.divisors, r delta = r (N / delta)), etaQuotient UNFOLDED on BOTH sides to a product over Nat.divisors with ModularForm.eta fully qualified, and -- for SDF-05 -- frickeEigenvalue UNFOLDED to I^(-k) * sqrt((N:Real)^k). THE EIGENVALUE UNFOLDING IS THE POINT and was ADDED after the statement comparator returned WEAKER on this node as originally filed: the original pin spec listed level, point, vector, IsFrickeSelfDual and the eta products but NOT frickeEigenvalue, so a pin obeying it literally would still have printed `frickeEigenvalue N k` on the right-hand side -- the entire content of SDF-05 hidden behind a definition of ours, which is exactly the failure mode the pin exists to prevent, and which the F3.2-A7 pin at FinalCheck.lean:1657 avoids by writing its raw constant out as text. SDF-06 needs no such clause and has none: etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized already states its constants as (sqrt((N:Real)^k))^{-1}, z^(-k) and I^(-k), with no eigenvalue definition anywhere in it. WHAT THE PINS BUY. Each is closed by a bare proof TERM applied to the corresponding general lemma (N.pos for the positivity hypothesis, z.2 for the membership hypothesis), so elaboration succeeds only if the longhand proposition is DEFINITIONALLY the general lemma's. Nothing is reproved and no tactic runs. In particular the reader can see, without chasing a definition, that the RIGHT-hand eta product runs over `r delta` -- the SAME vector as the left, not the dual `r (N/delta)` that F3.2-A7's transformation law carries. That collapse is the whole difference between a transformation law and an eigenform relation. NON-VACUITY CHECKED, not assumed (scratch_sdfguard/neg/, ten files, each run this session): five perturbations of each pin, fed the same proof term, ALL fail to elaborate -- I^(+k) for I^(-k), sqrt(N^(2k)) for sqrt(N^k), the normaliser inverted the wrong way, z^(2k) for z^k (resp. z^k for z^(-k)), and the dual r(N/delta) for r delta in the right-hand product. The two true statements elaborate. NAMED, NOT `example`, DELIBERATELY: FinalCheck.lean's other statement pins are anonymous examples, but this node needs a lean_name that resolves (check_dag rule 3) and an axiom guard of its own (rule 7), so the two pins are named theorems in namespace SocrateAI.ModularForms, following the F3.1-B0 gate-witness precedent at FinalCheck.lean:284. Both carry their own #print axioms guard. lean_name names the SDF-05 pin; the SDF-06 pin is SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized_statement_pin in the same file. DEPENDENCIES. depends_on lists SDF-05 and SDF-06, the two nodes the statement pins restate. The guard half covers all 23 SDF nodes; every one of them is reachable transitively from SDF-05/06 or is itself a leaf already proved (05 -> 04 -> 01, DEF-01; 05 -> 03 -> 02; 06 -> 05; 14 -> 12, 13 -> 07 ... 11; PIN-03 -> 16), and SDF-16 is listed explicitly because it is reachable only through a PIN node, so no node can be guarded before it is proved. SCOPE, so this is not oversold: this node adds ZERO mathematics. Both pins are identities between two explicit finite products of values of Mathlib's ModularForm.eta on the open upper half-plane, already proved as SDF-05 and SDF-06. They say NOTHING about Gamma0(N)-modularity, NOTHING at any cusp, and NOTHING about physics. PHYSICS SCOPE: nothing here formalises any physics; Persson-Volpato (arXiv:1504.07260) is cited elsewhere at the literature (L) tier only and their CHL / axio-dilaton S-duality claim is not a Lean statement anywhere in this library. NAMING: the condition r delta = r(N/delta) is SELF-DUAL (Fricke-symmetric), NEVER 'balanced' -- 'balanced' is reserved in this codebase for exists_balanced_add (F3.2-B1), an unrelated Int.bmod remainder lemma.", "built_from": ["FinalCheck.lean F3.2-A7 guard block (lines 1604-1646) — the guard style", "FinalCheck.lean F32A7Pins PIN 1 (line 1657) — the longhand-pin style, including writing the constant out rather than naming it", "FinalCheck.lean F3.1-B0 gate witness (line 284) — the precedent for a NAMED declaration in FinalCheck.lean so a DAG node's lean_name resolves", "SDF-05 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual)", "SDF-06 (etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual_normalized)", "PNat.pos (for 0 < (N : Nat))", "UpperHalfPlane.2 (for membership in the open upper half-plane)"], "difficulty": "mechanical", "paper_claim": null, "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/FinalCheck.lean"}
# --- Run 7 (FRK-11 statement layer): Fricke eigenspace decomposition + the honest eta-quotient lift. ---
{"id": "FRK-12", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_det_val_pos", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck section Frk1x). theorem frickeW_det_val_pos {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) : 0 < ((frickeW hN).det.val : Real). The Fricke matrix has strictly positive determinant N in the `.det.val` spelling Mathlib's slash and sigma actually use. THIS IS THE SIDE CONDITION THAT PINS sigma TO THE IDENTITY BRANCH rather than complex conjugation: Mathlib defines sigma g = if 0 < g.det.val then id else conj, so every unfolding lemma below (FRK-15, FRK-19b) consumes this hypothesis, and getting it wrong would silently conjugate every scalar. Proof: rw [frickeW_det_val]; exact_mod_cast hN. DECIDE-PINS ADDED THIS RUN, and they sit ABOVE this theorem in the source file so the sign was pinned BEFORE the general lemma was relied on: FRK-28/29/30 evaluate .det.val at the literal levels N = 1, 2, 12 and FRK-31 restates the 0 < _ form at N = 13, each computed straight from frickeMatrix via Matrix.det_fin_two_of and NOT via frickeW_det_val, so a sign slip in frickeMatrix could not be masked by a matching slip in frickeW_det_val. Hand check: det !![0,-1;N,0] = 0*0 - (-1)*N = +N, giving 1, 2, 12 and a positive value at 13; all four agree.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-28", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_det_val_pin_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck section Frk1x). theorem frickeW_det_val_pin_one : ((frickeW (h : 0 < 1)).det.val : Real) = 1. Decide-pin for FRK-12 (sign/definitional discipline). Computed from frickeMatrix directly via Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.val_det_apply, frickeW_coe, frickeMatrix, Matrix.det_fin_two_of and norm_num -- deliberately NOT through frickeW_det_val, so the pin is an INDEPENDENT computation of the determinant rather than a restatement of the general lemma. Hand value: det !![0,-1;1,0] = 0*0 - (-1)*1 = 1.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-29", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_det_val_pin_two", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck section Frk1x). theorem frickeW_det_val_pin_two : ((frickeW (h : 0 < 2)).det.val : Real) = 2. Decide-pin for FRK-12 (sign/definitional discipline). Computed from frickeMatrix directly via Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.val_det_apply, frickeW_coe, frickeMatrix, Matrix.det_fin_two_of and norm_num -- deliberately NOT through frickeW_det_val, so the pin is an INDEPENDENT computation of the determinant rather than a restatement of the general lemma. Hand value: det !![0,-1;2,0] = 0*0 - (-1)*2 = 2.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-30", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_det_val_pin_twelve", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck section Frk1x). theorem frickeW_det_val_pin_twelve : ((frickeW (h : 0 < 12)).det.val : Real) = 12. Decide-pin for FRK-12 (sign/definitional discipline). Computed from frickeMatrix directly via Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.val_det_apply, frickeW_coe, frickeMatrix, Matrix.det_fin_two_of and norm_num -- deliberately NOT through frickeW_det_val, so the pin is an INDEPENDENT computation of the determinant rather than a restatement of the general lemma. Hand value: det !![0,-1;12,0] = 12. Level 12 is pinned here because it is the level the withdrawn extremal eta-quotient document claims, so any later use of W_12 has its determinant fixed by an explicit computation.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-31", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_det_val_pos_pin_thirteen", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck section Frk1x). theorem frickeW_det_val_pos_pin_thirteen : 0 < ((frickeW (h : 0 < 13)).det.val : Real). Decide-pin for FRK-12 (sign/definitional discipline). Computed from frickeMatrix directly via Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.val_det_apply, frickeW_coe, frickeMatrix, Matrix.det_fin_two_of and norm_num -- deliberately NOT through frickeW_det_val, so the pin is an INDEPENDENT computation of the determinant rather than a restatement of the general lemma. Hand value: det !![0,-1;13,0] = 13 > 0. Stated in the STRICT-INEQUALITY shape FRK-12 has, which is syntactically the scrutinee of Mathlib's sigma g = if 0 < g.det.val then id else conj, at N = 13 -- the largest level where this library proves Ligozat. This is the pin that would catch a wrong branch, not merely a wrong value.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-13", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_denom", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded. theorem frickeW_denom {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (tau : H) : denom (frickeW hN) (tau : C) = (N : C) * (tau : C). The automorphy denominator of W_N at tau is N*tau, since W_N = [[0,-1],[N,0]] has bottom row (N, 0). Proof: simp [denom, frickeMatrix].", "paper_claim": null}
# --- FRK-32 .. FRK-36: the five Moebius-action decide-pins for FRK-14. Stated and proved BEFORE the general lemma is relied on; each is an INDEPENDENT numeral computation from frickeMatrix, never a restatement of FRK-14. ---
{"id": "FRK-32", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_smul_pin_two_I", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, FRK-32..FRK-36 section). theorem frickeW_smul_pin_two_I : ((frickeW (h : 0 < 2) . (I : H) : H) : C) = Complex.I / 2. Moebius decide-pin M1 for FRK-14 (sign/definitional discipline on the Moebius action). Evaluated at LITERAL N = 2 and LITERAL tau = i straight from coe_smul_of_det_pos, num, denom and frickeMatrix -- deliberately NOT through frickeW_smul_coe_neg_inv, so a wrong entry in frickeMatrix could not be hidden by a matching wrong sign in the general lemma. Hand value computed first in exact Gaussian rationals: -(1/(2i)) = i/2. DISCRIMINATES the transpose !![0,N;-1,0], which acts by tau -> -N/tau and would give 2i here. Note the determinant side condition is supplied by frickeW_det_val_pos, which is itself pinned independently at four literal levels by FRK-28..FRK-31, so there is no circularity.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-33", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_smul_pin_three_I", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded. theorem frickeW_smul_pin_three_I : ((frickeW (h : 0 < 3) . (I : H) : H) : C) = Complex.I / 3. Moebius decide-pin M2 for FRK-14, computed independently of the general lemma. Hand value: -(1/(3i)) = i/3. MOVES N relative to pin A, so it catches a DROPPED N (tau -> -1/tau would give i here), and it independently discriminates the transpose (which would give 3i).", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-34", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_smul_pin_one_onePlusI", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded. theorem frickeW_smul_pin_one_onePlusI : ((frickeW (h : 0 < 1) . ((1 + I) : H) : H) : C) = (-1 + Complex.I) / 2. Moebius decide-pin M3 for FRK-14, computed independently of the general lemma. Hand value: -(1/(1+i)) = (-1+i)/2. The first pin with a NONZERO REAL PART on both sides, so it catches a b-entry sign flip (!![0,1;N,0], i.e. tau -> +1/(N tau), which would give (1-i)/2 here) and any error invisible on the imaginary axis. It does NOT catch the transpose and does NOT catch a dropped N: at N = 1 all three maps coincide, verified numerically this run. That is why M3 alone would not suffice and why M1/M2/M4/M5 sit at N > 1.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-35", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_smul_pin_two_onePlusI", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded. theorem frickeW_smul_pin_two_onePlusI : ((frickeW (h : 0 < 2) . ((1 + I) : H) : H) : C) = (-1 + Complex.I) / 4. Moebius decide-pin M4 for FRK-14, computed independently of the general lemma. Hand value: -(1/(2+2i)) = (-1+i)/4. The ONLY pin that is simultaneously off the imaginary axis AND at N /= 1, so it separates the transpose (-N/tau = -2/(1+i) = (-1+i), not (-1+i)/4) and the b-flip ((1-i)/4) at the same time.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-36", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_smul_pin_twelve_twoI", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded. theorem frickeW_smul_pin_twelve_twoI : ((frickeW (h : 0 < 12) . ((2*I) : H) : H) : C) = Complex.I / 24. Moebius decide-pin M5 for FRK-14, computed independently of the general lemma. Hand value: -(1/(12 * 2i)) = -(1/(24i)) = i/24. The largest level pinned and the only pin with tau /= i and tau /= 1+i, so it is the one that tests N and tau varying together; a dropped N would give i/2. HONEST NOTE on the tactic: the first attempt left the residual numeral goal 24 = 12 * 2, i.e. the hand value was CONFIRMED against the denominator N*tau = 12*2i that denom actually produced, and one norm_num closed it. The statement was never adjusted.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-14", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_smul_coe_neg_inv", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded. theorem frickeW_smul_coe_neg_inv {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (tau : H) : ((frickeW hN . tau : H) : C) = -(1 / ((N : C) * (tau : C))). The Moebius action of W_N written in EXACTLY the syntactic form etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual (SDF-05) uses for its argument, which is what lets the pointwise eta identity and the slash operator be composed without a hand rewrite. DUPLICATION DISCLOSED, do not count it twice as new content: run 5 already proved this statement up to neg_div as SocrateAI.StringTheory.frickeW_smul_coe (TDUAL-M1), which spells the right-hand side -1/(N tau). That module is deliberately NOT imported here -- it is a physics-namespace file and this is a pure modular-forms file -- so the two-line proof is repeated. NAME DISCIPLINE, learned the hard way this run: the obvious name frickeW_smul_coe collides with TDUAL-M1's on the BASE NAME, and FinalCheck.lean:5200 guards TDUAL-M1 by that base name. With both in scope the guard becomes ambiguous and #print axioms emits BOTH footprints, which turned this run's first lake build red. Hence the _neg_inv suffix; the name is load-bearing. DECIDE-PINS ADDED AND VERIFIED THIS RUN (run 8), BEFORE relying on the general lemma: FRK-32..FRK-36 (frickeW_smul_pin_two_I = i/2, _three_I = i/3, _one_onePlusI = (-1+i)/2, _two_onePlusI = (-1+i)/4, _twelve_twoI = i/24), five INDEPENDENT numeral evaluations of the left-hand side from coe_smul_of_det_pos and frickeMatrix, each compared against a value computed first by hand in exact Gaussian rationals and none of them routed through this theorem. Between them they discriminate the transpose !![0,N;-1,0] (tau -> -N/tau), the b-entry sign flip !![0,1;N,0] (tau -> +1/(N tau)) and a dropped N (tau -> -1/tau). No pin can discriminate W_N from W_N inverse, because W_N^2 = -N*I is scalar and the two induce the same map on H; that is a genuine limit of numeral pinning here and is stated rather than hidden. All five are sorry-free and guarded by base-name match in FinalCheck.", "paper_claim": null}
# --- FRK-37 .. FRK-41: the five SLASH-CONSTANT decide-pins for FRK-15, added run 8. Each evaluates (f |[k] W_N) tau at LITERAL (N,k,tau) from Mathlib's slash_apply and frickeMatrix, with f the constant 1 so the value IS the constant. NOT OVERCLAIMED: because f is constant, sigma is applied to 1 and acts trivially whichever branch it takes, so NONE of these five discriminates the sigma branch -- that is pinned separately by FRK-28..FRK-31, which is the positivity side condition these proofs pass to if_pos (no circularity: those pins come from frickeMatrix, never from FRK-15). ---
{"id": "FRK-37", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_frickeW_const_pin_two_four", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, FRK-37..FRK-41 section). theorem slash_frickeW_const_pin_two_four : ((fun _ => (1:C)) |[(4:Int)] frickeW (h : 0 < 2)) (I : H) = 1/2. SLASH-CONSTANT decide-pin P1 for FRK-15, added run 8. Evaluates Mathlib's |det|^(k-1) * denom^(-k) at LITERAL N=2, k=4, tau=i straight from slash_apply and frickeMatrix -- the proof never mentions slash_frickeW_apply, which is stated BELOW it, so a wrong exponent in the general lemma could not be hidden by a matching wrong exponent here. Hand value 2^3 * (2i)^(-4) = 8/16 = 1/2, re-checked numerically in Python this run. Discriminates det exponent k-1 vs k (which would give 1), denom exponent -k vs +k (128), and a dropped N in denom (8). f is the CONSTANT 1, so the value of the slash IS the constant.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-38", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_frickeW_const_pin_three_two", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, FRK-37..FRK-41 section). theorem slash_frickeW_const_pin_three_two : ((fun _ => (1:C)) |[(2:Int)] frickeW (h : 0 < 3)) (I : H) = -(1/3). SLASH-CONSTANT decide-pin P2 for FRK-15. Hand value 3^1 * (3i)^(-2) = 3/(-9) = -1/3. THE SIGN CONTROL: the only pin whose hand value is NEGATIVE, so a spurious absolute value or a mishandled i^2 shows up here. A dropped N would give -3; det exponent k would give -1. Computed independently of slash_frickeW_apply.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-39", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_frickeW_const_pin_two_three", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, FRK-37..FRK-41 section). theorem slash_frickeW_const_pin_two_three : ((fun _ => (1:C)) |[(3:Int)] frickeW (h : 0 < 2)) (I : H) = I/2. SLASH-CONSTANT decide-pin P3 for FRK-15. ODD weight k=3 and the ONLY pin whose value is NOT REAL, so it is the one that would expose an i-power off by one. Hand value 2^2 * (2i)^(-3) = 4/(-8i) = i/2. Computed independently of slash_frickeW_apply.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-40", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_frickeW_const_pin_five_zero", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, FRK-37..FRK-41 section). theorem slash_frickeW_const_pin_five_zero : ((fun _ => (1:C)) |[(0:Int)] frickeW (h : 0 < 5)) (I : H) = 1/5. SLASH-CONSTANT decide-pin P4 for FRK-15. THE NEGATIVE-EXPONENT CONTROL: the only pin at k=0, where the det exponent k-1 is NEGATIVE and the denominator factor is 1. Hand value 5^(-1) * (5i)^0 = 1/5; if the det exponent were k rather than k-1 the value would be 1, so this pin alone fixes that offset. Computed independently of slash_frickeW_apply.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-41", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_frickeW_const_pin_twelve_two", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, FRK-37..FRK-41 section). theorem slash_frickeW_const_pin_twelve_two : ((fun _ => (1:C)) |[(2:Int)] frickeW (h : 0 < 12)) ((2*I) : H) = -(1/48). SLASH-CONSTANT decide-pin P5 for FRK-15. The largest level pinned and the ONLY pin with tau /= i. Hand value 12^1 * (24i)^(-2) = 12/(-576) = -1/48; det exponent k would give -1/4. Computed independently of slash_frickeW_apply.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-15", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_frickeW_apply", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12", "FRK-13", "FRK-37", "FRK-38", "FRK-39", "FRK-40", "FRK-41"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded. theorem slash_frickeW_apply {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) {k : Int} (f : H -> C) (tau : H) : (f |[k] frickeW hN) tau = f (frickeW hN . tau) * (N : C)^(k-1) * ((N : C)*(tau : C))^(-k). Mathlib's |det|^(k-1) * denom^(-k) normalisation evaluated at the Fricke matrix, with the sigma factor resolved to the identity by FRK-12. Read together with FRK-14 this says (f | W_N)(tau) = N^(-1) tau^(-k) f(-1/(N tau)) -- the exact shape needed to compare Mathlib's slash constant against the eta-quotient eigenvalue lambda, and the reason SDF-17b's eigenvalue is lambda/N and NOT lambda. RUN 8: re-verified end to end (build green, guard present, no sorry in the proof body) and BACKED BY FIVE NEW INDEPENDENT SLASH-CONSTANT DECIDE-PINS FRK-37..FRK-41 at (N,k,tau) = (2,4,i), (3,2,i), (2,3,i), (5,0,i), (12,2,2i), each computed from slash_apply and frickeMatrix without mentioning this lemma, and each agreeing with the hand value.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-16", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeInvolution_const_reconcile", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-10"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded; RE-VERIFIED and STRENGTHENED this run (run 9). theorem frickeInvolution_const_reconcile {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) : ((N:C)^(1-m)) * ((N:C)^(1-m)) * ((((N:R)^2 : R):C)^(2*m-1) * (((-(N:R)) : R):C)^(-(2*m))) = 1. THE constant identity the whole involution rests on: at weight 2*m the square of the normalisation N^(1-m) cancels FRK-10's composite scalar exactly. Proved with NO parity case split -- the exponent -(2*m) is manifestly even, so Even.neg_zpow disposes of the negative base directly, and the rest is zpow_add0 plus one `ring`-checked exponent identity (1-m)+(1-m)+(2*(2*m-1)+-(2*m)) = 0. The proof uses ONLY zpow_two, push_cast, ring, Even.neg_zpow, zpow_mul, zpow_add0 and zpow_zero; it does NOT invoke frickeW_sq_slash. FRK-10 fixes the exponent SHAPE this lemma must consume -- hence the depends_on edge is kept as a conceptual link -- but is not a proof dependency, and any built_from list naming frickeW_sq_slash is wrong. SIX DECIDE-PINS, ALL STATED BEFORE THE GENERAL LEMMA, all sorry-free and all guarded in FinalCheck.lean: frickeInvolution_const_pin_three_two (N=3,m=2); frickeInvolution_const_pin_six_zero (N=6,m=0, the 1-m=+1 end where the normalisation MULTIPLIES -- the pin that fixes the DIRECTION of the exponent, which FRK-10's node text records as previously unfixed); frickeInvolution_const_pin_two_three (N=2,m=3, the 1-m=-2 end where it DIVIDES); frickeInvolution_const_pin_five_negone (N=5,m=-1, NEGATIVE m, so both of FRK-10's exponents flip sign -- the instance that would break if the identity were stated with Nat-exponent pow); frickeInvolution_const_pin_ten_five (N=10,m=5, large numerals, where a wrong POWER of N cannot cancel by luck); and frickeInvolution_const_pin_wrong_direction, the NEGATIVE CONTROL: PIN 6's numbers with the multiplier exponent reversed to m-1 evaluate to 81, and the companion frickeInvolution_const_pin_wrong_direction_ne_one proves 81 != 1, so the mirror-image statement is REFUTED rather than merely unproved and the direction of 1-m is forced, not chosen. All six values were recomputed independently in exact rational arithmetic this run before the Lean pins were written; every one agreed with the Lean statement. SCOPE, stated so this is not read as more than it is: FRK-16 is the SCALAR CANCELLATION LEMMA ONLY. Its hypotheses are {N : Nat}, 0 < N, m : Int and its conclusion is an identity in C -- no ModularForm, no Gamma0GL, no eta quotient, no modularity is assumed anywhere, so it cannot be a relabelling of an unproved bridge (LL-33). hN is genuinely used (hN0 : (N:C) != 0, required for the negative zpow exponents). The Atkin-Lehner involution itself is FRK-11, still open with a sorry; the eigenspace decomposition (FRK-22/23) and every eta-quotient lift (SDF-18 onward) are likewise sorry. FRK-16 makes FRK-11's residue small; it does not close it. NOT VACUOUS AND NOT WITNESS-FREE at this node: the identity has content at every (N,m) with N > 0, six of them exhibited as literal numerals, and the negative control exhibits a neighbouring statement that is FALSE -- so the lemma distinguishes something rather than holding trivially.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-17", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sq_const_simplify", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-10"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (run: FRK-17). theorem frickeW_sq_const_simplify {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (k : Int) : (((N:R)^2 : R):C)^(k-1) * (((-(N:R)) : R):C)^(-k) = (-1:C)^k * (N:C)^(k-2). The spelling change promised in frickeW_sq_slash's own docstring but never proved there, at GENERAL k (not just even k). Needed for the paper's prose and for any statement quantified over k rather than over 2*m. PROOF, and the correction of this node's earlier REMAINING WORK text: NO parity case split is needed and Int.even_or_odd is NOT used. It is true that Mathlib has no general neg_zpow (only Even.neg_zpow / Odd.neg_zpow, re-checked this run by a whole-Mathlib grep, no head), but the negative base never has to be raised to -k in isolation: push_cast turns ((-N : R) : C) into (-1 : C) * (N : C), mul_zpow splits (-1 * N)^(-k) into (-1)^(-k) * N^(-k), and (-1 : C)^(-k) = (-1 : C)^k follows with no case analysis from zpow_neg together with (-1)^k * (-1)^k = ((-1)*(-1))^k = 1^k = 1, i.e. (-1)^k is its own inverse. The rest is zpow_two / push_cast, one _root_.zpow_mul, one zpow_add0 (needs (N:C) != 0, which is exactly hN) and the ring-checked exponent identity 2*(k-1) + (-k) = k-2. NOTE: zpow_neg must be written _root_.zpow_neg inside this file -- Matrix.zpow_neg is in scope and the bare name is ambiguous (this was the only build error). hN IS LOAD-BEARING, PROVED so rather than asserted: frickeW_sq_const_pin_zero_two_false (PIN 17) shows the identity is FALSE at N = 0, k = 2 (LHS = 0^1 * 0^(-2) = 0, RHS = (-1)^2 * 0^0 = 1), so the hypothesis cannot be dropped in any generalisation. PINS, all sorry-free and all guarded in FinalCheck: PINs 1-5 predate the proof -- frickeW_sq_const_pin_two_four (4), pin_three_two (1), pin_two_three (-2, the ODD-k SIGN CONTROL: dropping the (-1)^k factor gives +2 here), pin_six_twelve (60466176 = 6^10), pin_five_zero (1/25, the NEGATIVE-EXPONENT control that would break if the identity were stated with Nat-exponent pow). PIN 4 was ONE-SIDED (it pinned only the left-hand expression to a numeral and said nothing about the right), so this run added frickeW_sq_const_pin_six_twelve_rhs (PIN 12) supplying the matching right-hand half at the same (N,k) = (6,12), plus four further INDEPENDENTLY computed two-sided instances: pin_one_negthree ((1,-3) -> -1, odd AND negative k), pin_twelve_two ((12,2) -> 1, a composite non-prime-power level), pin_seven_negone ((7,-1) -> -1/343), pin_nine_five ((9,5) -> -729, odd k with large numerals where a wrong power of N cannot cancel by luck) with its companion pin_nine_five_value fixing that value to the numeral -729. All ten values were recomputed this run in exact rationals before any Lean was written and all ten agreed on both sides. SCOPE, stated so nobody overstates it: FRK-17 is NOT on the critical path to the eigenspace decomposition -- the even-weight involution goes through FRK-16 (frickeInvolution_const_reconcile), whose exponent -(2*m) is manifestly even, and which does not use this lemma. FRK-17 buys generality in k and the paper's prose spelling only. It does NOT claim the eigenspace decomposition itself (FRK-11 / FRK-23 remain open) and assumes NO modularity anywhere: it is pure zpow arithmetic in C, so there is no LL-33 hollow-bridge exposure in it.", "paper_claim": null, "built_from": ["SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sq_slash", "mul_zpow", "zpow_neg", "zpow_add₀", "zpow_two"]}
{"id": "FRK-18", "kind": "def", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeInvolution", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-09"], "statement_nl": "PROVED as a DEFINITION and RE-VERIFIED THIS RUN (run 8) by a full `lake build` (3790 jobs, 'Build completed successfully') plus `#print axioms SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeInvolution` = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -- NO sorryAx, so the def elaborates and nothing in its elaboration reaches an unproved auxiliary. noncomputable def frickeInvolution {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m) -> ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m) := fun f => ((N : C)^(1-m)) . frickeModularOperator hN f. THE WEIGHT IS INDEXED AS 2*m, NEVER AS k WITH AN Even k HYPOTHESIS, so the normalising exponent 1-m is a literal integer-linear expression and no Int division k/2 ever appears in the library. Uses Mathlib's complex scalar action ModularForm.instSMulC, available because Gamma0GL N = (Gamma0 N).map (mapGL R) carries the HasDetOne instance. WHY THE MULTIPLIER IS N^(1-m), now PINNED rather than asserted (added this run, FrickeEigenspace.lean section MultiplierPins, five decide-pins, all norm_num, all guarded): Mathlib's slash carries |det|^(k-1)*denom^(-k), which at W_N is N^(k-1)*(N*tau)^(-k) = N^(-1)*tau^(-k), while classical Atkin-Lehner is N^(-k/2)*tau^(-k); the converting factor is N^(1-k/2) = N^(1-m) at k=2m. Written with no Int division that is N^(-m) = N^(1-m)*N^(-1), and PINs 18-21 state exactly that instance together with the literal value of BOTH sides at (N,m) = (4,1) [1-m=0, multiplier trivial, value 1/4], (9,3) [1-m=-2, multiplier divides, value 1/729], (7,0) [1-m=1, multiplier multiplies, value 1], (5,-2) [NEGATIVE m, weight -4, value 25]. PIN 22 is a NEGATIVE CONTROL: the mirror-image multiplier N^(1+m) gives 9^4*9^(-1) = 729 at (9,3) where the classical constant is 1/729, and the pin proves 729 != 1/729, so the sign of m in the exponent is REFUTED-IF-WRONG, not merely unchecked. GUARDED: frickeInvolution itself now carries a #guard_msgs #print axioms guard in FinalCheck.lean (section Frk1x), following FRK-09's frickeModularOperator precedent, even though check_dag rule 7 exempts kind == 'def'; the five pins are guarded too. A TRIPWIRE guard was added in the same block asserting frickeInvolution_sq (FRK-11) still depends on sorryAx, so proving FRK-11 will FAIL THE BUILD until that guard is edited. NOT INCLUDED IN THIS NODE, and this node must not be read as progress on them: the @[simp] unfolding companion frickeInvolution_apply and the involution property frickeInvolution_sq are BOTH still sorry and belong to FRK-11's remaining work. A def has no mathematical content beyond its type.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-19", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator_smul", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12", "FRK-47"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10), all three declarations. (a) frickeModularOperator_add: additivity, from SlashAction.add_slash plus ModularForm.ext. (b) frickeModularOperator_smul (c : C): complex homogeneity -- the node's lean_name. (c) frickeModularOperator_smul_pin_I: the same statement at the NON-REAL scalar c = I, kept as a separate named declaration with its own guard so the non-real case cannot be lost if (b) is ever restated at real scalars. WHY (c) EXISTS: Mathlib's ModularForm.smul_slash reads (c . f) |[k] A = sigma A c . (f |[k] A), and sigma A is COMPLEX CONJUGATION when det A < 0. For A = W_N the determinant is +N > 0 (FRK-12, pinned at four literal levels by FRK-28..FRK-31), so the identity branch is correct -- but at a REAL scalar the two branches agree, so a wrong branch is invisible at the only scalar FRK-11 actually uses. The resolution is now factored out as FRK-47 (frickeW_sigma_apply) and pinned at non-real scalars by FRK-42..FRK-46, with negative controls. Each of the three declarations carries its own #print axioms guard; all print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. BUILT_FROM CORRECTION (run 11, verified by grep in Mathlib/NumberTheory/ModularForms/SlashActions.lean): the ingredient is the SlashAction CLASS FIELD `SlashAction.add_slash` (declared at line 41, given @[simp] at line 53), NOT `ModularForm.add_slash` -- that name is `private theorem add_slash` at line 114 inside `section privateSlash` (opened at 86, closed at 137, under `set_option backward.privateInPublic true`) and is UNREFERENCEABLE from this library; the landed proof uses the public class field. `ModularForm.smul_slash` IS public (line 147). TYPING PREREQUISITE the statement string omits: `c • f` at `c : C` does not typecheck over an arbitrary `Gamma : Subgroup (GL (Fin 2) R)`. Mathlib's real-scalar `instSMulR` (Basic.lean:247) cannot take alpha = C, so the only route is `instSMulC` (Basic.lean:270), which carries `[Gamma.HasDetOne]`, as does the `Module C` structure (Basic.lean:327). It resolves here only because `Gamma0GL N` is the abbrev `(Gamma0 N).map (mapGL R)` (FrickeSlash.lean:25) and Mathlib supplies `instance ... : HasDetOne (Gamma.map <| mapGL S)` (ArithmeticSubgroups.lean:59). Restated over a bare subgroup of GL(2,R) this node would be ILL-TYPED rather than false. ODD-k VACUITY (stated once here so no reader has to rediscover it): the node is stated at general k : Z and is true there, but for ODD k every instance is vacuous in the strong sense -- the module itself is ZERO, via `neg_one_mem_Gamma0GL` (FrickeEigenspace.lean:976) plus Mathlib's `ModularForm.eq_zero_of_neg_one_mem` (Basic.lean:231). The EVEN-k instances, which FRK-20a consumes at weight 2*m, are the entire content. SCOPE HONESTY: this is linearity ONLY -- the cheapest of the four classical Atkin-Lehner facts about W_N on M_k(Gamma0(N)). W_N^2 = id is FRK-11; Petersson self-adjointness and commutation with T_p for p not dividing N are NOT in this library and are claimed by no node -- they are the honest next obstructions for a full Atkin-Lehner package. RE-VERIFIED run 11: `lake build SocrateAI` -> `Build completed successfully (3770 jobs).`; `lake build SocrateAI.FinalCheck` -> `Build completed successfully (3721 jobs).`; no `sorry` in lines 834-869.", "paper_claim": null, "built_from": ["SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator", "ModularForm.smul_slash", "SlashAction.add_slash", "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sigma_apply"]}
{"id": "FRK-20", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeInvolutionLM_sq", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-11", "FRK-19"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10). (a) noncomputable def frickeInvolutionLM {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) : Module.End C (ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)) with toFun := frickeInvolution hN m; its two LINEARITY FIELDS map_add' and map_smul' -- which were the reason this node was open, and the reason frickeInvolutionLM_apply was deliberately left unguarded in run 8 -- are now discharged from FRK-19a and FRK-19b plus smul_add / smul_comm. (b) frickeInvolutionLM_sq : (frickeInvolutionLM hN m) * (frickeInvolutionLM hN m) = 1, the node's lean_name, proved by LinearMap.ext and FRK-11. This is what makes the eigenspaces Submodules rather than bare predicates. #print axioms on frickeInvolutionLM, frickeInvolutionLM_apply and frickeInvolutionLM_sq all print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]; all three are guarded. RE-VERIFIED RUN 12 (commands run this cycle, counts recomputed not carried forward): `pgrep -x lake` -> none (sole builder); `python3 scripts/disk_guard.py` -> disk free 27.01 GB, OK; `lake build SocrateAI.FinalCheck --packages=local-packages.json` -> `Build completed successfully (3721 jobs).` with NO `sorry` warning for FrickeEigenspace lines 869-900 (the file's 9 sorry warnings are all in the still-open SDF-17..SDF-20 block, lines 1093-1241). FinalCheck.lean now carries 1210 `#print axioms` guard lines (NOT the 1122 quoted in older briefs); check_dag reports 146 nodes (5 blocked, 7 open, 134 proved) (NOT the 104 quoted in older briefs). Because the build succeeded, the three `#guard_msgs` guards at FinalCheck.lean:8611-8618 (frickeInvolutionLM, frickeInvolutionLM_apply, frickeInvolutionLM_sq) all actually matched [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] this run -- a stale expected-axiom string would have failed the build. KIND CORRECTED THIS RUN: `def` -> `math`. The node's lean_name `frickeInvolutionLM_sq` is a THEOREM, and check_dag rule 7 exempts kind == 'def' from the guard requirement, so the theorem half of this node was previously protected by convention rather than by the checker. No guard was actually missing; the checker now enforces it. NORMALISATION IS A THEOREM HERE, NOT A CONVENTION: Mathlib's slash carries |det g|^(k-1) * denom(g,tau)^(-k), which at W_N is N^(-1)*tau^(-k); classical Atkin-Lehner is N^(-k/2)*tau^(-k)*f(-1/(N tau)). The converting factor N^(1-k/2) is exactly the definition's N^(1-m) at k = 2m, and FRK-48 (frickeInvolution_apply_classical, FrickeEigenspace.lean:818) PROVES the classical form. The instance N^(-m) = N^(1-m) * N^(-1) is decide-pinned at literal numerals by PINs 18-22 (FrickeEigenspace.lean:727-758) at (N,m) = (4,1), (9,3), (7,0), (5,-2), each pin also asserting the literal VALUE of both sides so no pin is a tautology between unevaluated expressions, plus frickeInvolution_mult_pin_wrong_dir refuting the mirror multiplier N^(1+m). NO HIDDEN MODULARITY (LL-33 axis, checked): f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m) is a hypothesis on Mathlib's bundled type; no eta quotient, no Ligozat, no N in {1,2,3,4,5,7,13} restriction and no ETA-01 dependency enters the statement or the proof. TYPING PREREQUISITE the statement string omits: `Module.End C M` needs `Module C M`, which Mathlib supplies only under [Gamma.HasDetOne] (Basic.lean:327, instSMulC at :270); it resolves here because Gamma0GL N is the abbrev (Gamma0 N).map (SpecialLinearGroup.mapGL R) (FrickeSlash.lean:25-26). Over a bare subgroup of GL(2,R) this node would be ILL-TYPED rather than false. SCOPE DELTAS vs the classical reference, none of them misstatements: (D1) CUSP FORMS ARE NOT COVERED -- Mathlib's CuspForm is a separate type with its own Module C instance (Basic.lean:521); no node gives an endomorphism of it, so the cusp-form eigenspace decomposition is NOT a corollary of anything in this library today. (D2) ONLY TWO OF THE FOUR classical W_N facts are delivered: linearity (FRK-19) and involutivity (FRK-11/FRK-20). Petersson self-adjointness and commutation with T_p for p not dividing N are ABSENT and claimed by no node -- prose must not call this 'the Atkin-Lehner theory'; the honest name is 'the Fricke involution as a module endomorphism'. (D3) The identification M_k(Gamma0(N)) ~= ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) k is USED, not proved, in this library. (D4) NON-DEGENERACY IS ONE-SIDED: FRK-27c exhibits ModularForm.const 1 in frickePlus but not in frickeMinus at every N > 0, so the two eigenspaces are demonstrably DIFFERENT; but NO NONZERO element of frickeMinus is exhibited at any level anywhere in this library (the only offered route, SDF-20, is still sorry). NOT VACUOUS in the module sense at even weight 2*m, and the odd-weight vacuity is EXHIBITED not assumed (neg_one_mem_Gamma0GL at :976 plus Mathlib's ModularForm.eq_zero_of_neg_one_mem, giving modularForm_odd_weight_subsingleton at :994); but the MINUS eigenspace is witness-free and this node must be reported as such.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-21", "kind": "def", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickePlus", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-20"], "statement_nl": "PROVED (as defs) AND GUARDED (run 10). noncomputable def frickePlus {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) : Submodule C (ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)) := LinearMap.ker (frickeInvolutionLM hN m - 1), and frickeMinus := LinearMap.ker (frickeInvolutionLM hN m + 1). These were already defs with real bodies in run 8, but they rested on FRK-20, whose linearity fields were sorry -- so a #print axioms on either would have printed sorryAx. It no longer does: both now print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], and both are guarded even though check_dag rule 7 exempts kind == 'def'. A def has no mathematical content beyond its type; the content is FRK-22 (membership) and FRK-23 (the decomposition).", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-22", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeEigenspace_mem_iff", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-21"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED, all three declarations; RE-VERIFIED THIS RUN (run 11) and the BOOKKEEPING GAP CLOSED. The node asserts TWO theorems: frickePlus_mem_iff : f in frickePlus hN m <-> frickeInvolution hN m f = f, and frickeMinus_mem_iff : f in frickeMinus hN m <-> frickeInvolution hN m f = -f, both {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)). Both are mechanical (LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.sub_apply / add_apply, sub_eq_zero / add_eq_zero_iff_eq_neg, then Iff.rfl -- the bare frickeInvolution and the bundled frickeInvolutionLM are the same term by frickeInvolutionLM_apply, so no coercion gap hides in the iff). Membership is unfolded to the concrete eigenvector equation so downstream users never reason through LinearMap.ker. WHY THE lean_name CHANGED (run 11): check_dag verifies a node by base-name match on a SINGLE lean_name, so the previous value (frickePlus_mem_iff) left frickeMinus_mem_iff unverified by the DAG gate -- half of what this node asserts. The node now resolves to frickeEigenspace_mem_iff (FRK-22c), a conjunction of the two iffs whose #print axioms covers BOTH halves, so a sorry in either would surface at the guard. All three declarations remain separately guarded in FinalCheck.lean and all three print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. FRK-22c adds NO mathematical content; it is bookkeeping, and is labelled as such in the source. SIGN ORIENTATION IS NOT ASSUMED: the plus/minus labels are refuted-if-swapped, not merely stated -- FRK-27a/b consume BOTH iffs to place ModularForm.const 1 IN frickePlus hN 0 and OUT of frickeMinus hN 0 at every N > 0, and that pair of proofs fails outright if the two iffs are exchanged. NOT VACUOUS at this node: both directions of both iffs are actually consumed downstream (FRK-23, FRK-27). NO HIDDEN MODULARITY (LL-33 axis, checked by grep over the region this run): f is a hypothesis on Mathlib's bundled ModularForm type; no etaQuotient, no Ligozat, no IsFrickeSelfDual, no N in {1,2,3,4,5,7,13} restriction appears in the statement or its proof. SCOPE, so this is not read as more: ModularForm only -- Mathlib's CuspForm is a separate type with its own Module instance and no node gives an endomorphism of it, so the classical S_k(Gamma0(N))^+- eigenspace is NOT a corollary. Only the involution/linearity half of Atkin-Lehner theory is present; Petersson self-adjointness of W_N and commutation with T_p (p not dividing N) are absent and claimed by no node. Weight is fixed to even 2*m; odd weight is not a gap but is PROVED vacuous (FRK-24, modularForm_odd_weight_subsingleton). THE NORMALISATION IS NOW PINNED TO THE CLASSICAL ONE: see FRK-50, which composes this node with FRK-48 to show membership is exactly N^(-k/2) tau^(-k) f(W_N . tau) = +- f(tau); prose must cite FRK-50 (or FRK-48) whenever it calls these the Atkin-Lehner eigenspaces, since frickeInvolution is defined through Mathlib's GL-slash multiplier N^(1-m), not through the classical N^(-k/2).", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-23", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.fricke_isCompl", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-11", "FRK-22"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10) -- THE EIGENSPACE DECOMPOSITION, in BOTH forms. (a) fricke_decomposition {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)) : exists fp in frickePlus hN m, exists fm in frickeMinus hN m, f = fp + fm -- the existential half, proved by the explicit projections fp = (1/2) . (f + T f), fm = (1/2) . (f - T f) with T = frickeInvolutionLM; membership is FRK-22 + FRK-11 + FRK-20's linearity, the sum is smul arithmetic in characteristic zero. (b) fricke_isCompl : IsCompl (frickePlus hN m) (frickeMinus hN m) -- the node's lean_name and the SHARP form. Codisjointness is (a); disjointness is T f = f and T f = -f => (2:C) . f = 0 => f = 0, using smul_eq_zero and (2:C) != 0. (b) IS STRICTLY STRONGER THAN (a) AND MUST NOT BE REPORTED AS IT: (a) alone permits overlap. Both are guarded separately for exactly that reason. NOT VACUOUS: FRK-27c exhibits an element of frickePlus that is not in frickeMinus at every level N > 0 in weight 0, so the two summands are demonstrably different. NOT SETTLED: no nonzero element of frickeMinus is exhibited at any level, so the decomposition is not shown to be non-degenerate in the minus direction; the only route offered to such an element is SDF-20, still open.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-24", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.modularForm_odd_weight_subsingleton", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10), all three declarations -- THE VACUITY FINDING, checked rather than assumed. (a) neg_one_mem_Gamma0GL (N : Nat) : (-1 : GL (Fin 2) R) in Gamma0GL N, proved by EXHIBITING (-1 : SL(2,Z)) -- whose lower-left entry is 0, hence 0 mod N, so Gamma0_mem applies -- and checking entrywise (fin_cases on both indices) that mapGL R sends it to (-1 : GL (Fin 2) R). The run brief required this to be verified before the vacuity claim could be relied on; it is, and it holds at every N with no hypothesis on N. (b) modularForm_odd_weight_eq_zero (hk : Odd k) (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) k) : f = 0, from Mathlib's ModularForm.eq_zero_of_neg_one_mem applied to (a). (c) modularForm_odd_weight_subsingleton (hk : Odd k) : Subsingleton (ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) k) -- the node's lean_name. CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly because the run brief demands it: for ODD weight the module is a singleton, so ANY eigenspace statement about it is vacuously true and worth nothing. That is why every result in the FRK block is indexed by the EVEN weight 2*m, and why the even case is the only headline. All three guarded; all print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. DECIDE-PINS (added run 12, RE-VERIFIED, all nine guarded in FinalCheck.lean and all printing [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]): the vacuity mechanism has exactly two moving parts and each is now pinned INDEPENDENTLY of the general proof. (i) -1 really is in Gamma0GL N -- FRK-51 checks by decide that the lower-left entry of (-1 : SL(2,Z)) is 0; FRK-52 and FRK-53 re-prove membership at the COMPOSITE level N = 12 and at the degenerate N = 0 WITHOUT calling neg_one_mem_Gamma0GL. (ii) the automorphy factor at -1 is denom(-1,z)^(-k) = (-1)^k -- FRK-54 computes denom (-1) z = -1 from the definition, FRK-55 and FRK-56 pin (-1)^k = -1 at k = 3 and at the negative odd k = -5 (the zpow-not-pow control), and FRK-57 is the NEGATIVE CONTROL at the even k = 4, where the value is +1 != -1 and the argument correctly proves nothing. FRK-58/FRK-59 are instance pins of the general theorem at (12,3) and (1,-7). SCOPE, so prose does not overstate: there is NO nebentypus version (this library carries the trivial character only, so 'odd-weight forms vanish' must not be written in the character sense chi(-1) = (-1)^k), and NOTHING is claimed about CuspForm, which is a separate bundled type in Mathlib -- the classical S_k(Gamma0(N)) = 0 for odd k is NOT a corollary of this node as stated. Both are honest gaps, not errors.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-25", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator_const_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-15", "FRK-21"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED, both declarations, and PINNED at five literal levels (run 12). (a) frickeModularOperator_const_one {N} (hN : 0 < N) : frickeModularOperator hN (ModularForm.const 1) = ((N:C)^(-1)) . ModularForm.const 1 -- the node's lean_name, direct from FRK-15 (slash_frickeW_apply): const 1 is constant so the f (W_N . tau) factor is 1, and k = 0 collapses the two zpow factors to N^(-1) * (N tau)^0. Mathlib's ModularForm.const x [Gamma.HasDetOne] : ModularForm Gamma 0 is a modular form at EVERY level UNCONDITIONALLY, so no etaQuotient, no Ligozat, no N in {1,2,3,4,5,7,13} restriction and no modularity hypothesis enters -- the LL-33 hollow-bridge axis is clean here. (b) const_one_ne_zero : ModularForm.const 1 != 0, by evaluating at <I, _> : H. Without (b) the witness would be empty, which is why it is a separate guarded declaration. Both print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. THIS NODE DOES NOT ASSERT frickePlus hN 0 != bot. An earlier draft of the node claimed that as half (b) and cited a scratch file for it; no declaration of that name existed anywhere in the library, and the statement is NOT derivable from this node's dependencies -- it additionally needs the membership criterion FRK-22a and the fixed-point fact FRK-26, and FRK-26 depends on FRK-25, so putting it here would make the DAG circular. It is now proved downstream as FRK-66 (frickePlus_ne_bot). THE N^(-1) IS A MATHLIB-SLASH ARTIFACT, NOT THE CLASSICAL CONSTANT: Mathlib's raw GL(2,R) slash carries |det|^(k-1) * denom^(-k), whereas the classical Atkin-Lehner operator carries N^(-k/2) * tau^(-k) and sends 1 |-> 1 at weight 0 with NO N^(-1). So the sentence 'the Fricke operator fixes the constant 1' is FALSE of frickeModularOperator and becomes true only after the N^(1-m) renormalisation of FRK-18 -- see FRK-26, and FRK-48/FRK-50 for the reconciliation with the classical normalisation. FRK-64 pins this negatively in Lean. Prose must never call half (a) an Atkin-Lehner statement citing FRK-25a alone. WEAKER THAN THE CLASSICAL REFERENCE, and labelled so: the classical statement is the involution plus the direct-sum decomposition of M_k(Gamma_0(N)) with Petersson self-adjointness and T_p-commutation, which lives at FRK-11/FRK-22/FRK-23, not here. This node is a weight-0 non-vacuity witness, and m = 0 is precisely where the decomposition is DEGENERATE (the -1 eigenspace is classically zero there). Classically it is a triviality. DEPENDENCY NOTE: FRK-21 is listed as a PROSE-ONLY dependency (the node's statement_nl uses the eigenspace vocabulary); neither proof (a) nor (b) invokes it. The load-bearing dependency is FRK-15 plus Mathlib.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-26", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeInvolution_const_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-18", "FRK-25"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10). frickeInvolution_const_one {N} (hN : 0 < N) : frickeInvolution hN 0 (ModularForm.const 1) = ModularForm.const 1. The normalised involution FIXES the constant 1 at weight 0 at EVERY level, because the normalisation N^(1-0) = N cancels FRK-25a's N^(-1) exactly (smul_smul, zpow_one, mul_inv_cancel0 with (N:C) != 0 from hN). This is the +1-eigenform that makes FRK-27 possible. Guarded; prints [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-27", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickePlus_ne_frickeMinus", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-22", "FRK-26"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10), all three declarations -- THE NON-VACUITY WITNESS the run brief demanded, and it is now exhibited rather than promised. (a) const_one_mem_frickePlus : ModularForm.const 1 in frickePlus hN 0, from FRK-22a and FRK-26. (b) const_one_not_mem_frickeMinus : ModularForm.const 1 NOT in frickeMinus hN 0 -- membership would give const 1 = -const 1 via FRK-22b and FRK-26, hence (2:C) . const 1 = 0, hence const 1 = 0 by smul_eq_zero and (2:C) != 0, contradicting FRK-25b. (c) frickePlus_ne_frickeMinus : frickePlus hN 0 != frickeMinus hN 0 -- the node's lean_name. UNCONDITIONAL and at EVERY level N > 0: no eta quotient, no Ligozat, no modularity hypothesis is used anywhere in (a), (b) or (c). THE HONEST LIMIT, so this is not overstated downstream: the witness separates the two eigenspaces by exhibiting an element of the FIRST that is not in the SECOND. It does NOT exhibit a nonzero element of frickeMinus, at this or any level, and no such element exists anywhere in this library. It does NOT prove frickeMinus hN 0 = bot either (expected, but unproved). A -1-eigenform of the Fricke involution is the next obstruction; the only route offered to one is SDF-20, still sorry.", "paper_claim": null}
# --- Run 11 (SDF-21 .. SDF-24): the EIGEN-SLASH pins for SDF-17b.  Until run 11 the slash half of SDF-17 had NO decide-pin at all; these eight lemmas instantiate its WHOLE implication at three literal eigenfunctions and refute the mirror constant N*lam at two of them.  Stated ABOVE the general lemma in the source file. ---
{"id": "SDF-21", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_eigen_pin_const", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12", "FRK-15"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, SDF-17 section). EIGEN-SLASH PIN E1 for SDF-17b, stated ABOVE it in the same module so Lean's scoping -- not a comment -- enforces that it does not consume the lemma it pins. TWO lemmas, both guarded: slash_eigen_pin_const_hyp (tau : H) : (fun _ => (1:C)) (frickeW (0<2) . tau) = 1 * tau^(0:Int) * (fun _ => (1:C)) tau, which DISCHARGES SDF-17b's hypothesis for f = 1, N = 2, k = 0, lam = 1 at EVERY tau; and slash_eigen_pin_const : ((fun _ => (1:C)) |[(0:Int)] frickeW (0<2)) (I : H) = ((2:C)^{-1} * 1) * 1 = 1/2. Hand value, computed first: 2^(0-1) * (2i)^0 = 1/2. Proved from Mathlib's slash_apply and frickeMatrix directly; the proof does NOT mention slash_frickeW_of_eigen. WHAT IT DISCRIMINATES: N vs N^{-1} in SDF-17b's constant (N would give 2). It does NOT discriminate the sigma branch -- f is constant, so sigma acts trivially whichever branch is taken; that branch is pinned separately by FRK-28..FRK-31 and FRK-42..FRK-46.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "SDF-22", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_eigen_pin_id", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12", "FRK-14", "FRK-15"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, SDF-17 section). EIGEN-SLASH PIN E2 for SDF-17b, stated ABOVE it. TWO lemmas, both guarded: slash_eigen_pin_id_hyp (tau : H) : ((frickeW (0<3) . tau : H) : C) = (-(1/3)) * tau^(-2:Int) * tau, discharging SDF-17b's hypothesis for f = (tau |-> tau), N = 3, k = -2, lam = -1/3 at EVERY tau (via FRK-14 and tau != 0); and slash_eigen_pin_id : ((fun tau => (tau:C)) |[(-2:Int)] frickeW (0<3)) (I : H) = ((3:C)^{-1} * (-(1/3))) * I = -I/9. Hand value, computed first in exact Gaussian rationals: f(W_3 . i) = -1/(3i) = i/3; 3^(-2-1) = 1/27; (3i)^2 = -9; product = -i/9. THE ONLY PIN OF THE THREE AT NEGATIVE WEIGHT, the only one with a NON-CONSTANT f, and the only one whose value is not real -- so a zpow slip that a k.toNat-style proof would hide shows up here.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "SDF-23", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_eigen_pin_inv", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12", "FRK-14", "FRK-15"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, SDF-17 section). EIGEN-SLASH PIN E3 for SDF-17b, stated ABOVE it. TWO lemmas, both guarded: slash_eigen_pin_inv_hyp (tau : H) : ((frickeW (0<2) . tau : H) : C)^{-1} = (-2) * tau^(2:Int) * (tau:C)^{-1}, discharging SDF-17b's hypothesis for f = (tau |-> tau^{-1}), N = 2, k = 2, lam = -2 at EVERY tau; and slash_eigen_pin_inv : ((fun tau => (tau:C)^{-1}) |[(2:Int)] frickeW (0<2)) (I : H) = ((2:C)^{-1} * (-2)) * I^{-1} = I. Hand value, computed first: f(W_2 . i) = (i/2)^{-1} = -2i; 2^(2-1) = 2; (2i)^(-2) = -1/4; product = i. POSITIVE weight and |lam| > 1, so unlike E1 the N^{-1} is dividing something other than 1 and a wrong power of N cannot cancel by luck. LIMIT STATED RATHER THAN HIDDEN: for f = tau^j the eigen relation forces k = -2j, so E1/E2/E3 reach EVEN k only. No ODD-k instance of SDF-17b is pinned and none is claimed. That costs nothing at the point of use (SDF-17c and SDF-18 consume SDF-17b at k = 2*m only) and the general proof is parity-free.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "SDF-24", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.slash_eigen_pin_const_wrong_direction", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-21", "SDF-23"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and guarded (FinalCheck, SDF-17 section). THE TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS for SDF-17b's constant: the mirror-image statement with N in place of N^{-1} is REFUTED, not merely unproved, so the direction of the N is forced by a proof and not chosen by convention. slash_eigen_pin_const_wrong_direction : ((fun _ => (1:C)) |[(0:Int)] frickeW (0<2)) (I : H) != ((2:C) * 1) * 1 -- the value is 1/2, the mirror constant would be 2. slash_eigen_pin_inv_wrong_direction : ((fun tau => (tau:C)^{-1}) |[(2:Int)] frickeW (0<2)) (I : H) != ((2:C) * (-2)) * I^{-1} -- the value is i, the mirror constant would give 4i. Both are guarded in FinalCheck under their own names; the node's lean_name is the first. Each is proved by rewriting with its own positive pin (SDF-21, SDF-23) and then a numeral disequality, so neither can be satisfied by a matching error in the general lemma.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "SDF-17", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.etaQuotientH_slash_frickeW_selfDual", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-14", "FRK-15", "SDF-05", "SDF-21", "SDF-22", "SDF-23", "SDF-24"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 11); the id is REUSED, not duplicated, and its depends_on [FRK-14, FRK-15, SDF-05] is unchanged. FOUR declarations, all in Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean, and NOT ONE of them mentions ModularForm -- that is the point of the node, not an accident: (a) etaQuotientH_frickeW_smul (hN : 0 < N) (hr : IsFrickeSelfDual N r) (hk : sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2*k) (tau : H) : etaQuotientH N r (frickeW hN . tau) = frickeEigenvalue N k * tau^k * etaQuotientH N r tau -- run 6's SDF-05 with the argument rewritten by FRK-14 into the GL(2,R) action; a statement about the FUNCTION etaQuotientH N r : H -> C. Proof: unfold etaQuotientH; rw [frickeW_smul_coe_neg_inv]; exact etaQuotient_fricke_selfDual hN hr hk tau.2. (b) slash_frickeW_of_eigen (hN : 0 < N) (lam : C) (f : H -> C) (hf : forall tau, f (frickeW hN . tau) = lam * tau^k * f tau) : f |[k] frickeW hN = ((N:C)^{-1} * lam) . f -- THE CONSTANT RECONCILIATION. f is a BARE function; the statement consumes no holomorphy, no Gamma0(N)-invariance, no growth condition, and it is deliberately NOT stated on ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) k, because that module is the ZERO module at odd k (modularForm_odd_weight_eq_zero, FRK-24b) and the bundled form of this statement would be VACUOUS at every odd weight. THE SLASH EIGENVALUE IS lam/N, NOT lam: frickeEigenvalue's lambda is defined by f(-1/(Nz)) = lambda z^k f(z), while Mathlib's slash carries |det|^(k-1) * denom^(-k), which at W_N is N^(k-1)*(N tau)^(-k) = N^(-1) tau^(-k) (FRK-15). Proof: funext; slash_frickeW_apply; hf; mul_zpow; two zpow_add0 cancellations needing (N:C) != 0 and (tau:C) != 0 (UpperHalfPlane.ne_zero). NO parity case split on k occurs. (c) etaQuotientH_slash_frickeW_selfDual : (etaQuotientH N r) |[k] frickeW hN = ((N:C)^{-1} * frickeEigenvalue N k) . (etaQuotientH N r) -- (a) and (b) composed, one line, still purely about the function. THIS IS THE NODE'S RESOLVING lean_name, so a #print axioms on it reports the footprint of (a), (b) and (c) together. (d) frickeEigenvalue_normalised_even (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) : (N:C)^(1-m) * ((N:C)^{-1} * frickeEigenvalue N (2*m)) = (-1:C)^m. NAME AND FACTOR ORDER ARE THE PRE-EXISTING ONES and are load-bearing: the four already-proved pins frickeEigenvalue_normalised_pin_* anchor on the _normalised_ stem, and this library has already been burned once by a base-name collision (FRK-14 vs TDUAL-M1's frickeW_smul_coe). (d) is guarded in FinalCheck under its OWN name -- it is NOT in (c)'s axiom footprint, and that is disclosed rather than glossed. PROOF ROUTE ACTUALLY TAKEN FOR (d), recorded because it is NOT the one the -- OPEN: note proposed: -(2*m) = (-2)*m, so I^(-(2m)) = (I^(-2))^m = (-1)^m by zpow_mul alone. SDF-07's I_zpow_emod and I_zpow_neg_eq_neg_one_iff are therefore NOT invoked; any built_from list naming them is wrong for this node as proved. The real square root uses 0 < N genuinely: sqrt((N:R)^(2m)) = sqrt(((N:R)^m)^2) = (N:R)^m because (N:R)^m > 0. PINS, ALL STATED AND PROVED BEFORE THE GENERAL LEMMAS. For (d), the four pre-existing frickeEigenvalue_normalised_pin_* (N=6 k=12 -> +1; N=1 k=2 -> -1, the MINUS side; N=6 k=0, fixing the direction of the exponent; N=6 k=-12, the negative-weight control). For (b), which until run 11 had NO pin at all, the EIGHT NEW slash_eigen_pin_* of SDF-21..SDF-24. VACUITY AND WITNESS, stated plainly: nothing in SDF-17 is vacuous -- every declaration has content at every N > 0 and, for (b), at every k, and the two negative controls exhibit neighbouring statements that are FALSE. But SDF-17 exhibits NO -1-eigenform: (c)'s eigenvalue is N^{-1} * frickeEigenvalue N k, and no instance is produced anywhere in this library at which the normalised value is -1 on a nonzero form. The only route to one is SDF-20, still sorry, with undischarged hypotheses. That remains the next obstruction and is reported as one. SCOPE, so this is not oversold: SDF-17 says NOTHING about Gamma0(N)-modularity of any eta quotient. The declarations that take modularity -- SDF-18a/b/c, SDF-19, SDF-20 -- are still sorry, and the FinalCheck sorryAx TRIPWIRE that sat on etaQuotientH_frickeW_smul FIRED as designed when SDF-17 landed and has been moved to frickeInvolution_eq_of_etaQuotient (SDF-18a), the first of those five. NO PHYSICS: no declaration or docstring in this node names any physical object.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "SDF-18", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeEigen_of_etaQuotient", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-11", "FRK-22", "SDF-17"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED, all four SDF-18 declarations plus two witness-gap declarations and four fresh value pins; RE-VERIFIED THIS RUN (run 13). THE CONDITIONAL LIFT AT GENERAL N -- and the whole point of the node is still the word CONDITIONAL (LL-33: a bridge theorem that assumes what it should prove is a hollow theorem). SDF-18a frickeInvolution_eq_of_etaQuotient {N} (hN : 0 < N) {r : EtaExp} (hr : IsFrickeSelfDual N r) {m : Int} (hk : sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2*(2*m)) (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)) (hf : forall tau, f tau = etaQuotientH N r tau) : frickeInvolution hN m f = ((-1:C)^m) . f. SDF-18b mem_frickePlus_of_etaQuotient (m Even) and SDF-18c mem_frickeMinus_of_etaQuotient (m Odd) are the two membership corollaries, and are STRICTLY WEAKER than SDF-18a (one-directional, information dropped) -- cite them as conveniences, never as the result. WHY THE lean_name IS SDF-18d AND NOT SDF-18a: check_dag verifies a node by base-name match on a SINGLE lean_name, so naming frickeInvolution_eq_of_etaQuotient alone would leave both corollaries unverified by the DAG gate -- the same bookkeeping gap FRK-22 closed in run 11. The node resolves to frickeEigen_of_etaQuotient (SDF-18d), a conjunction of all three whose #print axioms covers all three; all three plus SDF-18d are ALSO separately guarded in FinalCheck.lean and all print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. SDF-18d adds NO mathematical content. PROOF: ModularForm.ext, funext on hf, SDF-17c (etaQuotientH_slash_frickeW_selfDual) at k = 2*m, then SDF-17d (frickeEigenvalue_normalised_even) collapses N^(1-m)*(N^{-1}*lambda) to (-1)^m; the corollaries add Even.neg_one_zpow / Odd.neg_one_zpow and FRK-22a/b. No new mathematics; the node's old 'moderate' difficulty label overstated it. THE CONSTANT IS PINNED BEFORE THE GENERAL LEMMA, at four (N,m) pairs used by no other pin in this library, each recomputed by hand from i^(-k)*sqrt(N^k) first: sdf18_pin_level_eleven (N=11, m=1, lambda=-11, normalised -1), sdf18_pin_level_two_weight_six (N=2, m=3, lambda=-8, normalised -1), sdf18_pin_level_four_weight_eight (N=4, m=4, lambda=256, normalised +1), sdf18_pin_level_three_weight_neg_four (N=3, m=-2, negative weight, radicand 1/81, normalised +1). TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS are inside those pins and both are the spellings that would otherwise be indistinguishable: (-1)^(2m) instead of (-1)^m is REFUTED at N=11 m=1 (truth -1, wrong spelling +1), and dropping the N^(1-m) normalisation is REFUTED at N=4 m=4 (unnormalised 64, not 1). Both sides of the sign occur among the pins, so a proof that silently produced +1 everywhere could not pass. NOT VACUOUS AS A STATEMENT, BUT UNINSTANTIATED: the conclusion is a genuine eigenvector equation (and FRK-22/FRK-50 make membership the literal classical Atkin-Lehner equation), the weight 2*m is never the zero module (odd weight is separately proved vacuous by FRK-24b and never arises here), yet NOTHING IN THIS LIBRARY DISCHARGES THE HYPOTHESES f AND hf FOR A NONTRIVIAL r AT ANY N. This node therefore has ZERO INSTANCES TODAY and must be reported as a weaker, conditional half of the classical result: classical Ligozat + Atkin-Lehner PROVES modularity from arithmetic conditions on r and then derives the eigenvalue; SDF-18 assumes modularity and derives only the eigenvalue. THE WITNESS GAP IS NOW MACHINE-CHECKABLE, NOT PROSE. SDF-18e sdf18_level_eleven_hypotheses DECIDES that r = drk11R11 = (2,2) at N = 11 (i.e. eta(tau)^2 eta(11 tau)^2) satisfies EVERY arithmetic hypothesis of SDF-18c: IsFrickeSelfDual 11 drk11R11, sum r delta = 4 = 2*(2*1), and Odd 1 -- the frickeMinus branch, predicted eigenvalue (-1)^1 = -1, which is also the classical Fricke eigenvalue of the level-11 weight-2 newform. SDF-18f mem_frickeMinus_etaProductEleven is SDF-18c specialised there, and STILL takes f as a hypothesis. THE ONLY MISSING CONJUNCT IS CUSP BOUNDEDNESS AT N = 11 (F3.1-OBSTRUCTED): EtaLigozatLevelEleven.lean already proves the Gamma0(11) TRANSFORMATION LAW sorry-free (ModularForm.etaProductEleven_transform, etaMultiplierVal_eleven_eq_one, exp_etaPhiSum_eq_kroneckerSym_eleven) and NOT through the open ligozat_general, and holomorphy is mdiff_etaQuotientH. So the next obstruction is ONE NAMED CONDITION AT ONE LEVEL, not 'no witness exists anywhere'. EIGENSPACE SEPARATION, STATED HONESTLY: the +1 side has an UNCONDITIONAL witness (FRK-27c/FRK-66, ModularForm.const 1 at weight 0, m = 0, in frickePlus and not in frickeMinus, giving frickePlus /= frickeMinus and frickePlus /= bot); the -1 side has NO unconditional witness at any level, in this run or any earlier one. SCOPE LIMITS THE PAPER MUST STATE. (i) ModularForm, not CuspForm: Mathlib's CuspForm is a separate type and no node here gives an endomorphism of it, so the classical S_k(Gamma0(N))^{+/-} statement is NOT reproduced -- and level 11 is exactly where that bites, since FLT's CuspForm.exists_gamma0_eleven_apply_eq_eta_sq_mul_eta_sq is not reproduced either. (ii) Involution and eigenvalue only: no Petersson self-adjointness of W_N, no commutation with T_p for p not dividing N; classical Atkin-Lehner theory has both and no node claims them. (iii) Weight is indexed as 2*m so no Int division and no odd weight ever arises; that is not a gap versus the classical statement, since M_k(Gamma0(N)) = 0 for odd k classically too. NO HIDDEN MODULARITY (LL-33 axis, checked by grep over the region this run): every appearance of etaQuotientH in SDF-18's statements is under an explicit hypothesis; the proof calls only SDF-17c, SDF-17d, FRK-22a/b and Mathlib, none of which asserts modularity. The FinalCheck TRIPWIRE FIRED as designed when SDF-18a was proved and has been MOVED, not deleted: it now asserts sorryAx on frickeInvolution_etaQuotientModularForm (SDF-19), the first remaining sorry, so proving that will again fail the build and force this bookkeeping to be redone.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "SDF-19", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.sdf19_frickeEigen_etaQuotientModularForm", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-18"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 14); the id is REUSED, not duplicated, and depends_on stays [SDF-18]. THE RESTRICTED LIFT AT 0 < N <= 4, plus THE LIBRARY'S FIRST -1-EIGENSPACE NONTRIVIALITY STATEMENT. THREE declarations plus NINE pins, all in Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean. SDF-19a frickeInvolution_etaQuotientModularForm {N} (hN : 0 < N) (hN4 : N <= 4) {r : EtaExp} (hr : IsFrickeSelfDual N r) {m : Int} (hk : sum_{delta | N} r delta = 2*(2*m)) (h1 : LigozatCongr1 N r) (h2 : LigozatCongr2 N r) (hbd : forall gamma : SL(2,Z), IsBoundedAtImInfty ((etaQuotientH N r) |[2*m] gamma)) : frickeInvolution hN m (etaQuotientModularForm hN hN4 r hk h1 h2 <m, by ring> hbd) = ((-1:C)^m) . etaQuotientModularForm ... . NAME DISCIPLINE: the pre-existing name frickeInvolution_etaQuotientModularForm is KEPT, not reordered to etaQuotientModularForm_frickeInvolution -- the FinalCheck sorryAx TRIPWIRE sat on that exact name, and a reordered name would have orphaned the tripwire and left the original sorry in the library. The tripwire FIRED as designed when the sorry was replaced, and has been MOVED (not deleted) to frickeMinus_ne_bot_of_etaQuotient (SDF-20), the last remaining sorry in the file. PROOF OF 19a IS ONE TERM: frickeInvolution_eq_of_etaQuotient hN hr hk _ (fun _ => rfl) -- SDF-18a at f := etaQuotientModularForm ..., whose hf obligation is definitionally rfl (etaQuotientModularForm_apply). No new mathematics and no new modularity. SDF-19b frickeMinus_ne_bot_level_four (hbd : forall gamma : SL(2,Z), IsBoundedAtImInfty ((etaQuotientH 4 rMinusWitness) |[6] gamma)) : frickeMinus (0 < 4) 3 != bot, where rMinusWitness : EtaExp := fun delta => if delta = 2 then 12 else 0 -- the exponent vector of eta(2 tau)^12 at N = 4. Route: etaQuotientModularForm builds the form from the four DECIDED arithmetic conditions; mem_frickeMinus_of_etaQuotient (SDF-18c) puts it in frickeMinus; etaQuotientH_ne_zero says it is not 0; Submodule.mem_bot finishes. It does NOT go through SDF-20, which remains open, and SDF-20 is NOT a dependency of this node. SDF-19c sdf19_frickeEigen_etaQuotientModularForm is the PACKAGING conjunction of 19a and 19b and is THIS NODE'S RESOLVING lean_name, because check_dag verifies by base-name match on a SINGLE lean_name (the bookkeeping gap FRK-22c and SDF-18d each had to close); a #print axioms on it covers both theorems and, through 19b, rMinusWitness and every pin. All three declarations plus all nine pins are SEPARATELY guarded in FinalCheck.lean and all print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. PINS BEFORE THE GENERAL LEMMA, and all NEW to this node. FOUR VALUE PINS at N = 4 -- the witness's own level -- at k in {2,4,6,10} (m in {1,2,3,5}), each recomputed by hand from i^(-k)*sqrt(N^k) first: lambda = -4, 16, -64, -1024 and normalised N^(1-m)*(N^-1 lambda) = -1, +1, -1, -1 = (-1)^m. The k = 4 row is the PLUS side, so a proof that silently produced +1 everywhere is refuted. These four (N,k) pairs appear at no other pin in this library (SDF-18's four are (11,2), (2,6), (4,8), (3,-4)). THE k = 6 ROW IS THE ONE THE WITNESS STANDS ON, and it was checked THREE INDEPENDENT WAYS before any Lean was written: (a) from the definition, i^(-6)*sqrt(4^6) = (-1)*64 = -64; (b) from the classical eta transformation, eta(2*(-1/(4 tau)))^12 = eta(-1/(2 tau))^12 = (-i*2 tau)^6 eta(2 tau)^12 = (-i)^6 * 64 * tau^6 * eta(2 tau)^12 = -64 tau^6 eta(2 tau)^12; (c) numerically, evaluating eta(2 tau)^12 at tau = 0.3+0.9i, -0.17+1.4i and 0.05+0.62i and dividing, giving -64.000000000000 each time. All three agree. MUST-FAIL CONTROL: the same proof script with 64 in place of -64 leaves the goal -64 = 64 and does not compile (scratch_sdf19/MustFail.lean, run this session). TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS ON THE CONSTANT sit inside the k = 6 pin: the (-1)^(2m) spelling is REFUTED, and dropping the N^(1-m) normalisation is REFUTED (unnormalised 4^-1 * lambda = -16, not -1). FOUR DECIDE PINS settle the witness's arithmetic at the node's own spelling 2*(2*3), not merely 2*6: sum_{delta | 4} rMinusWitness delta = 2*(2*3), IsFrickeSelfDual 4 rMinusWitness, LigozatCongr1 4 rMinusWitness, LigozatCongr2 4 rMinusWitness. THREE COMBINATORIAL NEGATIVE CONTROLS (sdf19_pin_witness_neg_controls) show those decides are not true of any vector at all: moving the exponent to delta = 1 breaks self-duality at N = 4, the exponent 11 breaks congruence (i), and the sum is NOT 2*(2*2), so m = 3 is forced rather than chosen. NOT VACUOUS, BUT CONDITIONAL, AND THE DISTINCTION CARRIES THE WHOLE NODE. hbd -- Ligozat's condition (iii), cusp boundedness -- is STILL A HYPOTHESIS in both 19a and 19b, and this library discharges it for NO nontrivial exponent vector at ANY level (F3.1-OBSTRUCTED; re-verified this run by grep over Lean/, which finds no discharge anywhere). But hbd is CLASSICALLY TRUE at this vector -- eta(2 tau)^12 is the unique newform of S_6(Gamma0(4)), q-expansion q * prod (1-q^{2n})^{12}, visibly vanishing at i infinity -- so this is a theorem conditional on a true-but-unproved hypothesis, NOT a theorem with a false hypothesis and no content. The library neither proves nor uses that classical fact; it is cited as literature (L-tier) only. WITNESS STATUS, STATED PLAINLY AND NOT DRESSED UP. This is the FIRST -1-eigenspace nontriviality statement anywhere in this library, and it reduces the minus side from 'no route at all' to ONE named classical condition at ONE level for ONE exponent vector. It is NOT an unconditional witness. NO UNCONDITIONAL nonzero -1-Fricke-eigenform exists anywhere in this library. Moreover the +1 witness (FRK-27c/FRK-66, ModularForm.const 1) lives at m = 0 and this -1 witness at m = 3, so NO SINGLE (N, m) has BOTH eigenspaces shown nonzero, and frickePlus != frickeMinus is still proved only at weight 0. The eigenspace decomposition of M_6(Gamma0(4)) therefore has exactly ONE side witnessed, and that one conditionally. That is this node's standing limitation. FOUR WAYS THIS IS WEAKER THAN THE CLASSICAL RESULT, and the paper must state all four. (W1) Ligozat condition (iii) is ASSUMED, not derived: classical Ligozat PROVES holomorphy at the cusps from sum_{delta|N} gcd(d,delta)^2 r_delta/delta >= 0; this library takes it as hbd. (W2) Only the W_N eigenvalue: classical Atkin-Lehner (1970) gives the whole W_Q group for Q || N, Petersson self-adjointness, and commutation with T_p for p not dividing N; no node here claims any of those. (W3) ModularForm, NOT CuspForm: eta(2 tau)^12 is a CUSP form and the classical statement is about S_6(Gamma0(4))^-; this node lands only in ModularForm (Gamma0GL 4) 6, so the cuspidal eigenspace statement is not reproduced. (W4) N <= 4 is the real bound in the Lean sources (etaQuotientModularForm's hN4 hypothesis), NOT the wider {1,2,3,4,5,7,13} that appears in some prose. BUILT FROM, factually: frickeInvolution_eq_of_etaQuotient (SDF-18a), mem_frickeMinus_of_etaQuotient (SDF-18c), etaQuotientModularForm and etaQuotientModularForm_apply, etaQuotientH_ne_zero, frickeEigenvalue, and Mathlib's Submodule.mem_bot. LigozatCongr1 and LigozatCongr2 appear as hypothesis TYPES only, never as proof steps. TYPE ALIGNMENT, verified by elaboration and not by reading: etaQuotientModularForm returns ModularForm (Gamma0 N) k with Gamma0 N coerced to Subgroup (GL (Fin 2) R) via map (mapGL R), which is literally Gamma0GL N. The (6 : Int) weight literal in 19b's hbd unifies with frickeMinus _ 3's weight 2 * 3; no coercion gap. NEXT OBSTRUCTION: cusp boundedness (Ligozat (iii)) for rMinusWitness at N = 4 -- a single named condition at a single level, and the only thing between this library and an UNCONDITIONAL -1-Fricke-eigenform. SDF-20 (the general-f form) remains open and now carries the FinalCheck sorryAx tripwire. NO PHYSICS: no declaration, docstring or pin in this node names any physical object.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "SDF-20", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeMinus_ne_bot_of_etaQuotient", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["SDF-18", "FRK-27"], "statement_nl": "PROVED. frickeMinus_ne_bot_of_etaQuotient (hr : IsFrickeSelfDual N r) (hm : Odd m) (hk : sum r delta = 2*(2*m)) (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)) (hf : forall tau, f tau = etaQuotientH N r tau) (hf0 : f <> 0) : frickeMinus hN m <> bot. If a self-dual eta quotient of weight 2m with m ODD is a nonzero modular form, then the -1 eigenspace is nontrivial. CONDITIONAL: f and f<>0 are hypotheses, and nothing in this library discharges them unconditionally at any N -- no unconditional nonzero -1-Fricke-eigenform is exhibited anywhere. The real remaining obstruction is F3.1-OBSTRUCTED (Ligozat condition (iii) / cusp boundedness, undischarged for any nontrivial exponent vector at any level); this node is the conditional bridge to it, not the obstruction itself.", "paper_claim": null}

{"id": "FRK-42", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sigma_pin_two_I", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED and GUARDED (run 10). SIGMA-BRANCH DECIDE-PIN 1, stated BEFORE the general FRK-47. sigma (frickeW (0<2)) I = I, at a NON-REAL scalar. Mathlib's sigma is a literal `if 0 < g.det.val then .refl R C else Complex.conjCAE`; the two branches AGREE on real numbers and DIFFER on non-real ones, and FRK-11's own multiplier N^(1-m) is real -- so a wrong branch would have been mathematically invisible in the only place FRK-11 uses it. This pin is the smallest witness that distinguishes them. Hand value computed before the pin was written: identity branch gives I, conjugation branch gives conj I = -I (FRK-44), and I != -I (FRK-45).", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-43", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sigma_pin_thirteen", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED and GUARDED (run 10). SIGMA-BRANCH DECIDE-PIN 2, at N = 13 -- the largest level at which this library proves Ligozat -- and at c = 1 + 2I, which unlike FRK-42's c = I has a nonzero REAL part as well, so it also catches a branch that negated only the real component. sigma (frickeW (0<13)) (1 + 2I) = 1 + 2I. Hand value computed before the pin was written; the branch NOT taken gives 1 - 2I (FRK-46).", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-44", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sigma_pin_conj_I", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED and GUARDED (run 10). NEGATIVE CONTROL for FRK-42: the branch NOT taken, evaluated. (Complex.conjCAE I : C) = -I. Without this and FRK-45, FRK-42 would be a tautology between two unevaluated expressions rather than a discrimination between two branches.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-45", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sigma_pin_I_ne_neg_I", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED and GUARDED (run 10). Companion to FRK-44: (I : C) != -I, by Complex.ext_iff on the imaginary parts (1 vs -1). Together FRK-42/44/45 make the sigma branch resolution REFUTED-IF-WRONG rather than merely unchecked.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-46", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sigma_pin_conj_thirteen", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED and GUARDED (run 10). NEGATIVE CONTROL for FRK-43, stated as a conjunction so both halves are in one guarded declaration: (Complex.conjCAE (1+2I) : C) = 1 - 2I AND (1+2I : C) != 1 - 2I.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-47", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sigma_apply", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-12", "FRK-42", "FRK-43", "FRK-44", "FRK-45", "FRK-46"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10). theorem frickeW_sigma_apply {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (c : C) : sigma (frickeW hN) c = c. FRK-12 (det W_N = N > 0) turned into the exact rewrite that Mathlib's ModularForm.smul_slash consumes: sigma (W_N) is the IDENTITY automorphism of C, so scalars pass through a slash by W_N UNCONJUGATED. Proof is `rw [sigma, if_pos (frickeW_det_val_pos hN)]; rfl` -- one line, but it is the single step that unblocks both FRK-19 and FRK-11, and it is the one step where a wrong answer would have been invisible at the real scalars FRK-11 uses, which is why FRK-42..FRK-46 pin it at non-real scalars with negative controls FIRST. NEW NODE, fresh id; it does not duplicate FRK-12, which is the determinant-positivity fact rather than the sigma resolution.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-48", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeInvolution_apply_classical", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-14", "FRK-15", "FRK-18", "FRK-49"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10). THE STATEMENT PIN ON FRK-11'S NORMALISATION -- it certifies that what FRK-11 proves an involution OF is the classical Atkin-Lehner operator and not some other normalisation. theorem frickeInvolution_apply_classical {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)) (tau : H) : frickeInvolution hN m f tau = N^(-m) * tau^(-(2*m)) * f (frickeW hN . tau). Mathlib's slash carries |det g|^(k-1) * denom(g,tau)^(-k), which at W_N is N^(2m-1) * (N tau)^(-2m); the classical Atkin-Lehner form is N^(-k/2) tau^(-k) f(-1/(N tau)). Those are DIFFERENT EXPRESSIONS and their agreement is this theorem, not a convention: mul_zpow splits (N tau)^(-2m), then zpow_add0 collects (1-m)+(2m-1)+(-2m) = -m. FRK-14 (frickeW_smul_coe_neg_inv) rewrites W_N . tau to -(1/(N tau)), so the right-hand side is literally the classical one. The scalar instance N^(-m) = N^(1-m)*N^(-1) is pinned at literal numerals, with a negative control on the SIGN of m, by FRK-18's PINs 18-22. NEW NODE, fresh id.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-49", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeInvolution_apply", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-18"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 10). @[simp] theorem frickeInvolution_apply {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)) (tau : H) : frickeInvolution hN m f tau = ((N:C)^(1-m)) * (f |[2*m] frickeW hN) tau. Proof is `rfl`: every step is definitional -- frickeInvolution is a scalar action whose ModularForm coe is rfl (ModularForm.IsGLPos.coe_smul), and frickeModularOperator's coe is rfl through frickeSlashOperator_coe. Run 8's FRK-18 node explicitly recorded this declaration as still sorry and as belonging to FRK-11's remaining work; it is given its own id here so that FRK-11's dependency on it is visible in the graph rather than buried in prose. NEW NODE, fresh id.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-50", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickePlus_mem_iff_classical", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-22", "FRK-48"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 11), both declarations -- THE STATEMENT PIN that makes FRK-22 mean what the prose says it means. frickePlus_mem_iff_classical {N : Nat} (hN : 0 < N) (m : Int) (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL N) (2*m)) : f in frickePlus hN m <-> forall tau : H, (N:C)^(-m) * (tau:C)^(-(2*m)) * f (frickeW hN . tau) = f tau; and frickeMinus_mem_iff_classical, identically but with = -(f tau). Both guarded; both print [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. WHY IT IS NEEDED: frickeInvolution is defined through Mathlib's GL(2,R)-slash, which carries |det g|^(k-1) * denom(g,tau)^(-k); the classical Atkin-Lehner normalisation is N^(-k/2) tau^(-k) f(-1/(N tau)). Those are DIFFERENT EXPRESSIONS and their agreement is a theorem (FRK-48, frickeInvolution_apply_classical), not a convention. Read on its own, FRK-22 is a statement about an operator whose normalisation is not visibly the classical one; FRK-50 composes the two so that membership in frickePlus / frickeMinus IS the classical eigenform equation. With FRK-14 (((frickeW hN . tau : H) : C) = -(1/(N tau))) the right-hand side reads N^(-k/2) tau^(-k) f(-1/(N tau)) at k = 2*m. NO NEW MATHEMATICS: the proof is FRK-22 rewritten by FRK-48 in both directions, plus ModularForm.neg_apply for the minus half; the exponent arithmetic (1-m)+(2m-1)+(-2m) = -m lives in FRK-48 and is pinned at literal numerals with a negative control by PINs 18-22 of FrickeEigenspace.lean. NO MODULARITY IS ASSUMED: f is a hypothesis on the bundled ModularForm type; no eta quotient appears. SCOPE: this pins the NORMALISATION only. It does not exhibit any eigenform, does not touch CuspForm, and supplies nothing about Petersson self-adjointness or Hecke commutation. A single lean_name again names only the plus half; the minus half frickeMinus_mem_iff_classical is separately guarded in FinalCheck.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-51", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_neg_one_entry", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. VACUITY-MECHANISM DECIDE-PIN V1 for FRK-24, stated BEFORE the general lemma. theorem oddWeight_pin_neg_one_entry : ((-1 : SL(2,Z)) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) Int) 1 0 = 0, by decide. This is the entry the whole odd-weight vanishing rests on: -1 lies in Gamma0 N for EVERY N precisely because its lower-left entry is 0, hence 0 mod N. Computed straight from the matrix by decide, NOT through Gamma0_mem or neg_one_mem_Gamma0GL, so it is an independent check rather than a restatement.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-52", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_mem_twelve", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. VACUITY-MECHANISM PIN V2 for FRK-24 (N = 12, a COMPOSITE non-prime-power level): (-1 : GL (Fin 2) R) in Gamma0GL 12. Re-proved from scratch at the literal level -- it does NOT call neg_one_mem_Gamma0GL -- so a bug in the general FRK-24a proof could not hide behind it. The Gamma0 membership is discharged by decide on 12 | 0 in ZMod 12.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-53", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_mem_zero", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. VACUITY-MECHANISM PIN V3 for FRK-24 at the DEGENERATE level N = 0, which the classical texts do not pose: (-1 : GL (Fin 2) R) in Gamma0GL 0. Gamma0 0 is the c = 0 subgroup and -1 is still in it, which is exactly why FRK-24a needs no hypothesis on N and why the odd-weight vanishing holds at N = 0 too. Also proved independently of neg_one_mem_Gamma0GL.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-54", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_denom_neg_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. VACUITY-MECHANISM PIN V4 for FRK-24 -- THE DENOMINATOR. theorem oddWeight_pin_denom_neg_one (z : C) : UpperHalfPlane.denom (-1 : GL (Fin 2) R) z = -1, computed from the definition denom g z = g 1 0 * z + g 1 1. This is the factor Mathlib's ModularForm.eq_zero_of_neg_one_mem raises to the -k; if it were +1 the argument would collapse to f z = f z and there would be no vanishing at all.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-55", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_sign_three", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. VACUITY-MECHANISM PIN V5 for FRK-24 -- THE SIGN at k = 3 (odd): (-1 : C)^(3 : Int) = -1. Hand value -1, computed before the pin was written.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-56", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_sign_neg_five", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. VACUITY-MECHANISM PIN V6 for FRK-24 -- the NEGATIVE-k CONTROL at k = -5 (odd AND negative): (-1 : C)^(-5 : Int) = -1. This is the pin that would break if the statement were read with a Nat-exponent pow instead of zpow; FRK-24 quantifies over all of Int, negative odd weights included, and the classical textbook statements (usually posed for k >= 0) do not cover this instance.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-57", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_sign_even_control", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": [], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. VACUITY-MECHANISM PIN V7 for FRK-24 -- THE NEGATIVE CONTROL, and the only pin in the V-block that does NOT evaluate to -1: (-1 : C)^(4 : Int) = 1 AND (1 : C) != -1, at the EVEN k = 4. So the vanishing is genuinely an ODD-weight phenomenon and not an artifact of the argument: at even weight the same computation proves nothing, which is why the even case needs the whole frickeInvolution apparatus (FRK-11 .. FRK-23) instead.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-58", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_instance_twelve_three", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-24"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. INSTANCE PIN V8 on FRK-24 at literal numerals (N = 12, k = 3): (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL 12) 3) -> f = 0, with Odd 3 discharged by decide. Stated AFTER the general lemma because it is an instance OF it; it pins that the theorem actually fires at concrete (N, k) rather than being unusable in practice.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-59", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.oddWeight_pin_instance_one_neg_seven", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-24"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. INSTANCE PIN V9 on FRK-24 at the degenerate level and a NEGATIVE odd weight (N = 1, k = -7): (f : ModularForm (Gamma0GL 1) (-7)) -> f = 0, with Odd (-7) discharged by decide. Together with FRK-58 this exercises both the composite-level and the negative-weight regimes the general statement claims.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-60", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator_const_pin_two", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. CONSTANT DECIDE-PIN C1 for FRK-25, stated BEFORE the general lemma. frickeModularOperator (0<2) (ModularForm.const 1) <I> = 1/2. Hand value 2^(0-1) * (2i)^0 = 1/2, computed before the pin was written and re-checked numerically in Python this session. Evaluates the BUNDLED operator -- the exact LHS of FRK-25a, not the raw slash, which is pinned separately at FRK-37..FRK-41 -- straight from Mathlib slash_apply. The proof does NOT mention frickeModularOperator_const_one, so a wrong scalar there could not hide behind a matching wrong scalar here.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-61", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator_const_pin_three", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. CONSTANT DECIDE-PIN C2 for FRK-25 (N = 3, tau = 2i): value 1/3. Hand value 3^(-1) * (6i)^0. The only pin in the C-block with tau != i, so a tau-dependence leaking out of the denom^(-k) factor -- which must be trivial at k = 0 -- would show up here and nowhere else. Independent of frickeModularOperator_const_one.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-62", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator_const_pin_seven", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. CONSTANT DECIDE-PIN C3 for FRK-25 (N = 7, tau = i): value 1/7. Hand value 7^(-1). A third independent level, prime and larger than C1/C2. Independent of frickeModularOperator_const_one.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-63", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator_const_pin_one", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. CONSTANT DECIDE-PIN C4 for FRK-25 at the DEGENERATE level N = 1: value 1^(-1) = 1. This is the ONLY level at which Mathlib's scalar N^(-1) coincides with the classical Atkin-Lehner scalar 1, which is exactly why a pin at N = 1 alone would prove nothing about the normalisation -- it is included as the degenerate control and is read together with FRK-64. Independent of frickeModularOperator_const_one.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-64", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeModularOperator_const_not_fixed_five", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-DEF", "FRK-12"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. CONSTANT PIN C5 for FRK-25 -- THE NEGATIVE CONTROL, and the pin that matters for the prose. frickeModularOperator (0<5) (ModularForm.const 1) != ModularForm.const 1: the RAW operator does NOT fix the constant 1. So frickeModularOperator is NOT the classical Atkin-Lehner operator on the nose; the N^(-1) of FRK-25a is a genuine artifact of Mathlib's |det|^(k-1) * denom^(-k) slash, and only the normalised frickeInvolution (FRK-18, FRK-26) fixes the constant. C1-C4 assert only what the value IS and so could not detect a statement quietly read with the classical normalisation; C5 asserts what it is NOT. Independent of frickeModularOperator_const_one.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-65", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeInvolution_const_one_pin_twelve", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-26"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. RECONCILIATION INSTANCE PIN C6 (N = 12, a composite level): frickeInvolution (0<12) 0 (ModularForm.const 1) = ModularForm.const 1. Stated AFTER the general FRK-26 because it is an instance OF it. Read against FRK-64 (N = 5, where the RAW operator does not fix the constant) it pins the exact place the normalisation does its work: the raw operator scales by N^(-1), the N^(1-m) normalisation multiplies by N^(1-0) = N, and N * N^(-1) = 1.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "FRK-66", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickePlus_ne_bot", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-22", "FRK-25", "FRK-26", "FRK-27"], "statement_nl": "PROVED sorry-free and GUARDED. frickePlus_ne_bot {N} (hN : 0 < N) : frickePlus hN 0 != bot -- the +1 Fricke eigenspace in weight 0 is not the zero submodule, at EVERY level N > 0. Proof: Submodule.ne_bot_iff, with the witness const 1, which is a member by FRK-27a and nonzero by FRK-25b. THIS IS THE STATEMENT THE FRK-25 NODE ORIGINALLY ASKED FOR, and it is recorded HERE rather than at FRK-25 because it is not derivable from FRK-25's dependencies: it needs FRK-22a and FRK-26, and FRK-26 depends on FRK-25, so placing it upstream would make the DAG circular. UNCONDITIONAL: no eta quotient, no Ligozat, no modularity hypothesis. THE HONEST LIMIT: it says NOTHING about frickeMinus hN 0, which is expected to BE bot (weight-0 forms on Gamma_0(N) are constants) and is proved neither bot nor nonzero anywhere in this library. A nonzero -1 Fricke eigenform remains the next obstruction; the only route offered to one is SDF-20, still sorry.", "paper_claim": null}
{"id": "SDF-25", "kind": "math", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.sdf25_pin_battery", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeEigenspace.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-16", "FRK-17", "SDF-DEF-02", "SDF-19"], "statement_nl": "PROVED SORRY-FREE AND GUARDED (run 15). THE PIN BATTERY, under a FRESH id. NOT written as SDF-20: dag id SDF-20 is already taken by frickeMinus_ne_bot_of_etaQuotient (status open, the honest -1-eigenspace obstruction with a sorryAx tripwire in FinalCheck), and overwriting it would have destroyed that record. THIRTEEN new pins plus one packaging theorem, all in FrickeEigenspace.lean. GROUP (i), the CONSTANT-SPELLING pins at the four (N,k) the brief names, each TWO-SIDED against an explicit numeral (FRK-10's spelling (N^2)^(k-1)*(-N)^(-k) AND the target (-1)^k*N^(k-2), both evaluated, so a mis-stated RHS is refuted not merely unproved): sdf25_pin_const_four_six (4,6)->256; _two_two (2,2)->1; _three_neg_two (3,-2)->1/81 with a NEGATIVE CONTROL refuting the exponent k-1; _five_four (5,4)->25. HONEST LIMIT recorded in the file: all four of these k are EVEN, so none of them can see a dropped (-1)^k; the sign is pinned only by the pre-existing odd-k pins (frickeW_sq_const_pin_two_three, _one_negthree, _seven_negone, _nine_five). GROUP (ii), the NORMALISATION pins (N^(1-m))^2 * C(N,2m) = 1 at (4,3), (2,1), (3,-1), (5,2), weight written in the 2*m spelling: sdf25_pin_norm_four_three / _two_one / _three_neg_one / _five_two, the last with a NEGATIVE CONTROL (exponent reversed to m-1 gives 625 != 1). GROUP (iii), the EIGENVALUE BRIDGE, and this is what the run actually repairs: the brief's form frickeEigenvalue N (2*m) * N^-1 * N^(1-m) = (-1)^m had been checked only with a NUMERAL substituted for lambda, which tests the arithmetic but not the link to frickeEigenvalue, and the link is the load-bearing half. sdf25_pin_bridge_one_six (1,6), _nine_two (9,2) with a negative control refuting the dropped N^(1-m) factor, _four_zero (4,0), _six_one (6,1) with a negative control refuting the (-1)^(2m) spelling; each rewrites through the library's own proved value pins (frickeEigenvalue_pin_level_one, _pin_level_nine_weight_four, _pin_level_four_weight_zero, _pin_level_six_weight_two). This also widens level coverage: every value pin in SDF19Pins sits at N = 4, so the power of N in the normalisation had been pinned at ONE level; N in {1,6,9} now too (N = 1 is degenerate and says nothing about the power of N -- (9,2) and (6,1) carry that weight). GROUPS (iv) and (v) ARE NOT RE-PROVED: (iv), the witness decide-pins for eta(2tau)^12 at N = 4, is sdf19_pin_witness_sum / _selfDual / _congr1 / _congr2, already landed and already guarded; (v), the non-real sigma branch at c = I, is DISCHARGED by frickeW_sigma_pin_two_I (FrickeEigenspace.lean) and frickeModularOperator_smul_pin_I, both guarded. The packaging theorem sdf25_pin_battery conjoins one representative of all five groups so a single lean_name base-name match covers the battery. NO PIN DISAGREED WITH HAND COMPUTATION, so no statement was adjusted. NOTHING HERE ASSERTS MODULARITY: every conjunct is numeral arithmetic or a decide about IsFrickeSelfDual / LigozatCongr1 / LigozatCongr2. Ligozat condition (iii), cusp boundedness, is F3.1-OBSTRUCTED and appears nowhere in this battery.", "paper_claim": "The pin battery guarding the Fricke constant, its normalisation, and the eigenvalue bridge. Its VALUE as evidence is bounded and the paper must say so: pins are instance checks, not proofs of the general lemmas (FRK-16/FRK-17/SDF-17, proved separately). What they buy is refutation-if-wrong at concrete (N,k): four of the thirteen carry an explicit != conjunct, so a wrong sign, a wrong power of N, or a dropped normalisation is REFUTED at that instance rather than merely unchecked."}
